WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94369] = { title = "The Fate of Zephras", description = "Ansirem has told me much of the elemental lords and I am afraid that we have good reason to fear Al'Akir now that the wards that have hidden Zephras are down. If the Windlord chooses to attack us, we stand no chance to defend ourselves while we are here in his domain.\n\nHigh Elder Shadowsong needs to know of the danger we are in, and more importantly, what our intentions are for our mission to Azeroth. We will find the means to save our home. I swear it.", objectives = "Speak with Talaanis Shadowsong in Valanaar.", completion = "<Talaanis Shadowsong listens intently as you tell him of what transpired above the Shrine of Akir, and of Elaadrin's plan to leave Zephras Isle.>\n\nI need to reflect on this further, but looking at the upside, we have rid ourselves of Lorthuna and deprived the cult of their leader. Our home has not been invaded yet, and on the timeline of elemental demigods, it could be years... decades even, before Al'Akir deigns to turn his attention to us.\n\nThere is much to fear now, but much to celebrate as well." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94373] = { title = "Call of Earth", description = "Aye, the time's come, young shaman. Ye've grown stout and sturdy, like the stone beneath our boots. Takin' up the shaman's path shows ye've got the wisdom o' the mountain, even before ye've proven yerself. Ye've the grit of stone to walk the earth's path.\n\nBut to earn its favor, ye must face it proper. South o' here, the Frostmane trolls live in a cave.\n\nBring me two of the necklaces they wear, crafted from the Iceclaw bears. Then we'll speak more of yer future.", objectives = "Bring 2 Frostmane Bear Pendants to Teo Hammerstorm in Anvilmar.", progress = "Patience, lad, is the earth's finest virtue. It's seen mountains crumble and rivers carve valleys - slow and stubborn, like a true {race}. The earth calls to ye now, for trouble brews on the horizon. Return successful, and ye'll be one step closer to bein' whole. \n\nOthers may envy yer wisdom, but that's their burden to bear.", completion = "Well done, lad. Ye've proven yerself ready. Earth's the bedrock of all things. Strength, stamina, patience. It'll shield ye, but only if ye show it proper respect. Even stone can shift if slighted. Learn its ways, and ye'll grow wiser than most. Never forget the secrets it shares. \n\nI'll craft ye a sapta now - accept it, and ye'll walk the true path." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94374] = { title = "Call of Earth", description = "Aye, sapta's a brew forged with magic, bindin' our spirit to the elements. Only a few shaman know the recipe, and it's nae for the weak-willed. Drink it, and ye will see what others can't. Hold true--it's only to be drunk in a sacred place.\n\nHead north to the Spirit Stone, tucked at the end of a hidden path up the mountain. Drink it there... see what the earth has to show ye.", objectives = "Find the Spirit Stone and drink the Earth Sapta.", completion = "Ah... {name}... the earth welcomes you, even in this frozen land. Bound in body and spirit, you'll walk forward knowing the mountains are your strength, the plains your patience, and the world your essence.\n\nTo pass this rite, stand humbly before the earth. The other elements are not so still - they clash and roar. Learn their dual nature, even here among the snow and stone." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94375] = { title = "Call of Earth", description = "Take this rough quartz from me and bring it to Teo Hammerstorm as proof o' our meeting. He will craft a totem for ye, and this pebble will be the heart o' it. As small as it may seem, ye will come to find that size does not matter, and that even the smallest o' things can outlast many others.\n\nBe patient, {name}. Remain strong. And seek wisdom. This is what earth asks o' ye. In the end, ye shall become one with the earth--respect it as it shall respect ye.", objectives = "Bring the Rough Quartz to Teo Hammerstorm in Anvilmar.", progress = "Ahh, ye've returned. If ye have the stone, it means the mountain's chosen ye true. I'll give ye the totem it promised. But if ye've come empty-handed, off with ye! The path ain't for those who forget their way.", completion = "Well done! Know this - totems ain't just a mark of yer place among shamans. They're tools, a focus for spells tied to stone, soil, and other elements. As ye grow wiser, more o' the mountain's power will open to ye. The trainers will know when yer ready for more. But for now, take this totem, and let the ground speak through ye." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94411] = { title = "Meddlesome Mages", description = "Be warned, members of the High Order have been seen in the vicinity of the standing stones north of the village. We have warned them time and again to not meddle at our sacred sites, but they are growing more bold in pushing us. Prove your resolve to us by going to the standing stones and dispersing them.\n\nI am loathe to condone outright bloodshed, but do what you must to drive them off. Return to me when it's done.", objectives = "Slay 6 High Order Apprentices in Shen'dar Highlands.", completion = "Direct conflict with our shen'dorei brothers and sisters only weakens us as a people, but decisive action must at times be taken to prevent greater tragedy.\n\nThe mages of the High Order have zero regard for the consequences of their magical meddling. The forces that bind our island are fragile and vulnerable and all it could take is one thoughtless action to destroy our home." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94413] = { title = "A Magical Affront", description = "The recent emergence of the leylines on the surface of Zephras has been profound for our order. We have more direct and tangible access to the energies that permeate this place and it has increased our understanding of said magic greatly.\n\nThe Windshapers, however, view these emergences as scars on the land that must be \"healed\". This is an affront to our order and is something we simply cannot abide.\n\nGo to the leyline in the forest to the southwest and drive off the Windshapers you find there.", objectives = "Slay 6 Windshaper Novice Seers in Shen'dar Highlands.", completion = "Sometimes I find it hard to distinguish between the blind zealotry of the Al'Aketh cult, and the stubborn refusal of the Windshapers to change.\n\nIf they truly believed the winds would guide us, they should be sensing the direction the winds are blowing and flow with them rather than against them." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94414] = { title = "The Anchors of Zephras", description = "Greetings, young {name}. I oftentimes come here to look upon the ancient anchor pylon. Gifts from the spirits of the winds, they bind and sustain our island. Of late however, their magic has grown unstable and inconsistent.\n\nThey suffer no distress I can see. Their splendor has not changed.\n\nIf you'd like, I can lend you my gift to look upon them yourself.", objectives = "Speak with Halaan Hawk-Eye and borrow his gift to view the anchor pylon in the distance.", progress = "My gift is simple, and mundane. I cannot peer between worlds such as those with the skysight, nor can I draw upon the magic of the ley lines beneath Zephras like others can. But a gift it remains and I am grateful to have it.\n\nAppreciation of what you have is the key to happiness. Yearning for what you may have, or what you have lost, only leads to despair.", completion = "Thank you for taking a moment to share this with me. I will continue to watch over the grove, and ponder on the state of our homeland." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94427] = { title = "A Lesson in Divinity", description = "A key tenent of being a paladin is the pursuit of divinity. This is not the pursuit of godhood, but merely the pursuit of good itself, for good's sake. We've all arrived at this place due to tragedy of one form or another, and it would be easy to lose that grace that defined us as paladins in life.\n\nGo to the Undercity and seek out Tanis Alderwood in the Trade Quarter. They are in need, and they could benefit greatly from some grace.", objectives = "Speak to Tanis Alderwood in the Undercity.", completion = "You... you are a {class}? Please, do not hurt me. I-I know I'm not supposed to be panhandling. I have no quarrel with you or your order. Leave me be, I beg you!" }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94434] = { title = "A Lesson in Divinity", description = "Wait, you want to... help? Why would a paladin want to help a beggar like me?\n\nWell, I suppose that you could be of some assistance. \n\nIt's my wife you see. She, well... she's falling apart. I mean that literally. The apothecaries can stitch her back together right as rain, but they are about the Dark Lady's business and none are available to help. If you could perhaps bring me some fresh cloth then I could at least make her a wrapping to hold her together while we wait for the apothecaries.", objectives = "Bring 10 Linen Cloth to Tanis Alderwood in the Undercity.", progress = "I hope that this is no imposition upon you, goodly {class}.", completion = "This is very kind of you, {class}. Very kind indeed." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94435] = { title = "A Lesson in Divinity", description = "I don't know why you'd go out of your way to help me, but I appreciate it. If someone sent you my way, tell them I appreciate them too. You'll always have a friend in Tanis Alderwood, {class}.", objectives = "Return to Danitha Morr at Bandarion Keep.", completion = "You have done well, {name}. It was a small thing, but even small acts of service such as this may help strengthen our connection to the light.\n\nThe Dark Lady and many in her service mistrust us. Some even conspire against us, but we will visit their skepticism and fear with courage and righteousness. We will show them that we are members of the Forsaken and we are willing to do our part, be it large or small, to help our people prosper once again.\n\nTake this symbol, you will need it for what comes next." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94436] = { title = "A Lesson in Divinity", description = "It's time to demonstrate your ability to channel one of the light's greatest gifts.\n\nThe item I just gave you is called the Symbol of Life. Take care, as it may cause you some discomfort to handle a talisman of the light such as this. The light may be anathema to the force that created us, but it is still our guide and ally. The pain reminds us of this.\n\nGo see Deathguard Billmuth downstairs. He just arrived and he has petitioned us for aid. Show him and the Forsaken what a true paladin can do.", objectives = "Speak with Deathguard Billmuth at Bandarion Keep.\n\nShould you misplace your Symbol of Life, return to Danitha Morr for a replacement.", completion = "So you'll help me, then? Good, good. I'll admit I'm not proud of resorting to... well, resorting to asking paladins for aid. The priests waved me away and you might be my friend's only chance.\n\nPlease, help me." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94438] = { title = "A Lesson in Divinity", description = "Falgan and I were sent on a mission to scout out scarlet activity in Venomweb Vale. We managed to sneak close enough to one of their camps to hear about new orders involving an attack on Brill. Before we could decide what to do next, I stepped on a twig and the noise alerted them to us.\n\nFalgan yelled at me to run, so I ran. By the time I realized he wasn't with me, I was halfway to Brill. That brave idiot probably stayed behind to hold them off for me.\n\nPlease, find my friend and help him if you can.", objectives = "Take the Symbol of Life and use it to resurrect Deathguard Falgan at Venomweb Vale. \n\nShould you misplace your Symbol of Life, return to Danitha Morr for a replacement.", completion = "I'm... back? And saved by a {class} no less? I see you carry a Symbol of Life. I've not seen one of those since... well, since before the war when Lordaeron was a very different place. I can only assume you are here to help. Billmuth and I were sent here to scout out the scarlet activity here, and we found out that they are planning some kind of attack.\n\nIf you would be willing to help more, there may yet be more than you can do to help the Forsaken." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94440] = { title = "A Lesson in Divinity", description = "These Scarlet Crusaders often carry satchels with their deployment orders. We know an attack is coming, but if we can recover their orders, we can warn the rest of the Deathguard and prepare an ambush. \n\nYou are clearly an impressive paladin. Kill these scarlet animals and retrieve a copy of their orders and bring them back to Deathguard Billmuth. He'll take it from there.", objectives = "Retrieve the Scarlet Crusade Attack Plans from the Scarlet Crusaders at Venomweb Vale, and return to Deathguard Billmuth at Bandarion Keep.", progress = "What news of Deathguard Falgan?", completion = "Thank you for saving my friend,{name}. I will take these plans back to my commander and we will give those crusaders a welcoming they won't forget.\n\nI know that many among our people mistrust you paladins, but its clear to me that you are Forsaken through and through. I won't forget this, and I'll make sure others know of what you did here today." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94441] = { title = "A Lesson in Divinity", description = "Please give my thanks to Danitha Morr and tell her that the rest of the Deathguard will hear about the service that the paladins of Bandarion Keep performed for us. \n\nYou have a lot of promise as a paladin, and I am proud to have those like you among the ranks of the Forsaken. Dark Lady watch over you, {name}.", objectives = "Speak with Danitha Morr in the keep at Bandarion Keep.", completion = "The Symbol of Life is only able to be used by a {class} who is ready to make use of one of the light's greatest blessings. I'm proud to count you among us, and I now bestow upon you the gift of redemption. With this you will be able to resurrect your fallen companions. Use this new boon wisely.\n\nYou have done well for both the Forsaken as well as the paladins of Tyr's Watch. Any steps we can take to win the hearts and minds of our fellow Forsaken is well worth the effort. Go with the light, {name}." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94449] = { title = "Call of Fire", description = "It's been long since ye were last tested, {name}. Ye've shown patience, aye -- but now it's time ye learned of chaos... of destruction. Fire's call is loud, and if ye're ready to pay its price, it'll speak to ye. \n\nSeek out Bruegs Kindleborn, far east in the mountains. He dwells in a cave above South Gate Outpost. He'll know if ye're truly ready.", objectives = "Find Bruegs Kindleborn in Dun Morogh.", completion = "Hmm... that elder sent ye, eh? Well, a {class}'s word is solid, so I'll not argue. That means ye're ready for the next sapta. The sapta of fire. I see it in yer eyes already -- the burnin', the hunger. Ye've tasted power, and now ye want more. But mind yerself, {name}. Remember what the stone taught ye. Fire's easy to wield, but harder to master. Know when to hold back." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94465] = { title = "Call of Fire", description = "Aye, ye've the strength to bear the totem o' fire, lad--but strength alone won't make ye ready.\n\nBeyond the Valley o' Kings, in the crags of Loch Modan, lies a hidden path to one o' our sacred peaks. There, Braldir Ashmantle guards the Shrine o' the Dormant Flame. \n\nTake this torch to him--it shows yer intent. Return it burnin' by the shrine's brazier, and I'll see ye earn the totem proper.", objectives = "Bring the Torch of the Dormant Flame to Braldir Ashmantle in Loch Modan.", progress = "Greetin's, {name}. Ye've made it to the Shrine o' the Dormant Flame, eh? Not many do. Only those well-versed in the {class}'s path can grasp the secrets this place holds. \n\nShame ye came all this way just to be turned back--the climb's no stroll through Dun Morogh. But I'm the shrine's keeper, and I won't be lettin' just any foot trod about.", completion = "Ah, me apologies, {name}. Didn't spot the Torch in yer hand. An honor to meet ye proper.\n\nMany a wanderer climbs these heights chasin' tales of treasure or beasts, only to find naught but stone and silence. But we know better, don't we, {name}?\n\nThis shrine holds truths far deeper than the Alliance can fathom. To us, it's a sacred flame that waits to be awakened." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94466] = { title = "Call of Fire", description = "Bah, ye didn't trek all this way for tales, did ye, {name}? Ye seek the Eternal Flame and the fire totem.\n\nFirst, ye'll need a sapta to bind yer spirit to the flame.\n\nI'll craft it--but I'll need two things: fire tar from Tunnel Rat Geomancers in the kobold caves up north, and a reagent pouch from a Stonesplinter Seer lurkin' in the southern hills. Dangerous work, but worthy of the flame.", objectives = "Bring 1 Fire Tar and 1 Reagent Pouch to Braldir Ashmantle in Loch Modan.", progress = "Aye, I've near all I need for the fire sapta, {name}--just missin' the fire tar and the seer's pouch. The tar's carried by Tunnel Rat Geomancers in the kobold caves up north. The pouch ye'll need to wrest from a Stonesplinter seer in the southern hills. These ingredients are bound to flame, as all true saptas must be. Their elemental ties make our craft strong.", completion = "These'll do fine, {name}.\n\nFire ain't just fury and ruin--mark me words. It's life, it's forge, it's the breath o' creation. All things are bound in balance. One force tempers the other, gives it meaning. Without shadow, light's but a glare. Without flame, stone's but cold memory.\n\nMasterin' magic means knowin' when to blend, not just burn. That's true wisdom, lad." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94467] = { title = "Call of Fire", description = "The fire sapta's ready, {name}. Now ye face the flame. Use it at the shrine, then climb to the peak. There, ye'll see the spirit--he'll not strike 'til ye do, but he'll know ye see him.\n\nStrike fast, lad. The longer ye wait, the stronger he burns. When he falls, take his glowing embers and place 'em in the brazier. Light the torch and earn the fire's favor.", objectives = "Defeat the Minor Manifestation of Fire, and place the Glowing Ember in the brazier atop the Shrine of Eternal Flame.", progress = "The brazier stands about a third your height, with charred inscriptions along its smooth metal rails. The metal shows no signs of wear from the weather, and the bowl seated at the top of it feels cool to the touch. \n\nBlackrock mountain looms in the distance, in clear view to honor from this sacred place.", completion = "A white hot flame ignites within the bowl as you place the ember within. You can feel the magical effects of the sapta coursing through your body and the fire dances rhythmically before you.\n\nYou place the top of the torch within the basin, and it immediately catches on fire. The smoke seems to drift towards the mountain of blackrock." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94468] = { title = "Call of Fire", description = "Torch firmly in hand, you turn away from the brazier and look out over Loch Modan. You feel an excitement tugging at your spirit as the wind picks up and forces the flame to dance violently.\n\nYou start off down the path back to Dun Morogh in search of Bruegs Kindleborn.", objectives = "Bring the Torch of Eternal Flame to Bruegs Kindleborn in Dun Morogh.", progress = "Aye, {name}? What do ye have there?", completion = "By Madoran's beard, yer spirit burns brighter than any torch I've laid eyes on, {name}--and that's somethin' to be proud of.\n\nKeep walkin' this path, and the elements'll bend to yer will. Our kin will come to ye for wisdom and guidance. So let me be the first to offer me hearty congratulations -- and present ye with yer newest totem. Ye've earned it, flameborn." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94472] = { title = "Earth Sapta", description = "", objectives = "Speak to Teo Hammerstorm for another Earth Sapta.", completion = "Take this and remember, it is sacred." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94473] = { title = "Fire Sapta", description = "", objectives = "Speak to Braldir Ashmantle for another Fire Sapta", completion = "May fire burn within your heart, Ukko.\n\nThe elements await you." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94479] = { title = "One Person's Trash", description = "Picking up the rusting metal, you see another, shinier, engineering component. It looks like anything else of use has been picked clean.\n\nPerhaps somebody nearby recognizes this part or who might want to salvage it.", objectives = "Search the Tainted Foothills for someone interested in the metallic piece you found." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94480] = { title = "A Gift From Our Enemies", description = "The humans of these lands are only one of many threats. With the encroaching Twilight and snarls of gnolls echoing from the hills nearby, battle may call at a moment's notice. Maintaining the strength of our allies may be the difference between Rog'mar's success or our removal from these lands.\n\nDeliver the goods you've gathered to Gorg. He'll make sure our allies are well fed.", objectives = "Deliver the Stolen Feed to Gorg in Rog'mar." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94481] = { title = "A Serving of Strength", description = "This hearty stew keeps our trainees fed, enough so that our enemies remain at a distance.\n\nBring this and feed our trainees to the west. Don't listen to any complaints. With how difficult defending our supply lines has become, they should be so lucky we're not feeding them dirt.", objectives = "Feed 8 Rog'mar Trainees at the training grounds." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94483] = { title = "Show Them How It's Done", description = "Our scouts have reported training camps by the river to the south. If I'd received word sooner, it would have saved us both the hassle of locating and removing the human filth in a timely manner.\n\nContinue your efforts, {name}. Holding back the humans to their precious little keep will buy us time to focus on other matters at hand.\n\nBe swift about it.", objectives = "Slay 8 Farholde Priests and 12 Farholde Scouts south of the river." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94484] = { title = "Unnerving Silence", description = "A moment if you will, {name}. Are you headed towards Shadowgale Forest? There is a druid conclave there in a cave to the northeast. I have been waiting on word from them but their correspondence is long overdue.\n\nWith Ban'aethall in ruins and all the unrest lately I worry something dire may have happened. Please, if you are able, go seek out Elegael Thornpaw and put my mind at ease.", objectives = "Find and speak with Elegael Thornpaw in the northeastern part of Shadowgale Forest.", completion = "Thank goodness our message got to Lotheluum. Wait, where are the rest of the reinforcements? Surely it is not just you they sent?\n\n<Elegael pales as you relay your conversation with Lotheluum.>\n\nSo the message did not get through. We are in dire straits indeed then.\n\nIt seems we must handle this on our own. Time is of the essence." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94485] = { title = "Tears of the Lady", description = "If we are to save my fellows in the Nightclaw Den, I am going to need some ingredients for a poultice. The first and most important is a spindly moss called Lady's Tear. It typically grows on the base of the trees here in Shadowgale.\n\nThis moss secretes a sticky substance that acts as an antiseptic and is perfect for binding open wounds. I have gathered what little I can reach but I know there is more in this forest.\n\nGo and be swift. We are going to need a lot if the injured I left behind still live.", objectives = "Collect 8 Lady's Tear Moss.", progress = "Have you found the Lady's Tear?", completion = "<Elegael takes the sticky mound of moss from you with a weak smile.>\n\nThank you, {name}, you have done well. This is exactly what we need." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94486] = { title = "Feathers for Binding", description = "The other ingredient I need for the poultice is feathers from the Shadowgale shrieklings that roam this forest. In their juvenile form, the shrieklings have insulative feathers which would be ideal to put over the moss. These feathers will prevent the antiseptic sap from drying out and will provide at least some protection against the elements.\n\nBe warned, the shrieklings are normally docile but they have been incredibly hostile of late. Their large talons can easily disembowel you if you aren't careful.", objectives = "Collect 20 feathers from the Shadowgale Shrieklings in Shadowgale Forest.", progress = "It deeply saddens me to ask you to kill the young shrieklings, but with the rise in their aggression it is for the best. We can only handle so many emergencies at a time.", completion = "Thank you for these. I will be sure to use every feather so their sacrifice will not be in vain." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94487] = { title = "Unwanted and Unworthy", description = "The Al'Aketh Cultists ambushed us with no warning, though their motives remain a mystery to me. I knew these cultists had clouds between their ears, but I never imagined they would upset the delicate balance here on Zephras with such brutality. Go, slay as many as you can and take their heirlooms if they wear any.\n\n<Elegael spits.>\n\nThese storm-cursed cultists don't deserve to be called shen'dorei. The beasts of the forest can have their bodies. Their ashes don't deserve the winds.", objectives = "Collect 10 Bloodied Heirlooms from Al'Aketh Footsoldiers and Al'Aketh Stormchasers in the Shadowgale Forest.", progress = "I will make the cult pay for every drop of {class} blood they have spilled this day.", completion = "<Elegael looks down at the collection of bloodied heirlooms with distress.>\n\nSo many young lives with so much potential now gone forever. Thank you for returning these, {class}.\n\nI will hold onto them for safekeeping until I am able to take them to the High Elder. There they can go back into the collection and await the next and perhaps more worthy generation to come of age." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94488] = { title = "The Ties That Bind", description = "The reason for cultists' presence here still baffles me, but I smell a familiar scent over the bloodshed.\n\nOne of our circle druids, Haalien, disappeared months back. It appears he's thrown his sorry hide in with the cultists.\n\nShow him what happens when he spills the blood of his kin! Take his head and return it to me.", objectives = "Kill Commander Haalien and bring his head to Elegael Thornpaw in the Shadowgale Forest.", progress = "Are our brethren's lives truly worth so little to you, Haalien?", completion = "<Elegael grimaces at the severed head, but nods curtly.>\n\nThank you, {name}. No matter how much rage I have within me, it would have been difficult to strike down my own cousin.\n\nDo not mourn for him. His ignorance and malice has killed many innocents this day." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94489] = { title = "The Wounds of Betrayal", description = "I have finished the poultices. Quickly, take them to the druids in the cave, north just across the clearing. I know my brethren are in much more dire condition than I. They are likely too injured to heal their own wounds. There are so few of us shen'dorei druids that every life is precious.\n\nBefore you go, I have a selfish request. My mate, Jorel Windsinger was in dire condition when I left. Please, see to his wounds if he still lives.", objectives = "Enter the Nightfang Den and heal 1 druids and find Jorel Windsinger in Shadowgale Forest.", progress = "{class}! You have returned. Were you able to reach my brothers and sisters? Did you find Jorel?", completion = "<Elegael's face pales as you relay the fate of Jorel and the condition of the rest of the druids.>\n\nNo... no! This is far worse than I had--\n\n<Elegael chokes back a sob and grits her teeth, letting out a pained snarl.>\n\nThey will pay. They will ALL pay. Anyone who allies with the Al'Aketh will feel my wrath! This I swear." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94490] = { title = "Ripped Missive", description = "<Tucked behind one of Haalien's bracers is a note that's been slightly torn and bloodstained in your fight. It looks like it contains useful information about the cultist motivations for the attack on the druid den. Elegael would be interested in this intel.>", objectives = "Bring the Ripped Missive to Elegael Thornpaw in the Shadowgale Forest.", completion = "They were here for the pylon? But to what end? We were not the original reason for their attack?\n\n<Elegael trails off shaking with rage as she reads.>\n\nThey murdered my people because we were an inconvenience! I shall tear apart every cultist with my fangs! I will make sure none leave this place with their lives.\n\nGo, swiftly! If the orders truly originated in Valanaar, it means it is likely a traitor hiding there. Give the missive to Lotheluum in Valanaar and tell him what has transpired." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94491] = { title = "The Fate of the Den", description = "It would appear that there is a correspondent hiding somewhere in Valanaar feeding information to the cult. I am clearly in no shape to make the journey, but Lotheluum needs to know what transpired here.\n\nHe should also know the fate of those who are no longer with us. Thanks to your help I think we can handle the rest of the situation from here, though the damage has been done.\n\nPlease go swiftly, {name}. I hope our paths will cross again someday. Until then, I have cultists to slay.", objectives = "Give the missive to Lotheluum in Valanaar and tell him what has transpired.", completion = "<Lotheluum wears a look of genuine terror as you recount the events from the {class} den.>\n\nI--I'm sorry, {name}. I need just a moment. There are no words I possess that can describe the loss.\n\nThis is grave news indeed. If this missive is not fabricated, then we indeed have at best an accomplice and at worst a traitor here in Valanaar. I will take this to the High Elder immediately! I will not let my fellows' sacrifice be in vain." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94493] = { title = "A Sacrifice in Vain", description = "Thank goodness our message got to Lotheluum. Wait, where are the rest of the reinforcements? Surely it is not just you they sent?\n\n<Elegael pales as you explain yourself.>\n\nSo the message did not get to Valanaar. We are in dire straits indeed then.\n\n<Elegael sighs deeply then looks resolute.>\n\nThen we must handle this on our own. Time is of the essence.", objectives = "Speak with Elegael Thornpaw in the northeastern part of Shadowgale Forest.", completion = "The Al'aketh Cultists ambushed us with little to no warning. Many inside my den lay wounded or dying. I had attempted to send a message to Valanaar but it appears my efforts were in vain.\n\nPlease, if you have come here I beg for your help. I don't know how much longer my fellows will be able to survive this onslaught." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94494] = { title = "Call of Water", description = "Long has it been since ye were last tested, {name}. Ye have shown patience thus far in yer studies, but the time has come for ye to learn about the purity of water.\n\nSeek out Norric Lochthane in Loch Modan. He is along the north western edge o' the lake, south of Stonewrought Dam. Ye will find him there at his burrow hut. Good luck to ye, {name}.", objectives = "Find Norric Lochthane in Loch Modan.", completion = "The wind's rushin' at yer back, the stone's firm beneath yer boots, and the fire in yer belly's burnin' bright. Aye, it's time ye learned the truth o' water's purity. Yer path's been long, but it's yer spirit that'll carry ye further still. Now, go on, take that first step. The mountain waits for no one." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94495] = { title = "Call of Water", description = "If there's one truth ye need to learn about water, it's this: water means rebirth. It carves stone, cleanses filth, and heals the weary -- but only when it's pure. Taint it, and it'll ruin all it touches.\n\nIf ye seek the water sapta, find Hervdana Saegrund in the Wetlands. Her family dwells in a cave beneath the southern falls.\n\nGo on then, don't let the river outrun ye.", objectives = "Find Hervdana Saegrund in the Wetlands.", completion = "Aye, I see it in yer eyes, {race}. You're wonderin' what kind o' soul chooses to live out here, deep in the Wetlands, with Dark Iron scum lurkin' about and nary a guard in sight. Well, we all have our reasons, love. \n\nBut the real question is, what brings you to our home? Out here at the edge of the falls, I reckon we both know the answer to that." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94497] = { title = "Call of Water", description = "Ah, so ye've come seekin' the sapta, have ye? Well then, listen close, love. To find understandin' and earn the sapta, ye must seek water in its various forms. As ye gather the samples, keep yer eyes open. Watch the beasts that guard it, the land it nourishes, and how it changes lives.\n\nWe'll start simple: fill this skin at the base o' the falls, where the fresh meets the brackish. Go on now, and mind the marsh.", objectives = "Fill the Empty Brown Waterskin at the bottom of the waterfalls below Hervdana's cave and return it to her in the Wetlands.", progress = "I'm nearly ready to send ye off on the rest o' yer tasks. But tell me, have ye filled the skin yet? The ocean brings life, aye -- but it carries sediment, minerals, and energies far different from the snowmelt and springwater of the highlands. Where sea and spring meet, there's wisdom to be found.", completion = "Glad ye managed to steer clear o' the Dark Iron. Shame they've crept so far north--makes ye wonder what dwarfkind could do if the clans ever stopped squabblin' and worked as one.\n\nStill, the tides rise high when the moons are strong, and the seawater floods the marsh. It's here that we study our estuary water.\n\nThank ye for this sacred offering, it marks the beginning of your stage as a vessel--one who seeks the waters' wisdom." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94499] = { title = "Call of Water", description = "Aye, Redridge drinks deep from Lake Everstill, but by the time the waters tumble down Stonewatch Falls, somethin' has seeped in. The murlocs down there are big, twisted brutes. Not like the ones ye find here or in the Loch. Lucky for the townsfolk they keep to the base o' the falls.\n\nBring a sampling to me. I've a mind to find out if it's magic, venom, or somethin' worse that's taintin' the waters near that old fort.", objectives = "Fill the Empty Red Waterskin at Stonewatch Falls near the Nightcrawler Murlocs and return to Hervdana Saegrund in the Wetlands.", progress = "The folk o' Lakeshire don't ken how good they've got it -- fresh water flowin' right at their boots, keepin' their nets full, their crops green, and their coin purses jinglin'. Even when the kingdom's guard can barely spare a lad with a sword, they've got Everstill watchin' over 'em.", completion = "Aye, this is good water, {name}. The magic used by the shadowseers in the region must be changin' the murlocs. Nothin' but pure water, this be. Yer dedication to the task at hand and abilities to seek out that which is needed proves you're ready for the next stage of your journey.\n\nOne more sample is all I need to create the reagent needed for your sapta. Norric will be pleased as well." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94500] = { title = "Call of Water", description = "Take this waterskin and journey deep into the emerald shade o' Ashenvale. Astranaar rests cradled by waters untouched by corruption. Ruins litter the bed o' the lake, hinting at a bygone era. Bring back a sample from the lake. Pure, ancient, and possibly enchanted water.\n\nIt's the last liquid I need before I send ye back to Norric.\n\nBoard the boat in Menethil to Auberdine. It stops in Southshore on the way over.\n\nAnd mind yerself... the forest's got eyes, and they don't blink.", objectives = "Fill the Unfilled Blue Waterskin at the waters of Astranaar in Ashenvale and return to Hervdana Saegrund in the Wetlands.", progress = "Do you have the water yet, {name}? If ye haven't made the trek to Kalimdor yet, be careful.", completion = "Well done, {name}! With all three samples in hand, I'll brew ye a vial o' water so pure it'd make the mountains weep. It's the final piece for yer rite o' passage. I'm proud to call ye kin, {name}. Ye've done {class} proud, and I look forward to hearing yer tales in the future." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94501] = { title = "Call of Water", description = "Norric will have one more task for ye before rewarding ye with the water totem rites. The vial of water I've given ye is necessary for whatever that task is. Go now and find him. We shall meet again some day.", objectives = "Bring the Vial of Purest Water to Norric Lochthane in Loch Modan.", progress = "Hello again, {name}. Yer looking well. \n\nWhat brings you back to me so soon?", completion = "Ahh, water blessed by Hervdana herself, and gathered by your own hands? A gift indeed. \n\nThese vials shall birth your sapta, letting you glimpse the water spirits at Stendel's Pond, near Moonbrook. The last few drops of the water have an equally important purpose... waste not even a cork stopper dampened with sacred water." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94502] = { title = "Call of Water", description = "In Westfall, outside o' Moonbrook lies Stendel's Pond. Once a pure spring, now touched by dark forces. The spirits there 'ave gone silent. \n\nYe must drink the water sapta, then face the corruption that fouls the waters. Take its bracers and the last drops o' Hervdana's potion, then place 'em on the shrine. That'll call forth a spirit, cleansed and true. Speak with it, learn what ye can.\n\nBring me proof the deed's done, and I'll grant ye the totem.", objectives = "Drink the Water Sapta and Cleanse the corruption at Stendel's Pond in Westfall.\nReturn to Norric in Loch Modan when finished.", progress = "The shrine stands aged and forgotten, cloaked in dust and cobwebs. The pond beside it lies eerily still, its surface untouched by wind or life. Scattered along the shore are the bones of beasts once burdened by labor. The water's murky sheen raises a troubling question--has it been poisoned by the surrounding malaise, or is it the very source of it?", completion = "You place the bracers atop the shrine and then pour the remaining drops of Norric's potion into dry stone. You begin to incant the simple words Norric taught you and the droplets vaporize atop the stone within the bindings...." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94503] = { title = "Call of Water", description = "Light erupts as the final word leaves your lips. The hiss of water turning to mist fades into silence, and your senses reel as the corrupt spirits around you unravel, their essence scattered like ash in the wind.", objectives = "Speak to the Minor Manifestation of Water in Westfall.", completion = "Thanks to you. Thanks to the shamans.\n\nCorruption ebbs but life continues to wane. Up to shamans to protect life." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94504] = { title = "Barkskin Beginnings", description = "Some may speak with you now, but not all. For more of our tribe to be what you know as friend, you must not rush.\n\nStay by our side, work with our young and old, and guard us from those who wish us harm.\n\nWhen you have more to bring to us, we will have more to share.", objectives = "Raise your reputation with the Barkskin Burrow to Neutral." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94505] = { title = "Call of Water", description = "Take shard. Take shard and give life.\n\nGive life and understand. Understand water is life... corruption stops life.\n\nYou protect and give life with water's power.", objectives = "Bring the Shard of Water to Norric Lochthane in Loch Modan.", progress = "How fared your journey to Westfall? Success there is hard to measure, but even small victories carry weight.", completion = "Aye, this is the proof I asked for, and ye've done well, {name}. I'm proud to be the first to offer my congratulations--and yer water totem. Use it wisely, and may fortune walk beside ye.\n\nYer next trial won't come soon, so take this time to learn. Pure water heals, aye, but its gifts go far beyond mending wounds." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94532] = { title = "Gnoll Infestation", description = "Though the gnoll presence has dwindled with the Twilight's encroachment, the threat remains.\n\nThe hills to the southwest are infested with their kind, disrupting trades and travelers alike.\n\nClear a path for our allies by removing the threat.", objectives = "Kill 8 Redridge Mystics, 8 Redridge Trappers, and 6 Redridge Brutes for Neza Bloodsnout at Rog'mar." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94533] = { title = "Snargl's Snout", description = "Among the cackling inhabitants of the Bristle Hills southwest of here is an elder gnoll by the name of Snargl. The sounds emanating from this particular gnoll are quite unpleasant. Their presence inspires those around, creating a problem for allies and scouts who enter the area.\n\nA trophy as a memento of our having dealt with this most unpleasant gnoll fiend would fit nicely with my collection.\n\nBe swift about it, {name}.", objectives = "Locate Snargl in the Bristle Hills, kill him, and retrieve his snout for Neza Bloodsnout." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94535] = { title = "Bristle Hills Bandits", description = "Our allies mining ore from the hills to the south reported several attacks by gnolls in the area.\n\nTravel south, locate their camps and retrieve the stolen ore. Take it from their dead bodies if need be.", objectives = "Gather 40 Stolen Ore from gnolls in the Bristle Hills for Kreza Darkthorn." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94556] = { title = "Jom-jom's Escape", description = "Jom-jom came looking for friend. Now Jom-jom want to go home.", objectives = "Escort Jom-jom to Clugfist at Bolder'ok." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94559] = { title = "UNUSED", description = "There is a turncoat amongst the Al'Aketh. They claim to know the cult's true intentions for the island and want to come in, but will only do so with assurances of protection.\n\nThis defector is hiding at a house just northwest of Valanaar, just inside the highlands. I need someone who can discreetly go there, find the traitor, find out and escort him back to us. This might be a trap, but if this information is as important as this traitor claims, it's worth some risk.", objectives = "Seek out the Al'Aketh Turncoat in the Shen'dar Highlands." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94568] = { title = "The Cult's True Plans", description = "The turncoat clearly was afraid of what the cult had planned, enough so to defect and seek our aid. It's truly unfortunate that he is dead and took his secrets to the grave with him.\n\nWe must discuss this further to determine our next steps.", objectives = "Speak with Talaanis Shadowsong and observe the conversation.", progress = "That turncoat risked everything to escape the cult and bring us this crystal...", completion = "We could try and send peacekeepers to directly engage the cult forces, but we would not fare well against them in open battle.\n\nWe are going to need a different approach." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94613] = { title = "My Kingdom for a Horse", description = "Our warhorses come from two nearby farms. One of them, owned by the Wheeler family off the road just outside of town, has apparently lost all of their stock. The cause of this is currently unknown.\n\nWith no horses, we have no cavalry, and without cavalry, our campaign against the Horde stands no chance.\n\nThus, you see, this situation must be resolved with utmost haste. Of where to start, however, I am less sure.\n\nGo to Wheeler's Grange and speak to Benjy. See what he has to say for himself.", objectives = "Go to Wheeler's Grange to inquire about the missing horses." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94614] = { title = "Freshwater Fiends", description = "You seen those murlocs down by the river, just west of here? Nasty things. Bad for my animals, and bad for the wildlife. Not to mention, they've settled right on top of my favorite fishing spot!\n\nThere ain't a soul in the Riverglades who wouldn't appreciate you getting rid of a few, that's for sure. \n\nPlease, kill any you see. You'd be doin' us a whole heap of good.", objectives = "Kill 8 Mudfin Oracles and 8 Mudfin Warriors along the river near Wheeler's Grange." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94615] = { title = "Foal Play", description = "I've got no idea what happened to our horses. I got up one morning to feed 'em and they were all gone, just like that.\n\nLife outside Farholde's a bit rougher. Anything could've got 'em--animals, murlocs, orcs, you name it.\n\nIf we wanna narrow down our list of culprits, we oughta search around the stables for clues.", objectives = "Search near the stables at Wheeler's Grange for evidence of the missing horses' whereabouts." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94616] = { title = "Water Sapta", description = "", objectives = "Take the water sapta and find the tainted pond water in Westfall, {name}. I have great faith in your abilities.", completion = "Take the water sapta and find the tainted pond water in Westfall, {name}. I have great faith in your abilities." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94617] = { title = "Coyote Huntin'", description = "There's a pack of coyotes livin' in a den west of here. We can see 'em sometimes from across the river. They used to hunt fish on the shore, but I guess the murlocs pushed 'em out of their usual feeding ground, and so they've taken to eating horses.\n\nThe leader of the coyote pack's a bigger one with dark fur. We'd nicknamed him \"Sootfur\". I reckon if you kill him, the rest'll scatter.", objectives = "Kill the coyote known as Sootfur, and bring its pelt back to Benjy Wheeler." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94618] = { title = "Wheeler's Fleeing Steeds", description = "From what you found, it seems like the coyotes got most of the horses. Still, there's a few not accounted for.\n\nThose that didn't get eaten probably ran off scared someplace. I don't know how many of those horses there are, but we'd better find 'em before the coyotes come back.\n\n<Benjy holds out a sack in front of you.>\n\nHere. If you find one, give it some of our feed. That'll get it to trust you so you can lead it back here.", objectives = "Find one of the horses that fled Wheeler's Grange after the coyote attack and give it some feed." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94638] = { title = "Strength and Mercy", description = "You have come to me in hopes of learning to take a shape of strength. I have a task for you, though it lies heavy on my heart.\n\nMy mate, Ur'endra, has lost herself to madness and has begun to attack her own kin. Without the magic of the winds, many creatures have begun to lose themselves... Ur'endra included. She makes her lair in a cave to the west of here, in the bluffs along the border between the Shen'dar Highlands and the Gustberry Lowlands.\n\nEnd her suffering and I shall grant you my blessing.", objectives = "Find and kill Ur'endra in the Shen'dar Highlands.", progress = "What I ask of you is no easy task. Take heart in your courage and return to me when the deed is done.", completion = "The agony I feel over her loss is immeasurable, but it is what is necessary for the balance. You have demonstrated a resolve to persevere, even when a terrible price is asked.\n\nYou have done well, {class}. I shall grant you the blessing to take on the shape of my kin. Be a beacon for those that lack the strength to persevere and a defender of those in need.\n\nGo now, and embrace the way of the claw, child." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94668] = { title = "Bloodmaster's Ring", description = "You smashed weak Twilight ogres. But they weak.\n\nToday you show Bloodmaster and little goblin friend you belong.\n\nTomorrow, maybe we meet again if you still breathing.", objectives = "Report to Jezap at the Bloodmaster's Ring." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94669] = { title = "Pay to Play", description = "First things first. I'm gonna need a deposit for your, uh... safety.\n\nLook, I don't make the rules here. It's required.\n\nNow if you should choose not to pay I'll be forced to tell old Clugfist our new friend wasn't so keen on proving their strength to our warm, welcoming friends here.\n\nThat would be a real shame. Catch my drift, bub?", objectives = "Pay the safety deposit to qualify for the Bloodmaster's Ring." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94670] = { title = "Bloodmaster's Ring", description = "The battle of the Bloodmaster's Ring begins!\n\nWe'll start you off easy here, pal. This flighty fiend'll take you down, then pick ya clean.\n\nNow quit standin' around and step into the ring. Fame awaits!", objectives = "Defeat Buzzbeak in the Bloodmaster's Ring." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94672] = { title = "Encroaching Twilight", description = "Humans are not our only adversary within the Riverglades, {name}, nor are they our most dire.\n\nA cult known as the Twilight's Hammer has begun a campaign against those they deem heretics in the eyes of their twisted gods. The ravaged remains of a human settlement to the west are but the first to fall to their conquest. No doubt Rog'mar will be next.\n\nWe cannot afford to let them establish a foothold so close to our doorstep. Go to this so-called Sunnyglade and thin their numbers.", objectives = "Defeat 8 Twilight Raiders and 8 Twilight Neophytes within Sunnyglade for Tran'gul in Rog'mar." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94678] = { title = "Gnoll Infestation", description = "The gnolls have been a thorn in our side ever since we arrived. While less a threat than the Twilight's Hammer, they are aggressive, persistent and, worst of all, numerous.\n\nThe hills beyond this post are infested with them, making passage to the north dangerous, and posing a threat to those living outside the walls of Farholde Keep.\n\nIf we are ever to make these lands safe, removing the gnoll threat is imperative.", objectives = "Kill 8 Redridge Mystics, 8 Redridge Trappers, and 6 Redridge Brutes for Cedric Dalton at Southern Watch." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94679] = { title = "Snargl's Snout", description = "Gnolls value strength above all else. By killing their strongest, we not only lessen the threat they pose physically, but also strike fear into their hearts.\n\nIn a den among the Bristle Hills is a notorious gnoll by the name of Snargl. His death would no doubt sow panic among the Redridge's ranks.\n\nBring me his snout, and be quick about it.", objectives = "Locate Snargl in the Bristle Hills, kill him, and bring his snout to Cedric Dalton at Southern Watch." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94680] = { title = "Twilight Missives", description = "There have always been small pockets of Twilight's Hammer cultists here and there, but never have I seen them in such numbers. They seem emboldened by someone, or something, to expand their influence.\n\nI would know more of these cultists and what they seek. Their shadowmancers are blessed by the dark powers and are likely the most trusted within their order to lead attacks of this scale.\n\nBring me anything you find off their corpses that we may glean knowledge into their campaign.", objectives = "Retrieve 3 Twilight Missives from Twilight Shadowmancers in Sunnyglade for Tran'gul in Rog'mar." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94727] = { title = "Digging for Answers", description = "The Twilight's Hammer are here for more than simple chaos, {name}. They appear to be digging throughout the Riverglades for something. As for what they are searching for, I cannot say. A source of power, of course, but what that is still eludes me.\n\nTheir zealots may not be willing to divulge their secrets, but they must have someone doing the digging for them. These are the ones you are to question. Return to Sunnyglade and 'convince' one of their miners to talk. We must get to the bottom of this.", objectives = "Convince a Twilight's Hammer miner in Sunnyglade to divulge their secrets." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94733] = { title = "Our Ogre Friend", description = "Alright, so you won a few battles. I think you might have what it takes to make it here after all.\n\nBefore I convince our next combatant to jump into the ring with you there's something I need from you first--food for Chub'chob's pet boar, Snufflesnout.\n\nI promised I'd look after it, and, well, this gig here's keepin' me quite busy. Trust me, this'll benefit the both of us.\n\nMosey on over to the east of Clugfist's clubhouse. You're lookin' for a shy fella who goes by the name Gobam.", objectives = "Locate Gobam in Bolder'ok." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94734] = { title = "A Boar's Delight", description = "Gobam know Chub'chob pet love to eat food. Specially good food!\n\nYum yum berry and plant from river make good treat for Snufflesnout. Berry sweet. Best berry from human farm near ocean.\n\nYou find. Bring back. Me help make big treat.", objectives = "Gather 8 Sweetberry and 12 Riverweed for Gobam." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94737] = { title = "A Treat for a Friend", description = "Ok friend. Here is treat. Snufflesnout snort and be happy when she see this.\n\nAnd tell goblin please stop talk so much.", objectives = "Deliver the bundle of goods to Jezap Jinglesprocket in Bolder'ok." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94739] = { title = "Bloodmaster's Ring", description = "Glad you made it through the first round, I guess.\n\nThis next contestant and I go way back. He ain't the brightest fella, but he's sure good at pummeling anything in his path.\n\nJust head on into the pit and get yourself ready while I make the announcement.", objectives = "Defeat Kronk in the Bloodmaster's Ring." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94744] = { title = "The Wayward Warrior", description = "You did well slowing the Twilight's Hammer. Their foothold in Sunnyglade has weakened and you've turned their ogre warriors against them. Now we take the fight to them.\n\nMy brother, Dag'rosh, has already gone ahead with a scouting party. I would have preferred he waited for you, but he is impulsive and overeager--like a true warrior. I'd be honored if you joined him in battle at their stronghold to the west.", objectives = "Find Da'grosh in the hills west of Rog'mar." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94745] = { title = "Carving a Path", description = "Do you see the fortress just west of here? The Twilight's Shroud, they call it. Filled to the brim with Twilight's Hammer cowards.\n\nThey may have walls and numbers, but their pitiful reliance on devilry and ancient gods makes them weak. Show them how vulnerable they really are!", objectives = "Defeat 8 Twilight Fanatics, 8 Twilight Corrupters, and 8 Twilight Champions within the Twilight's Shroud for Da'grosh." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94748] = { title = "Break Their Chains", description = "Those Twilight's Hammer dogs caught us before we could properly begin our attack. I was able to fight my way out, but my warriors were not so lucky. They were dragged off by the cult's champions and imprisoned in the fortress to the west.\n\nOrcs do not belong in cages, {class}. Free my brothers and sisters, and we will show these mongrels a real fight.", objectives = "Rescue 5 Rog'mar Scouts within the Twilight's Shroud for Da'grosh." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94768] = { title = "Bring Me His Head", description = "Tran'gul's notes pointed to a leader of this Twilight's Hammer presence somewhere in that fortress. With my warriors free and the cult's numbers in disarray, now is the time to pierce the heart of this infestation.\n\nReturn to the Twilight's Shroud and enter their Stronghold. That is where you will find Overlord Kilgar. That is where we will exact our revenge.", objectives = "Defeat Overlord Kilgar within the Twilight's Shroud and bring his head to Da'grosh." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94773] = { title = "Divine Grace", description = "", objectives = "You have done the Light a great service by becoming a shining example to those who travel in these dangerous lands and beyond. Please, accept this lesson as a thanks for all you've done.", completion = "You have done the Light a great service by becoming a shining example to those who travel in these dangerous lands and beyond. Please, accept this lesson as a thanks for all you've done." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94774] = { title = "Divine Grace", description = "You've caught the attention of our superiors, {name}. They've asked you to travel to the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind as soon as possible. Apparently they feel you've proven yourself already and are prepared to further your training. When you get there, find High Priestess Laurena. She will be able to guide you further. Good luck, and may the Light be with you.", objectives = "Speak to High Priestess Laurena in Stormwind.", completion = "I'm glad you've arrived, {name}. There are many things we will have to discuss, but more importantly is your training in the ways of the Light.\n\nThere are lessons all servants of the Light must learn. If you are ready, we'll begin discussing some of those now." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94775] = { title = "Divine Grace", description = "Elune bless you, good {race}. I hope your Light finds you and protects you well this day.\n\nOne of your priests was here not long ago looking for you. He mentioned you returning to the Cathedral of Light as soon as possible to speak with High Priestess Laurena. It seems you've done well to garner such attention. I wouldn't spend too much time here--your people have need of you.", objectives = "Speak to High Priestess Laurena in Stormwind." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94776] = { title = "Divine Grace", description = "Time's come for you to head to Stormwind, {name}. High Priestess Laurena in the Cathedral of Light wants to speak to you. Gotta be somethin' really good or really bad for the High Priestess to want you there personally, but I'm guessin' you've only done well for yourself and it's a good thing that she wants to speak to ya.\n\nBut don't waste too much time 'round here. I'd head there as soon as you can.", objectives = "Speak to High Priestess Laurena in Stormwind." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94777] = { title = "Divine Grace", description = "Just a short time ago, one of your priests was here looking for you, {race}. He said that if I were to see you, I should direct you towards the Cathedral of Light. He said it was very important, but I would not be overly concerned if I were you. His demeanor seemed positive... as though it were good news. I wouldn't take too long in making my way there if I were you.\n\nElune be with you, good {race}.", objectives = "Speak to High Priestess Laurena in Stormwind." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94778] = { title = "Divine Grace", description = "You're needed in Stormwind, {name}. The High Priestess there, Laurena, says it's time for you to prove you're worthy of the next level of your training. Don't waste too much time finding your way there. You can find her in the Cathedral of Light in the center of the city. Give her my regards, and prove how worthy you are of such a calling. The Light be with you, {name}.", objectives = "Speak to High Priestess Laurena in Stormwind." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94779] = { title = "Divine Grace", description = "Praise be to Elune, and to your Light, {name}.\n\nAbout this time, many of our order learn abilities reflecting their faith in Elune. If knowledge serves me, I believe the same holds true for your order also.\n\nWhen your business in Darnassus is complete, I would seek out one of your High Priestesses for further training.", objectives = "Speak to High Priestess Laurena in Stormwind." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94782] = { title = "The Western Post", description = "With the warlocks under control, I'd say this area's well in wing.\n\n<The crow nods sagely, looking pleased.>\n\nThough our work here is done, there are other areas that could use your help and as an underwing of mine I would like you to go see what all the fuss is about.\n\nFollow the path northwest up the road to the old outpost. An old friend awaits!", objectives = "Meet Zet'gan at the outpost." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94789] = { title = "Call of Air", description = "The winds o' Azeroth greet ye, and soon ye'll stand among some o' our mightiest kin. I'm proud to see how far ye've come--your future looks bright indeed.\n\nThe element o' air's a tricky one to master, but I've faith your skill will see ye through any challenge.\n\nMake your way north into Arathi Highlands. In its northern hills, you'll find Veyric Thundervein. He'll teach ye more.", objectives = "Find Veyric Thundervein in Arathi Highlands." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94792] = { title = "Taming the Beast", description = "Many hunters prefer to travel with animal companions. With a beast at your side, you will find that you can survive even the most dangerous of circumstances. As they say, everything is easier with a friend. However, obtaining an animal companion is something that must be done with care. The balance of nature is delicate, and must always be respected.\n\nTake this Taming Rod with you to the forest. With it, you will be able to tame a Rockhide Boar and practice your skills as a hunter.", objectives = "Use the Taming Rod to tame a Rockhide Boar. Practice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Josephine Carson.", progress = "You will learn, {name}, and one day you will be a great {class}.", completion = "Excellent, {name}! You are quite a fast learner." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94793] = { title = "Training the Beast", description = "You now have the power to tame a pet, but you must also gain the skills to train it. For this, there is none better than Isaac Chan, a lifelong woodsman. He will give you the ability to train your new pet.\n\nGo with the winds, young {class}.", objectives = "Speak to Isaac Chan in Goldshire.", completion = "A fledgling {class}, I see. Yes, I can bestow you with the skills you need to train and guide your pet. Not only will you be able to teach your pet new abilities, you will now be able to feed your pet, as well as revive it, should it fall in battle.\n\nRemember, {name}, always respect the balance and live in awe of nature around you. Now, go forth. We shall speak again, at a later date." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94817] = { title = "Confounding Flash", description = "", objectives = "You took your time arriving, {name}. But you can be excused given your dedicated service to the Light. Please pay close attention to this lesson.", completion = "You took your time arriving, {name}. But you can be excused given your dedicated service to the Light. Please pay close attention to this lesson." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94818] = { title = "Contingency Plan", description = "", objectives = "Continue your service to the Light and you will become a great {class}, {name}. Maintain your vigilance and dedication!\n\nYou are ready for your next lesson in service." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94819] = { title = "Contingency Plan", description = "{name}, your High Priestess Mims would have an audience with you in Ironforge. Make haste, my clever friend, your next test quickly approaches. Although I wish I could bear witness to your race's own special rites, my place is here. But may the Light go with you in your travels. Mims should still be in the Mystic Ward once you reach the city. She will be waiting.", objectives = "Speak to High Priestess Mims in Ironforge.", completion = "Continue your service to the Light and you will become a great {class}, {name}. Maintain your vigilance and dedication!\n\nYou are ready for your next lesson in service." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94820] = { title = "Contingency Plan", description = "Your race is so very clever, {name}. We are proud to call you allies. And as each day's sun sets, you and your kin grow closer to reclaiming your city, but with the burden of keeping your families safe in exile. That yearning for home must weigh heavily on you.\n\nWord came from Ironforge just recently. It asked that you return there and speak to High Priestess Mims in the Mystic Ward. I would not keep her waiting. May Elune guide your travels.", objectives = "Speak to High Priestess Mims in Ironforge." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94821] = { title = "Confounding Flash", description = "A priest recently visited our halls seeking you out, young {race}. He said that he was on a mission to find you and that you should return to the Hall of Mysteries in Ironforge as soon as possible. When you arrive, seek out High Priestess Mims--she will tell you more.\n\nThe Light be with you, {name}.", objectives = "Speak to High Priestess Mims in Ironforge.", completion = "You took your time arriving, {name}. But you can be excused given your dedicated service to the Light. Please pay close attention to this lesson." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94822] = { title = "Confounding Flash", description = "You've caught the attention of our superiors, {name}. They've asked you to travel to the Hall of Mysteries in Ironforge as soon as possible. Apparently they feel you've proven yourself already and are prepared to further your training. When you get there, find High Priestess Mims. She will be able to guide you further. Good luck, and may the Light be with you.", objectives = "Speak to High Priestess Mims in Ironforge.", completion = "You took your time arriving, Cub. But you can be excused given your dedicated service to the Light. Please pay close attention to this lesson." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94823] = { title = "Confounding Flash", description = "Elune bless you, good {race}. I hope your Light finds you and protects you well this day.\n\nOne of your priests was here not long ago looking for you. He mentioned you returning to the Hall of Mysteries as soon as possible to speak with High Priestess Mims. It seems you've done well to garner such attention. I wouldn't spend too much time here--your people have need of you.", objectives = "Speak to High Priestess Mims in Ironforge." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94824] = { title = "Confounding Flash", description = "Time's come for you to head to Ironforge, {name}. High Priestess Mims in the Hall of Mysteries commands you to come speak with her. Gotta be somethin' really good or really bad for the High Priestess to want you there personally, but I'm guessin' you've only done well for yourself and it's a good thing that she wants to speak to ya.\n\nBut don't waste too much time 'round here. I'd head there as soon as you can.", objectives = "Speak to High Priestess Mims in Ironforge.", completion = "You took your time arriving, Papi. But you can be excused given your dedicated service to the Light. Please pay close attention to this lesson." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94825] = { title = "Confounding Flash", description = "Just a short time ago, one of your priests was here looking for you, {race}. He said that if I were to see you, I should direct you towards the Hall of Mysteries. He said it was very important, but I would not be overly concerned if I were you. His demeanor seemed positive... as though it were good news. I wouldn't take too long in making my way there if I were you.\n\nElune be with you, good {race}.", objectives = "Speak to High Priestess Mims in Ironforge." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94826] = { title = "Confounding Flash", description = "Praise be to Elune, and to your Light, {name}.\n\nAbout this time, many of our order learn abilities reflecting their faith in Elune. If knowledge serves me, I believe the same holds true for your order also.\n\nWhen your business in Darnassus is complete, I would seek out your High Priestess for further training.", objectives = "Speak to High Priestess Mims in Ironforge." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94829] = { title = "What We Lost", description = "If you've come to demand more of our crop, you're too late. No doubt you saw my farm. Destroyed. All of it.\n\nGood folk toiled in these fields for years to feed troops and civilians alike. But when those cultists arrived, where was the military? Where was our promised protection after all the rations they'd taken from us?\n\nIf you've any sense of decency, I beg you. The least we can do is recover their belongings from those cursed raiders. Let my people rest with their kin in the graveyard to the west.", objectives = "Collect 5 Farmers' Mementos from Twilight Raiders and place them on the graves west of Elbrim's Farm." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94832] = { title = "Belle's Ring", description = "Unfortunately I haven't had much luck with identifying the ring's owner to bring closure to their family.\n\nPerhaps Daythor can be of assistance. He knew the others of our regiment quite well.\n\nI only hope it does not bring back unpleasant memories...", objectives = "Show the ring to Daythor Brellan." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94841] = { title = "Lost Shipping Crate", description = "<A handwritten label appears on the side of the crate. On the right side is a map with a large red circle along a southeastern shoreline north of a poorly drawn temple surrounded by water and some kind of winged creatures. On the left is a note in massive font.>\n\nPROPERTY OF FRIZ FRAZZLESPARK\n\nPOWDERFUSE PORT\n\nWARNING: NOT for tampering. Do NOT open without supervision.\n\n<An additional note appears at the bottom of the label.>\n\nIf lost, return to Friz Frazzlespark. Powderfuse Port. Riverglades.", objectives = "Deliver the Lost Shipping Crate to Friz Frazzlespark at Powderfuse Port in the Riverglades." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94842] = { title = "Unsavory Plant Food", description = "We make our own fertilizer out here. It's a special formula of mine that reeks like hell, but grows trees like they're weeds.\n\nIt's a 1:1:2 ratio of crawfish shells, manure, and murloc heads. Tasty, right?\n\nThe manure's easy enough. We've got the ranch to the south for that. The heads and shells? Those you're going to have to go wading in the river for.\n\nIf you feel like lending a hand, we could sure use your help getting some fertilizer ingredients.", objectives = "Gather 4 Jumbo Crawfish Shells, 4 pieces of Fresh Manure, and 8 Mudfin Murloc Heads for Halligan Turner." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94843] = { title = "From Seed to Sprout", description = "Considering you got yourself wrist-deep in guts and manure for us, it's only right you get to do the fun part too.\n\nThe boys and I gather seeds from the trees as we work. With the fertilizer you've provided, I've made a planting kit to put them in the ground to grow new saplings.\n\nTake it, and find some good planting spots around the work sites.", objectives = "Plant 1 saplings around the lumber camp with Halligan Turner's tree sprouting kit." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94857] = { title = "If a Tree Falls, and No One Hears...", description = "Stranger, listen to me!\n\nI work as a lumberjack for the nearby logging camp. As you can see, I've been trapped here in an accident. If I don't get out from here soon, I'll either bleed out, or be eaten by wild animals.\n\nPlease, go to the logging camp and fetch help!", objectives = "Go to Turner's Logging Camp and get help." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94858] = { title = "All That's Left", description = "There was one more thing I wanted to talk to you about, friend.\n\nWhen the Twilight's Hammer attacked, I put everyone who couldn't defend themselves in the barn to hide. I thought they would be safe. I thought...\n\n<Elbrim's voice cracks as he recounts what happened.>\n\nIf you could do me one last kindness, will you go see what's left of my family? They should be buried here at home with me. I just don't have the heart to check myself.", objectives = "Find Farmer Elbrim's family's possessions in the nearby barn and return them to him." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94861] = { title = "Helping Hands", description = "Well, I guess that explains why Curly didn't come back for lunch break. Looks like I have to bail him out again -- typical. The way he makes me worry, I swear, I'll be gray in a year.\n\nCome on, we'll have to save him ourselves, and it sounds like we don't have much time.", objectives = "Go with Hurley to save Curly." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94863] = { title = "Taming the Beast", description = "You've already mastered taming a boar. Now it's time for the next lesson. The forest holds fiercer companions, and with care, you can earn their trust.\n\nTake this Taming Rod and seek out a Gray Forest Wolf. Remember, nature's balance must be respected. Prove your skill as a hunter once more.", objectives = "Use the Taming Rod to tame a Gray Forest Wolf. Practice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Josephine Carson.", progress = "With learning, {name}, comes mastery.", completion = "Well done, {name}! You're quite in tune with the beast." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94864] = { title = "Taming the Beast", description = "You've proven yourself by taming a boar and a wolf. Now it's time for your final challenge. Elwynn's balance depends on respect and skill. Take this Taming Rod and seek out a Young Forest Bear. Show that you can earn the trust of even the mightiest companion. \n\nCompleting this lesson will deepen your attunement to beasts.", objectives = "Use the Taming Rod to tame a Young Forest Bear. Practice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Josephine Carson.", progress = "Go forth, {name}, and tame the burliest of Elwynn beasts.", completion = "The brawn of the forest. Brave work, {name}!" }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94872] = { title = "Buying Friendship: Magram", description = "The fierce Magram are undoubtedly winning the war of territories at the moment. While we can all be thankful the clashes haven't erupted too frequently throughout the desert, every day their village just to the east grows a little bigger; their soldiers a little bolder.\n\nI worry gravely about the consequences of an unchecked Magram clan, but I cannot deny their potential as an ally.\n\nIf you wish to earn their trust, offer this sack of totems to their quartermaster, but be careful.", objectives = "Bring the Totem Tote to the Magram Quartermaster at Magram Village in the Desolace to significantly increase your reputation with that clan. You must be of at least Neutral standing with the Magram Clan Centaur." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94873] = { title = "Buying Friendship: Gelkis", description = "Either dominant centaur clan is likely to pose a good ally, but I ought to offer a word of caution regarding the Gelkis.\n\nI have trustworthy intel that suggests, between the Magram and the Gelkis, the latter are very much on the losing side. This may work to our advantage--desperation may push the isolated clan into opening up to outside help.\n\nI have prepared a tote of totems for you to take to their quartermaster, assuming they have one, in Gelkis Village. This may work in our favor.", objectives = "Bring the Totem Tote to the Gelkis Quartermaster at Gelkis Village in the Desolace to significantly increase your reputation with that clan.  You must be of at least Neutral standing with the Gelkis Clan Centaur.", progress = "An outsider this deep in the village? You best be bringing business.", completion = "<Molkar peeks into the bag. A smirk tugs at his lips, falling only briefly as he catches a glimpse of a clearly fake totem. He pretends to not see it.>\n\nI do not know what possessed an outsider to bring our clan such a gift. It is a great boon for our people, as the Magram Clan have been unusually vicious as of late.\n\nYou no longer need to tread carefully in our village. I will inform Uthek, who will speak with the Khan." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94877] = { title = "Saving Sunnyglade", description = "When you look around you, what do you see? A broken home and a tired people.\n\nStormwind has left us to fend for ourselves, and we have less to do that with every day. Many within these walls are refugees who barely escaped tragedy without so much as even their own families.\n\nFarholde is no Stormwind, stranger. We lost a settlement in the northwest to the Twilight's Hammer, but we will not let them keep it. If you wish to fight, go to Sunnyglade and purge those savages from our lands.", objectives = "Defeat 8 Twilight Raiders, 8 Twilight Shadowmancers, and 8 Twilight Neophytes within Sunnyglade for Demar Brant." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94879] = { title = "Scraps of Knowledge", description = "You've seen the ruined city to the north, yes? Sunnyglade? Demar tries sending troops, but we're no closer to reclaiming it. I have a better idea.\n\nIn truth, this attack by the Twilight's Hammer is not the first. They seem to be coordinating from a centralized location, and I would know where. While you're out doing what you adventurers do best, see if you can't keep an eye out for any documents they may have misplaced. With enough of them, I should be able to piece together their intentions.", objectives = "Collect 5 Twilight Pages from within Sunnyglade for Ashe Amberall in Farholde Keep." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94881] = { title = "Curious Trinkets", description = "My, what have we here? A brave new {class} come to save us from our woes? How charming! Maybe you can help me with something then? I'd quite like to learn more about this cult in Sunnyglade.\n\nLike any cult, they operate in a caste system. Those with an affinity for magic are often in high favor and are given tokens to demonstrate such. These charms are then imbued, and thus have a rich abundance of cultist magic.\n\nI wish to see these tokens for myself. Be a dear and see if you can bring me a few, hmm?", objectives = "Retrieve 25 Twilight Charms from Twilight Shadowmancers and Twilight Neophytes in Sunnyglade for Ashe Amberhall in Farholde Keep." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94884] = { title = "An Unsettling Discovery", description = "I've had enough of this cave. Once you clear your way out, I'll slip out amidst the chaos.\n\nI'm afraid I'm in too weak of condition to carry those samples, however. Their energy is overwhelming, and I've been trapped down here for Light knows how long. Once we get out of here, please take them to Lady Amberhall immediately. I must rest.", objectives = "Bring the Filled Crystal Catalyst to Ashe Amberhall in Farholde Keep." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94885] = { title = "Field Marshal's Log", description = "The log is full of meticulous recordings on the comings and goings of Twilight's Hammer forces throughout the Riverglades. \n\nThe author is nowhere to be found, but this information could help shed light on enemy movements.\n\nSomeone in Farholde will want to see this.", objectives = "Deliver the Field Marshal's Log to Demar Brant in Farholde Keep." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94886] = { title = "The Western Front", description = "As helpful as you've been here in Farholde, I believe your talents could be put to better use elsewhere.\n\nA patrol of ours went missing some time ago. They were in charge of our western borders, but with the information Miss Amberhall has uncovered, I fear they walked right into the Twilight Hammer's central encampment.\n\nWe can handle the cleanup in Sunnyglade ourselves. If the good lady is right, it's critical that we check on our wayward sergeant. He could use all the help he can get.", objectives = "Find Sergeant Riftan near the Twilight's Shroud to the west." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94887] = { title = "Saving Marshal Ryan", description = "Field Marshal Ryan is one of our best. His keen eyes and reliable intel have been paramount to our war efforts.\n\nHis final reports refer to a Twilight's Hammer fortress to the west. Find him before it's too late. And take his logbook with you. It may offer more clues as to the whereabouts of our missing marshal.", objectives = "Find Marshal Ryan within the Twilight's Shroud." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94888] = { title = "No Soldier Left Behind", description = "If Amberhall is so impatient for her report, it would have been nice if she sent more than one {class}. Must be hard work hiding in her ivory tower.\n\nLook, every attempt to contact Farholde Keep ends with our runners being captured by Twilight scouts. I can't afford to risk any more troops going into that fortress, but we can't keep my people imprisoned in there either.\n\nYou want us to return? Help me rescue my soldiers first. You should be able to find the keys to their cages off their champions' corpses.", objectives = "Rescue 5 Farholde Scouts within the Twilight's Shroud for Sergeant Riftan." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94889] = { title = "Carving a Path", description = "It seems every day the Twilight's Hammer are drawing more into their order, while we haven't heard so much as a word from Stormwind. Sooner or later we'll be overrun.\n\nI don't care what a bureaucrat like Amberhall says. I'm not abandoning this position while an army amasses in our own homeland. If we leave now, we'll only have to deal with these cultists again later. Only next time, on our doorstep.\n\nIf your orders are to babysit me anyway, at least make yourself useful and help me cull these zealots.", objectives = "Defeat 8 Twilight Fanatics, 8 Twilight Corrupters, and 8 Twilight Champions within the Twilight's Shroud for Sergeant Riftan." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94890] = { title = "Bring Me His Head", description = "With this kind of momentum, we can't stop now. The soldiers we rescued are itching to draw blood, and you've already proven yourself a capable battering ram.\n\nReturn to the Twilight's Shroud and finish what we've started. Their leader, an orc by the name of Overlord Kilgar, hides deep within his keep while his underlings are lost in their panic.\n\nIf we want to put an end to this, bring me the head of Kilgar. These gods-fearing cowards can't make a single decision on their own.", objectives = "Defeat Overlord Kilgar within the Twilight's Shroud and bring his head to Sergeant Riftan." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94891] = { title = "News to Farholde", description = "Seems like things are quieting down around here for now, but I want to keep an eye out. You want to send Amberhall a report? Send her this.\n\n<Sergeant Riftan tosses Kilgar's head back to you.>\n\nThat ought to shut her up. At least for a while. Good work out there.", objectives = "Return to Ashe Amberhall in Farholde Keep." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94892] = { title = "Dying Wish", description = "It's too late for me, stranger. I'm not going to be making it out of this one. Take my crest to the Knight Commander. Warn him...\n\n<Ryan's eyes begin to glaze over as he mumbles to himself.>\n\nI'm sorry. I should have come home. Abigail...", objectives = "Return Marshal Ryan's crest to Knight Commander Demar Brant in Farholde Keep." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94893] = { title = "Delivering Closure", description = "So, his final thoughts were of Abigail?\n\nI know this is not your business, friend, but I must ask you to deliver the news of the Marshal's passing on my behalf. Ryan's betrothed, Abigail Lawson, did not join us when we established Farholde Keep. The two of them apparently had a disagreement, and while I do not know the specifics, I do know that she now resides within Stormwind City.\n\nPlease take the Marshal's crest to Terry for me. I don't think my presence would be a welcome one.", objectives = "Deliver Marshal Ryan's Crest to Abigail Lawson in the Cathedral Square of Stormwind City." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94894] = { title = "The Twilight Threat", description = "Lady Amberhall told me of your exploits with the Twilight's Hammer. I'm impressed. But concerned.\n\nFarholde started its campaign originally to remove the Horde from our homeland. While that remains our primary goal, we cannot take this sudden surge in cultist activity lightly. If our pleas to Stormwind remain unheard, we will be overwhelmed as we face foes on two fronts alone.\n\nWith the evidence you carry, perhaps they can set aside their pride long enough to listen. At this point it's our only option.", objectives = "Deliver Kilgar's Head to Bolvar Fordragon within Stormwind Keep in Stormwind City." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94895] = { title = "Lost Shipping Crate", description = "<A handwritten label appears on the side of the crate. On the right side is a map with a large red circle along a southeastern shoreline north of a poorly drawn temple surrounded by water and some kind of winged creatures. On the left is a note in massive font.>\n\nPROPERTY OF FRIZ FRAZZLESPARK\n\nPOWDERFUSE PORT\n\nWARNING: NOT for tampering. Do NOT open without supervision.\n\n<An additional note appears at the bottom of the label.>\n\nIf lost, return to Friz Frazzlespark. Powderfuse Port. Riverglades.", objectives = "Deliver the Lost Shipping Crate to Friz Frazzlespark at Powderfuse Port in the Riverglades." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94896] = { title = "Aid For The Refugees", description = "You look like a capable adventurer. Do you happen to be headed towards Shadowgale Forest? Ban'aethal lies deep in the forest; that's where we're all from.\n\n<Ealaane gestures to the other refugees.>\n\nWe've recently had to evacuate Ban'aethal, as it began to fall into the sky. It was sudden and in the middle of the night. If you are headed that way, would you please look for any belongings left behind? The forest and village are far too dangerous for us to return to now.", objectives = "Collect 8 Abandoned Belongings from the ruins of Ban'aethal.", progress = "So many of us left with nothing more than the clothes on our backs. Any belongings you might recover would be cherished.", completion = "Thank you, {class}, you have done a great kindness to us refugees this day. I will make sure to return these to their owners. At least it gives us a place to start over from." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94897] = { title = "The Fate of a Loved One", description = "If you are traveling to Ban'aethal, I have a selfish request. My love, Resaan... I believe is no longer a part of this world. He had tried to go back to get supplies even though I begged him to stay. It has been over a week already and I fear the worst.\n\nPlease, if you find him, bring him home. If he has perished then I beg you to please bring me his heirloom.", objectives = "Find Resaan in the Ruins of Ban'aethal.", progress = "Have you any news of Resaan? Please, {class}, the wait is hard to endure after everything that has happened.", completion = "<Ealaane's eyes well with tears.>\n\nOh, Resaan my love. What will become of us now? There was so much... it feels as if our lives together had just started.\n\nThank you, {class}. The world is cruel to take both my home and my love from me. At least his heirloom will give me some closure." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94898] = { title = "Violent Winds (Temp Disabled)", description = "When our home started to fall into the sky that fateful night, it's as if the elements themselves were waiting to consume us. Wind spirits began appearing as we were fleeing, and to our dismay they began attacking the fleeing survivors.\n\nWe lost many villagers to the sky, but even more to the relentless anger of those wind spirits. I don't know if it was our village falling into the sky, but they are extremely dangerous.\n\nIf you are able, please put them to rest.", objectives = "Slay 10 Wind Hollows." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94901] = { title = "Hopping Helpers", description = "[PH] Collect frogs", objectives = "Collect X Gustjumper frogs." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94902] = { title = "Valanaar Vintages", description = "[PH] Collect grapes from the vineyard", objectives = "Collect X grapes." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94907] = { title = "A Small Favor", description = "You've been such a good little {class} for me, I wonder if I could ask you to do one more small favor.\n\nWith the reagents you collected being so finely attuned to Twilight's Hammer magic, they are perfect for a summoning ritual. However, we'll need to take them to the source of their power.\n\nShould you happen upon a conduit while you're gallivanting about the Twilight's Shroud, see if you can't call upon one of the cult's thralls and capture it with this soulstone for me. For questioning, of course.", objectives = "Summon a Twilight's Thrall from a conduit within the Twilight Shroud and capture it with Amberhall's Soulstone." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94911] = { title = "Child of Nature", description = "Greetings, young {race}. I can see that you have much promise in the druidic arts. There is one who you may want to speak with in the city of Thunder Bluff by the name of Turak Runetotem. He will teach you how to reach the stronghold of the Cenarion Circle on Kalimdor, Moonglade. \n\nYou will be welcomed there, and the druids of the circle will impart their knowledge upon you. \n\nAs your people would say--go with the wind's blessing, young one. I wish you good fortune in your adventures.", objectives = "Speak with Turak Runetotem in Thunder Bluff.", completion = "A high elf, speaking to me... in Thunder Bluff. Will wonders never cease?\n\nWell, shaper of wind, let me join our Earthen Ring brothers and sisters in welcoming you to Azeroth. My fellow druids of the Cenarion Circle have much wisdom to impart upon you, child of nature." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94912] = { title = "Child of Nature", description = "Greetings, young {class}. \n\nHave you heard of the Cenarion Circle? I'd expect not. They are an ancient order of naturalists and practitioners of the druidic arts, much like yourself. In the city of Stormwind you'll find a night elf by the name of Sheldras Moontree. He will teach you how to reach the stronghold of the Cenarion Circle on Kalimdor, a place called Moonglade.\n\nGo now. You have much to learn if you wish to save your home.", objectives = "Speak with Sheldras Moontree in Stormwind.", completion = "Greetings, fellow {class}. It pleases me to meet a fellow {class} from among the Skyborne, and to be among the first to welcome you to Azeroth.\n\nI think you will find that my fellow druids of the Cenarion Circle have much wisdom to impart upon you, child of nature." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94913] = { title = "Moonglade", description = "All druids are welcomed to the sacred lands of Moonglade. Keeper Remulos--Moonglade's guardian--keeps watch over all druids who hibernate there. I'll teach you the spell that lets you transport yourself there. Cast it whenever you seek Moonglade's knowledge or solace.\n\nAs for your first lesson here on Azeroth, travel to Moonglade and speak with Dendrite Starblaze in Nighthaven about the path you're now on. Good luck, young druid.", objectives = "Use the spell \"Teleport: Moonglade\" to travel to Moonglade. When you arrive, speak with Dendrite Starblaze in the village of Nighthaven.", completion = "Ah I see that you have already mastered the form of the Bear. Good, good. You are well on your way, young {class}." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94914] = { title = "Moonglade", description = "All druids are welcomed to the sacred lands of Moonglade. Keeper Remulos--Moonglade's guardian--keeps watch over all druids who hibernate there. I'll teach you the spell that lets you transport yourself there. Cast it whenever you seek Moonglade's knowledge or solace.\n\nAs for your first lesson here on Azeroth, travel to Moonglade and speak with Dendrite Starblaze in Nighthaven about the path you're now on. Good luck, young druid.", objectives = "Use the spell \"Teleport: Moonglade\" to travel to Moonglade. When you arrive, speak with Dendrite Starblaze in the village of Nighthaven.", completion = "Ah I see that you have already mastered the form of the Bear. Good, good. You are well on your way, young {class}." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94923] = { title = "Hats Off", description = "<Robbie leans in to talk to you, as if sharing a grave secret.>\n\nPsst! Hey <mister/miss>, I need your help!\n\nMy sister got me a hat for my birthday but I lost it playing in the river. I'm not allowed to be down there because of the murlocs so I can't ask Dad or Ellie for help because then they'll know where I was!\n\nIt's a good hat. I bet one of those murlocs found it and kept it for himself!", objectives = "Find Robbie's Hat somewhere along the river near the murlocs." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94924] = { title = "Hunting the Hunters", description = "The orcish poachers are a bloodthirsty lot. They'll kill anything that moves--be it men, lions, or horses. They are a threat to all life in the Riverglades, and must be stopped.\n\nThey roam the plains in packs, like rabid animals. If you see any, put them down.", objectives = "Kill 12 Rog'mar Poachers for Watcher Cornelius." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94925] = { title = "A Fur Trade", description = "Farholde prides itself on its independence, but there are a few things we can only get through trade.\n\nWe've negotiated an arrangement with a dealer at Powderfuse Port. We provide her with goods that are dangerous to acquire, and she provides us with specialty munitions.\n\nCurrently, she's in the market for lion fur. A pride of them live atop a large hill in the center of the plains. If you'd like to make yourself useful, you could aid me in harvesting some of their hides.", objectives = "Bring 8 Prized Lion Hides to Watcher Terral." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94926] = { title = "Drop the Hammer", description = "Like most ogre weaponry, this hammer is large, unwieldy, and well-worn. A creature of any other race could hardly swing it at all.\n\nTo you, it is of little more use than a trophy, but perhaps someone at Farholde would appreciate knowing of Komuk's demise.", objectives = "Take Komuk's Maul to Farholde Keep as proof of the ogre's demise." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94927] = { title = "Dunston Checks Out", description = "When you're ready, I'll unlock my shackles, and we'll commence the escape. We'll take the quickest route, right through the center of camp. Be prepared for a fight.\n\nOnce we're out, I'll return to Farholde for medical treatment. As a final favor, I ask that you update Cornelius on my whereabouts. Frankly, the last thing I want after all this is to get an earful from that man.", objectives = "Help Dunston break out of Bolder'ok then return to Watcher Cornelius." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94928] = { title = "A Few Furs for Friz", description = "These hides are to be delivered to Powderfuse Port. It is a goblin-run port to the northeast.\n\nWhen you get there, deliver the hides to Friz Frazzlespark. Tell her they're from Cornelius. The details of our trade have already been worked out, so she'll know what they are for.", objectives = "Deliver the Bundle of Lion Hides to Friz Frazzlespark at Powderfuse Port." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94929] = { title = "Deliver the Second Shipment", description = "I know I said that was it, but I promise, I wouldn't ask this if it weren't important. It's a shipment of utmost urgency.\n\nAn old acquaintance resides in a keep within the Riverglades. To get there, travel northeast through the bogs avoiding the deadly creatures within. Along the northeastern hillside sits an old path. Travel its road all the way through the hills and when you hit the fork in the road stay north, then east. You should see Farholde along the eastern shore.\n\nI thank you for your aid.", objectives = "Bring the Shipment to Demar Brant at Farholde Keep in the Riverglades." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94930] = { title = "Lost Shipping Crate", description = "<A handwritten label appears on the side of the crate. On the right side is a map with a large red circle along a southeastern shoreline north of a poorly drawn temple surrounded by water and some kind of winged creatures. On the left is a note in massive font.>\n\nPROPERTY OF FRIZ FRAZZLESPARK\n\nPOWDERFUSE PORT\n\nWARNING: NOT for tampering. Do NOT open without supervision.\n\n<An additional note appears at the bottom of the label.>\n\nIf lost, return to Friz Frazzlespark. Powderfuse Port. Riverglades.", objectives = "Deliver the Lost Shipping Crate to Friz Frazzlespark at Powderfuse Port in the Riverglades." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94931] = { title = "Stolen Saws", description = "The boys up at Southern Watch do a good job keeping gnolls out for the most part. Every now and then a few sneak into the camp at night and cause a bit of trouble. They especially like to steal saw blades, which they likely use to make weapons out of the sharp metal.\n\nIf you could get some back for us, it'd be a big help. The gnolls have probably got 'em stashed away somewhere in their camps up in the hills to the west.", objectives = "Recover 8 Saw Blades from the gnoll camps in Bristle Hills for Halligan Turner at the lumber mill." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94946] = { title = "The Magical City of Dalaran", description = "I had intended to be the first of us to step foot onto Azeroth, but recent events with the cult have changed my plans. As a result, I will be remaining here in Valanaar for a time. Fret not though, we have several mages awaiting our people's arrival in Dalaran. I'd encourage you to explore Azeroth while we set our affairs in order here. We will call upon agents such as yourself when you are needed.\n\nWhen you are ready, please proceed to the dock just outside this lodge and board the skycutter ship there.", objectives = "Take the skycutter ship from Zephras Isle to Dalaran City and speak with Danaaris Stargale when you arrive.", completion = "Ah, you've made it. Wonderful. It's going to take us some time to get ourselves established here, so you may want to take some time to explore the city. Be warned however, try not to venture too far from the safety of the city proper.  \n\nAs idyllic as this new land appears, it can be extremely dangerous to wander outside of Dalaran without appropriate preparation and experience." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94947] = { title = "Welcome to Azeroth", description = "It's a big world down here, and we need our people to start branching out to explore it. That's where you come in.\n\nThe Kirin Tor is a member of an \"Alliance\" of like-minded nations. The de-facto heart of this alliance is the city of Stormwind to the south. Elaadrin has asked me to find someone to travel to Stormwind and meet with the regent lord there, a human named Bolvar Fordragon.\n\nWhen you are ready, the Kirin Tor mages have set up a special portal for the High Order to use to access Stormwind.", objectives = "Take the Skyborne Portal to Stormwind and report to Bolvar Fordragon in Stormwind Keep.", completion = "Well met, {class}. I am Bolvar Fordragon, regent to the throne of Stormwind.\n\nA Kirin Tor messenger told me to expect to receive members of the High Order, and here you stand. It's been some time since a high elf has stood in this throne room, but I am glad to accept you now as a guest.\n\nOn behalf of the King, I welcome you to Stormwind and give you leave to travel freely through alliance lands. Welcome to Azeroth, Skyborne." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94961] = { title = "Biting the Hand", description = "<The gnoll pulls a bit of gold from his pocket and waves it at you.>\n\n{race}, I offer trade! There is more where this came from. Help me get revenge, and I will show you!", objectives = "Bring 20 Twilight Finger Bones to Fuzzle." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94962] = { title = "Bloodmaster's Ring", description = "Alright, so you got a few wins under your belt. So what?\n\nYou're a long way from becoming the champ, bub. But I tell ya what--I'll make sure this next battle ain't one you'll soon forget.\n\nHope you're ready for a surprise.", objectives = "Defeat Bonegnaw in the Bloodmaster's Ring." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94963] = { title = "Biting the Hand", description = "Come, {race}. It is time to leave this place. If any try to stop us, we will tear them to shreds!\n\nOnce we are safe, I will take you to your reward.", objectives = "<Fuzzle snarls.>" }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94964] = { title = "Bloodmaster's Ring", description = "Let's see if we can keep this crowd's excitement goin'.\n\nThis next contender ain't no joke.\n\nBest of luck to ya! See you soon, maybe.", objectives = "Defeat Mog'thar in the Bloodmaster's Ring." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94965] = { title = "Bloodmaster's Ring", description = "Alright, so I'll place the treat and then you enter the ring and prepare for what's comin'.\n\nWhat? Why you lookin' at me like that? I said we're gonna feed her. What I may have forgotten to mention was that ol' Snufflesnout gets pretty riled up at the sight of her favorite treat.\n\nYou're in a bit of a sticky situation here, bub. Proving yourself to our ogre friends is of the utmost importance, but boy oh boy would I be nervous inflicting harm to Chubchob's precious companion.\n\nWell, off ya go!", objectives = "Defeat Snufflesnout in the Bloodmaster's Ring." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94968] = { title = "Eye of Mugg", description = "Of the few that managed to infiltrate the cave, most have perished. It seems these Twilight have a foothold much larger than we thought. We will not stand by while these cultists continue to ravage these lands and make sacrifices of our allies. We end this now, {name}.\n\nInfiltrate this stronghold, slaughter their forces and bring me proof of their leader's demise.", objectives = "Infiltrate Krol'dok Stronghold and return to Krom'rosh with proof of their leader's demise." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94969] = { title = "Krol'dok No More!", description = "Don't ask. You wouldn't believe me if I told you.\n\nLet's just focus on getting me out of here! Oh, and you as well, of course.", objectives = "Escort Marcus Tilwell to safety." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94971] = { title = "A Paladin's Steed", description = "One of the most important parts of a paladin's arsenal has always been their warhorse. These specially consecrated animals bear paladins and their arms into battle, and are as fearless and bold as the best of us.\n\nWhile our situation has changed, our need for steeds to bear us into battle has not. It's time that you had such a mount for yourself.", objectives = "Speak with Danitha Morr to learn to summon your Warhorse." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94972] = { title = "Tome of Twilight", description = "With their location revealed, it is likely that within this stronghold are secrets kept well hidden from those we have encountered thus far. It would be wise for us to locate and recover any information that may be of use to our fight against these cultists.\n\nSee what you can uncover, {name}. I await your return.", objectives = "Recover the Tome of Twilight from Krol'dok Stronghold." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94973] = { title = "Krol'dok Moulding", description = "<The moulding appears to be for a key.>", objectives = "Find someone in Rog'mar who may know about the mould." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94974] = { title = "Key Ingredients", description = "The moulding is crude and worn, but we may be able to fashion a key.\n\nIt may take some time to gather the components necessary. I'll keep these embers running hot while you gather the materials.", objectives = "Bring 12 Thick Leather and 4 Iron Bar to Kreza Darkthorn." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94975] = { title = "A Token of Vengeance", description = "Our work here is not finished, {name}. These cultists have inflicted unimaginable pain upon our allies and rendered these lands for their taking.\n\nWe will not tolerate these actions any longer.\n\nTo the north lies a hidden cave network, masked by the rugged terrain. Our scouts spoke of cultist movement under the veil of darkness.\n\nSeek out this cave and find where these cultists are hiding. It's time we deliver a message they won't soon forget.", objectives = "Collect 15 Cultist Ears from the Twilight's Hammer in Krol'dok Stronghold." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94978] = { title = "Taming the Beast", description = "Every hunter begins by learning the bond between beast and master. This is your first challenge. In time, you'll tame creatures from every corner of the world, but for now, start with our rivers and lakes on Zephras. \n\nTake this Taming Rod and seek out a Windsong Crawler.\n\nShow that you can earn its trust, and begin your path toward true mastery.", objectives = "Use the Taming Rod to tame a Windsong Crawler found near bodies of water. \nPractice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Quel'ana Quickgale in Valanaar.", progress = "You will learn, {name}, and one day you will be a great {class}.", completion = "Well tamed, {name}! You are becoming adept already." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94979] = { title = "Taming the Beast", description = "You've proven you can tame the river's crawler. Now it's time to test your skill on open ground. The plains of Zephras echo with the cries of the galestrider, a proud, winged hunter that runs like the wind.\n\nTake this Taming Rod and seek one out. Travel to the lowlands and earn its trust.\n\nShow you're ready for the trials yet to come.", objectives = "Use the Taming Rod to tame an Ornery Galestrider in the Gustberry Lowlands. \nPractice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Quel'ana Quickgale in Valanaar.", progress = "You will learn, {name}, and one day you will be a great {class}.", completion = "You're back already! Impressive speed, {name}!" }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94980] = { title = "Krol'dok Moulding", description = "<The moulding appears to be for a key.>", objectives = "Find someone in Farholde Keep who may know about the mould." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94981] = { title = "Key Ingredients", description = "The moulding is rather crude, but we may be able to fashion a key with the right materials.\n\nI'll keep the embers running hot while you gather the necessary components.", objectives = "Bring 12 Thick Leather and 4 Iron Bars to Alphonse Dumas." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94982] = { title = "Eye of Mugg", description = "Our scouts mentioned a network of caves to the northwest along the mountains, hidden by natural surroundings. Most who sought information from deep within have yet to return. I fear they may be lost.\n\nThose watching from a distance mentioned a Twilight presence moving in and out of the caves, often in darkness.\n\nLocate this stronghold. If it is what I think it is we must deliver a deathly blow to their leader. Only then may we continue our efforts to remove them from these lands.", objectives = "Infiltrate Krol'dok Stronghold and return to Commander Brant with proof of their leader's demise." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94983] = { title = "Twilight Mementos", description = "The stories our scouts shared were quite horrid. I'll spare you the gruesome details. What we've discovered confirms previous reports of a cultist hideout.\n\nTo the north lies a cave, well hidden by its surroundings. This cave leads to... well, a place we've yet to infiltrate. We believe it's a foothold, nestled deep within the mountains.\n\nIt's time we repay the cultists for their actions against our allies.\n\nVenture north, seek out our enemies, and return to me with proof of their demise.", objectives = "Collect 8 Cultist Bangles from the Twilight's Hammer in Krol'dok Stronghold." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94984] = { title = "Tome of Twilight", description = "No matter our efforts, the Twilight forces persist. We've deduced they must be coming from somewhere else.\n\nWith the new pet you brought me, I was able to politely ask our dear Twilight Thrall if it knew anything about where its former masters were coming from. Of note was mention of shadow magics and an ogre by the name of Nar'gurk in a hidden stronghold north of Sunnyglade.\n\nSeek him out. Kill him and recover what you can. There must be something we can learn from these efforts.", objectives = "Kill Nar'gurk within Krol'dok Stronghold and recover any valuable information." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94992] = { title = "Rescue Roundup", description = "<The horse bows its head in your direction then nudges its nose into your underarm. Wherever you go, it may follow.>", objectives = "Bring the lost horse back to Wheeler's Grange." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94997] = { title = "Lingering Essence", description = "We mustn't linger. Take these to the keep at once.\n\nFind Ashe Amberhall. She may be a pain, but she's well respected in her field of study. Perhaps she can shed some light on what energies are contained within these objects.", objectives = "Bring the Satchel of Cursed Mementos to Ashe Amberhall in Farholde Keep." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94998] = { title = "Curios of Curiosity", description = "Quite simple to dispel, really. Remnants of something, that's for sure. What, exactly, I do not know.\n\nWell, I'm afraid I've done all that I can. I'm sorry if you were expecting more from me, but... on second thought, the craftsmanship of these is quite unique. Perhaps they could be of some use.\n\nTake these to Melanie Sable. Tell her I sent you. Let her know they're safe.\n\nShe may have some use for them just yet.", objectives = "Bring the Satchel of Mementos to Melanie Sable." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[94999] = { title = "Eyes for the Watchman", description = "Oh! Sorry, I didn't see you there.\n\nI was just putting together a little something for a friend of mine. Well... more of an acquaintance, really. Have you met Watcher Fredericks yet? He's stationed at Southern Watch just west of here.\n\nHe comes by the ranch on patrol every now and then. I thought it would be nice to give him a little something to show my appreciation.\n\nI'd deliver it myself, but I need to keep an eye on my little brother and tend to the ranch.\n\nI'm sure you understand.", objectives = "Deliver Eleanor's care package to Watcher Fredericks at Southern Watch." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95006] = { title = "Stolen Power", description = "<Orokai closes his eyes and becomes perfectly still as he communes with the branch. You can feel the stinging prickle of magic on your skin as he does so.>\n\nOh my, little mortal. The tales this branch has to tell...\n\nCome, let me show you.", objectives = "Speak with Orokai when you are ready to see what he learned from the Faintly Glowing Branch." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95026] = { title = "Blight No More", description = "Escapin' war don't mean we be safe here. Dem creatures to da east been plaguin' da area all dis time.\n\nMaybe you be ready for a challenge, eh?\n\nStrike 'em down. Ain't nobody gonna be missin' dem after all.", objectives = "Eliminate 3 Forgotten Soldiers and 12 Fleshflay Raveners." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95027] = { title = "Feathers in Flight", description = "We always need more arrows for hunting and fighting, and for feathers, we use the white feathers of the Hyjal owl. They're naturally fluffy and soft, but I stiffen them up with a mixture designed to make them perfect for fletching.\n\nYou can get feathers from the owls, of course, but they also leave behind feathers in their nests, which you can find all over to the south of here.\n\nBring back a bundle of feathers, all right?", objectives = "Head south into the valley and collect owl feathers from their nests." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95033] = { title = "On the Other Side", description = "If you be gettin' tired of dem wide open plains, my old friend Uzer'i always be lookin' for help. He always be twistin' dem magics, but little do most o' dem people know he be quite da hunter too.\n\nIf you's interested, you can find him all da way out at Camp Mojache in Feralas.\n\nTell him ol' Tan'jani sent ya.", objectives = "Tan'jani wants you to speak with Witch Doctor Uzer'i at Camp Mojache in Feralas." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95034] = { title = "The Debt", description = "I think you should know that it wasn't actually the Gnolls who attacked us on the road.\n\nWe were actually attacked by a giant, wolf-like creature that I now know as a \"worgen\". It dispatched our guards and came for me, but Banon threw himself in its path. I managed to get a spell off which startled the creature, causing it to flee, but Banon was already badly bitten. He insisted I leave him there but I refused.\n\nWe were limping back here when the gnolls found us. What came next was terrifying...", objectives = "Speak with Lumina Windsinger in the Sepulcher.", completion = "So now you understand. At the very end of his strength after being pierced by a dozen gnoll blades, he reared up to strike me. In that final moment we locked eyes, and I could tell he still knew who he was and that he recognized me. He knew what was happening but he had no control over himself. That was the worst part.\n\nIf such a thing is possible, I will see the creature that doomed him dead so that it can never visit this horror on another living thing. I swear it upon the sky above." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95036] = { title = "A Moon-Kissed Blade", description = "Trevan tells me that the worgen are a major threat to the citizens of Silverpine Forest. Despite their strength and resilience they can be killed, but there is one in particular that just doesn't ever seem to stay dead due to unknown magic.\n\nThat's the one that attacked us. He is known as Old Fire-Eye and he is the biggest and meanest of their kind. To put him down, we'll need a special kind of weapon.\n\nSpeak with Trevan and he will supply you with a list of what is needed to forge such a weapon.", objectives = "Speak with Trevan Rol in the Sepulcher and bring him the materials he requires.", progress = "Trust in the light to guide your blade. However, the light needs a good blade to guide.", completion = "Now that we've got the materials we need, we just need a smith to craft the blade for us. I think I know just such a smith." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95041] = { title = "Data Hoarders", description = "Before we fled Gnomeregan, I made a hard copy of my family's archives. Arcanotechnical field equations, Second War submarine hull designs, Grandma Quikswitch's chili recipe... our greatest accomplishments are in those files.\n\nIt wasn't until we reached Ironforge that I found a hole in my pack! Several punch cards are gone, and without them the data's too scrambled to recover.\n\nThe cards must be buried in the snow, somewhere outside Gnomeregan. Could you find them? I know it's a long shot...", objectives = "Collect 7 Gnomeregan Archival Data cards from around Gnomeregan, then deliver them to Jemma Quikswitch in Ironforge.", progress = "How is the data retrieval progressing?", completion = "These cards seem a bit damp... but I can work with this! Thank you, {name}!" }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95042] = { title = "Seeking the Kor Gem", description = "A Forsaken paladin... here in Ashenvale? Amusing. \n\nSo you seek a Kor Gem? Unsurprising as these are sometimes employed to empower magical weapons and implements by the paladins of the alliance. Why should a fallen paladin like you be any different?\n\nIf you truly desire one of the gems, then you must head north to the ruins known as Blackfathom Deeps. The naga who still use the gems are down below. Do not go alone, {class}.", objectives = "Bring a Kor Gem to Ulric Frostveil in Ashenvale.", progress = "Kor gems can be used for great acts of evil. Far be it from me to judge if your intentions are pure. It matters not to me.", completion = "You'll no doubt notice the corruption that permeates this gem. For your purposes, The magic needed to dispel the evil that the naga witches have infused into the gem is rather simple. A shame really, there's much one could learn from such powers.\n\nI don't suppose you'd be willing to abandon whatever quest caused you seek this gem, and sell it to me instead? It could prove valuable to my... academic pursuits." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95056] = { title = "Krol'dok No More!", description = "NYI", objectives = "Escort NAME to safety." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95059] = { title = "Frazzlespark's Crate", description = "Time for a special delivery.\n\nKnight Commander Demar Brant at Farholde is waiting for this. For some reason he always makes me say his full name. What an odd fella.\n\nAnywho, you can find him holed up in the keep southwest of here. Massive stone fortress. Ya can't miss it.", objectives = "Deliver Frazzlespark's Crate to Knight Commander Demar Brant in Farholde Keep." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95062] = { title = "Frazzlespark's Crate", description = "Time for a special delivery.\n\nOld Krom'rosh is waiting for this package over at Rog'mar just west of here.\n\nI suggest you get it to him quickly, but carefully. Why, you might ask? It's better to not ask questions.", objectives = "Deliver Frazzlespark's Crate to Krom'rosh at Rog'mar." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95063] = { title = "Bloodmaster's Ring", description = "Ok, listen up. You've showed quite a bit of prowess in the ring. You've managed to upset Chub'chob more than words can explain. Sure glad I ain't you right now.\n\nJust in case you was wonderin', I should remind you that your entry fee does not cover accidental death.\n\nIt's been great knowin' ya, but you're on your own from here on out, bub.\n\nBest of luck to ya.", objectives = "Defeat Chub'chob, Bloodmaster of Bolder'ok, in the Bloodmaster's Ring, then share the news of becoming the newly crowned champion of the Bloodmaster's Ring with Clugfist at Bolder'ok." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95064] = { title = "Preventative Measures", description = "The orcs have become an encroaching threat ever since their arrival. First, claiming the lands by the river and now their presence grows within the plains...\n\nI'll never understand their kind, nor do I care, truth be told, but I'll be damned if they think there's more ground to be taken.", objectives = "Kill 12 Rog'mar Trainees for Watcher Cornelius at Terral's Watch." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95065] = { title = "Fishin' Time", description = "What a view... Best an old man can ask for.\n\nThe fish sure are bitin' now, though I'm down to my last bait. I don't suppose you have any spare fishing supplies on you? Of course not, forgive me. I get so excited at the thought of casting another line it didn't dawn on me I may be one of the few carrying supplies everywhere I go.\n\nWould you be able to help refresh my stock? Catherine Leland has an assortment of fishing goods just west of the Trade District along the canals. Tell her old Gray sent you.", objectives = "Bring 1 Shiny Bauble and 3 Nightcrawlers to Gilbert Gray at the harbor in Stormwind.", progress = "Did you get the fishing supplies?", completion = "Great timing! Caught a big one with my last bait. Great day so far. They're really biting out here!\n\nTell you what, since you were kind enough to keep this old man in business how about a few fish for the road?" }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95066] = { title = "The Rog'mar Situation", description = "The message we've delivered is clear.\n\nReturn to Brant within the keep and show him the report. I'm certain he'll be pleased with our progress.", objectives = "Deliver the report to Demar Brant in Farholde Keep." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95107] = { title = "Deeproar Down", description = "One chief of the Deadwood, Deeproar, barks in the depths of their den. He was once of no burrow, and in a night of bad blood, he fell sway to their spells.\n\nNow, he feeds on their sour sap, with twice the cursed roar.\n\nGo. End his foul ways. Take his staff and bring it here, so I know he holds it no more.", objectives = "Kill Chieftain Deeproar and return his staff to Elder Pinespeaker in Barkskin Burrow." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95108] = { title = "Mystic Mix", description = "With far sight, we have seen their den. Deadwood brew dark rites in their pots. They feed this foul mix to their young, so bad roots take. Then they learn to fight with vile ways.\n\nGo, stop this spread. Slay the dark ones and smash their stew.", objectives = "Kill two Deadwood Death Mystics and destroy two Deadwood Cauldrons within Deadwood Den." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95111] = { title = "An Underrated Talent", description = "In Tarren Mill there is a weaponsmith known as Ott. By all accounts he is an unremarkable smith, selling simple blades to travelers. I purchased a sword from him myself, and when I took it to the undercity for maintenance some time later, the smiths there were surprised at its quality. They assumed it came from a well-known master smith, but no, it was just Ott.\n\nI'd like to give this orc a chance to do something truly special. Take the materials to Ott in Tarren Mill and offer him the commission.", objectives = "Speak with Ott and ask him to forge your blade.", progress = "Are you in need of a blade, {class}?", completion = "Interesting. I don't think anyone has ever asked me to actually carry out a custom commission for them. Mostly I just make humble, functional weapons in my own style. It's not much, but its honest work and I don't seek accolades or glory.\n\nI'm happy to try, but why would you seek me for this? There are plenty of smiths in the Undercity that will take on custom jobs like this." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95118] = { title = "Saltwater Savages", description = "Murlocs, murlocs, murlocs! That's all I ever hear about; from the sailors, the fishermen, even my own kids! Everyone's on my case about 'em! They're a nuisance, I admit, but I got a port to run here!\n\nHelp a guy out, would ya? Kill a couple 'a those things and I'll make it worth your time.", objectives = "Kill 8 Murloc Oracles and 8 Murloc Warriors along the Eastwind Shore." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95119] = { title = "Unfriendly Competition", description = "You know the Eastsea crew? Real unsavory bunch, and that's coming from the guy running a place called \"Powderfuse Port\".\n\nThey're destructive, bloodthirsty, and, worst of all, cutting into my bottom line. They steal cargo, and sink ships, both of which end up costing me the big bucks!\n\nWe gotta take down their whole operation, starting with the ones closest to here. You can find 'em along the beaches to the north.", objectives = "Kill 10 Eastsea Buccaneers and 10 Eastsea Musketeers along the Eastwind Shore, north of Powderfuse Port." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95120] = { title = "WANTED: Old Rot-Chum", description = "Sailors and swimmers beware! An especially aggressive murloc, nicknamed \"Old Rot-Chum\" by local fishermen, has been seen attacking rowboats and other small vessels in the waters to the south, near a collection of murloc-infested islands.\n\nA reward is being offered by Wharfmaster Whizzbuzz in exchange for proof of the creature's demise.", objectives = "Bring proof of Old Rot-Chum's demise to Wharfmaster Whizzbuzz." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95121] = { title = "A Taste of the Sea", description = "Welcome to Fimbo's cafe on the water! Today's menu is roasted boar, and roasted fish...same as every day...\n\nThis menu needs a shake up, badly. I've had my eye on a new seafood stew recipe, but I'm gonna need some fresh meat. A few murloc eyes and some crab meat oughta do.\n\nYou can find both along the beaches nearby. Can't beat some good ol' fashioned local ingredients!", objectives = "Gather 12 Murloc Eyes and 6 pieces of Sand Crawler Meat for Fimbo Greasemitz." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95122] = { title = "Unchecked Expansion", description = "Those Eastsea pirates you whacked, while dangerous, were just the small fries. They've got bigger, badder brothers in arms north of here. They ransacked Windstead--took all the plunder they could, then burned it to the ground.\n\nThey've gotta be stopped before their turf gets any farther inland. Thin out their ranks so that doesn't happen.", objectives = "Kill 8 Eastsea Raiders and 8 Eastsea Bombardiers for Wharfmaster Whizzbuzz." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95123] = { title = "A Blast Ye Scurvy Dogs!", description = "As much as I love seeing Eastsea heads roll, we also gotta take out their ships. Can't have 'em running off for reinforcements, now can we?\n\nI've got a plan for that, but we're gonna need some gunpowder. A LOT of it.\n\nThe pirates are probably storing some near the freshly-demolished Winstead to the north. See if you can get your hands on it. I'll fill you in on the rest later.", objectives = "Steal 5 Eastsea Powder Kegs for Wharfmaster Whizzbuzz." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95124] = { title = "Admiral Lamora", description = "Now it's time to go after the big man himself: Admiral Lamora. Obviously, I want him dead, but I need a little something extra from him too.\n\nSeeing how all his plundering has been costing me a fortune, I figure it's only right that I recoup some losses.\n\nLamora's on one of the Eastsea's boats northeast of here. Find out which and where on it he's keeping his loot. Bring me whatever he's got. If it's locked up, he's likely got the key on him.", objectives = "Slay Admiral Lamora, locate his stash of loot, and return it to Wharfmaster Whizzbuzz." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95125] = { title = "Ott's Masterwork", description = "These are some truly fine materials, {class}. You honor me by allowing me to forge this blade for you and I only hope that I can live up to your expectations.\n\nPlease, stand back so that I may begin the forging process.", objectives = "Watch as Ott forges your blade.", progress = "My blade will not fail you, {class}.", completion = "This blade is my finest work and I hope it serves you well in your travels. Thank you again for this opportunity.\n\nAka'Magosh, friend." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95126] = { title = "The Moonsilver Blade", description = "Here's the blade. You said that a paladin named Trevan sent you? Please extend my thanks to him for this opportunity when you next see him. Go with honor, friend.", objectives = "Bring Ott's Masterwork to Trevan Rol in Silverpine Forest.", progress = "Was Ott able to carry out the commission?", completion = "<Trevan takes the blade and inspects it carefully.> \n\nThis will do nicely, {name}. I knew that Ott had it in him to make something truly great.\n\nThe only thing left now is to kill that beast. Speak with Lumina when you are ready." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95140] = { title = "Old Fire-Eye", description = "I see that you have your weapon now, {class}. I pray that it will not fail you.\n\nThe locals tell me that Old Fire-Eye hunts in a large area south of here and you can generally find him near the gates to Gilneas. Find him, and use your new blade to end him. When it is done, return and you will have the gratitude of the Windshapers.", objectives = "Use the Moonsilver Blade to destroy Old Fire-Eye in Silverpine Forest.", progress = "Is it done? Is the beast slain?", completion = "Thank you, {name}. Banon may now rest in peace.\n\nIf you would be willing to allow it, I believe that I can impart some magic upon your freshly blooded blade to infuse it with a small measure of the magic of my people.\n\n\n\nIt is done. It's a small thing, and I could scarcely improve such a magnificent blade. Regardless, I will pray to the winds that it serves you well, {class}." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95141] = { title = "Report to Rog'mar", description = "Far to the northeast beyond Stonard lies an embattled land along the eastern coast known as the Riverglades.\n\nMany have sought to lay claim to these lands, but few have succeeded. There is one, however, whose experience battling our enemies proved enough to settle a small outpost known as Rog'mar. Through countless attacks, it still remains.\n\nAs ruthless as Krom'rosh may be, his will has served our allies greatly. If it's battle you seek, head northeast to seek out this old friend of ours.", objectives = "Report to Krom'rosh at the Rog'mar outpost in the Riverglades." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95143] = { title = "Finding Tan'jani", description = "I've been watching you, {name}. You handle yourself well out here. Perhaps you'd be interested in helping me locate my brother, Tan'jani.\n\nHe was always searching for something--for what I do not know. I received two messages since he left. The first from another traveler, letting me know he'd run into Tan'jani somewhere south of Loch Modan. The second was a bloodstained letter mentioning Riverglades and somewhere called Rog'mar, even further south. The rest was illegible.\n\nThink you can locate him for me?", objectives = "Find Tan'jani at Rog'mar in the Riverglades." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95144] = { title = "Overseas Delivery", description = "Hey, bub. Got a package that needs to go to an old friend of mine. Whatever you do--\n\nDO NOT OPEN THE PACKAGE!\n\nTake this--carefully--to Friz Frazzlespark across the seas over to our sister port in the Riverglades. And before you ask, no I would not suggest swimming. Didn't work out so well for the last guy. Oh, and don't tilt it, shake it, or make any sudden movements.\n\nI recommend heading east to Steamwheedle Port. The ship from there usually provides safe passage.\n\nBest of luck to ya!", objectives = "Deliver Fizzgrimble's Mysterious Crate to Friz Frazzlespark at Powderfuse Port in the Riverglades." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95147] = { title = "The Lost Scout", description = "You... where did you come from? You shouldn't be here!\n\n<Bolain struggles through the pain--bruised, battered, and a disease-ridden bite wound to his leg.>\n\nTake this to Dalton. Head north up the road and east where the plains open wider than this gash in my damn leg. I'd tell you to tell him he was right, but I won't give him that satisfaction... at least not until after I'm dead.\n\nI hate these damn hills!", objectives = "Deliver Bolain's message to Captain Dalton at Southern Watch." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95148] = { title = "Southern Watch Gnoll Report", description = "As much as I'd like to deliver the blood-soaked message to the knight commander himself, I'd also like to keep my post. I've cleaned it up a bit so it's less... well, bloody.\n\nGiven the recent gnoll uprisings, I'm afraid the task of delivering the news falls upon you.", objectives = "Deliver the Southern Watch Gnoll Report to the knight commander at Farholde Keep." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95156] = { title = "Stuff 'Em and Stick 'Em", description = "Our training dummies are starting to show significant wear and tear. If we don't fix them up soon I worry our recruits may be unprepared for battle.\n\nIf you hadn't seen it on your way in, there's a small farmstead just outside the keep run by a man by the name of Wheeler. He may have a few extra bushels of hay he'd be willing to part with.\n\nI'll see to it he's compensated if he's able to spare supplies for our efforts.", objectives = "Collect 3 Bundles of Hay for Ember at the training grounds." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95161] = { title = "Remember That I Love You", description = "If you're looking for Jeremy Heartweaver, your best bet is to talk to his newly adopted mother, Avette Fellwood out in Duskwood. Sweet woman. Likely needs another pair of hands for her work, but it beats staying in the orphanage.\n\nIf you see little Jeremy, do be sure to tell him we're all thinking of him, won't you?", objectives = "Deliver the Blood-Stained Letter to Avette Fellwood in Duskwood.", progress = "Yes? What do you need?", completion = "Oh no...\n\nIt's nice of you to bring this, but I don't think Jeremy is ready to see it. Matron Nightingale said my little Jeremy hasn't spoken since the attack on Lordaeron, and I don't intend to force him now. Showing him this will only cause him more pain.\n\nDon't look at me like that. I won't hide his past from him, but he needs time to heal. I'll give this to him when he's older. Thank you for stopping by, but I think it's time you should go." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95162] = { title = "Paletusk Harvesting", description = "With so little land not claimed by the humans or Twilight's Hammer, this ranch is one of our very few sources of food. Ogres aren't much in the way of farmers, but they love a good paletusk roast, and have agreed to let me stay so long as the meat keeps coming.\n\nAs our war advances, the demand for food is only ever increasing. Now I hardly have enough food to keep these ogres from looking at me like I'm their next meal.\n\nIf we want to have enough meat for Rog'mar, I'll need your help with the harvest.", objectives = "Gather 10 Chunks of Boar Meat for Na'zok near Bolder'ok." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95163] = { title = "Drive Them Back", description = "As you can see, there are more pigs strewn about the valley than there are in their pens. Gorgegut has been less than an ideal farmhand, but he keeps the humans away.\n\nSome of the little ones have escaped across the river. They're still too small to be harvested out in the field so we need to return them here. Take this stick and give them a good swat! That should send them scampering back to their pens.", objectives = "Return 10 Young Paletusks to Na'zok's farm near Bolder'ok." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95165] = { title = "See Ya, Scallywags!", description = "So, here's how we're gonna sink those ships. \n\nI can use that gunpowder you stole and make timed charges. All you've gotta do is hop on each of the Eastsea's boats, and plant one charge in the hull of each. Look for a spot near their cannons, that gunpowder'll make our explosives even more powerful. Once the charges are set, get outta there, and I'll hit the detonator!\n\nThe elegance of the plan is in its simplicity, don't ya think?", objectives = "Plant a remote explosive charge on each of the Eastsea's three boats." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95181] = { title = "Twilight Scouting Report", description = "Quiet down!\n\n<Azka snaps, adjusting her gaze in your direction.>\n\nI'll have your head before you give away my position to the cultists.\n\nWatch your step and keep a low tone when traveling through these hills. Otherwise I'll be sending a report to Krom'rosh that another of our own has been taken.\n\nNow take this and get out of here quickly... and quietly! Krom'rosh is waiting on this report. You can find him and the others at the outpost inland to the east.", objectives = "Deliver Azka's message to Krom'rosh at Rog'mar." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95183] = { title = "Step One: Rock", description = "You want ogre weapon? Me know no. You small. Can't hold good.\n\nYou bring Hamur more rocks, me make you tiny weapon. Good for tiny creature.\n\nFind good rocks for good weapon. Hamur has discerning eye. Not just any rock will do. Find rocks near river outside Bolder'ok.", objectives = "Gather 10 Good Rocks for Hamur in Bolder'ok." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95184] = { title = "The Sharpest of Blades", description = "The rigors of training for battle are one thing, but these trainees don't yet understand the difference between a training sword and the well-kept blade of a seasoned veteran.\n\nI think it's time we show our recruits how a sharpened blade can be the difference between victory and death.\n\nIf you can find us a few sharpening stones, we'll put them to good use. There are certain craftsmen known to study this trade. I'd suggest starting there.", objectives = "Bring 8 Solid Sharpening Stones to Ember Bladewhisper at the Farholde training grounds." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95189] = { title = "Crest of Lordaeron", description = "<A weathered crest depicting the mark of Lordaeron. With so few relics left after the kingdom's fall, someone in Stormwind would be very keen to get their hands on this.>", objectives = "Return the Crest of Lordaeron to Lady Dena Kennedy in Stormwind City.", progress = "Welcome to the gallery. Feel free to browse.", completion = "How in the world did you find this? It's in such remarkable condition... all things considered.\n\nThank you for restoring this piece of Alliance history, {class}. I'll have my best people get to work restoring this immediately." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95194] = { title = "Our Man in Theramore", description = "Greetings, {name}. There's a matter that SI:7 could use your help with. Our man on Theramore Isle tells us that Jaina Proudmoore's marines just brought in a man found washed up on the shore.\n\nNormally this wouldn't be of much interest to us but it seems that this man told the marines that he was none other than the king of Stormwind, Varian Wrynn. Go to Theramore and meet a dwarf named Sully at the inn. He's expecting you and will give you instructions when you arrive.\n\nFind out what's going on.", objectives = "Seek out the SI:7 agent stationed on Theramore Isle." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95195] = { title = "Bloodied Insignia", description = "<The old Alliance insignia appears to have belonged to a soldier of Lordaeron. These ruins are likely filled with similar medals that living relatives would be grateful to have returned to them.>", objectives = "Collect 10 Bloodied Insignias and take them to General Marcus Jonathan in Stormwind City.", progress = "You look as if you're carrying a heavy burden, {name}. What is it?", completion = "Your instincts to bring these to me were not unfounded. When Lordaeron fell to the scourge, many people fled to take refuge here in Stormwind. There are likely few who remain to claim these insignias themselves.\n\nYour duty to Stormwind is commended, {name}. I'll begin distributing these tokens to next of kin right away." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95196] = { title = "Watch Yer Back", description = "Listen up. I'm going to walk out that door behind you. Yer gonna wait until I'm good and gone, and then yer gonna meet me behind the graveyard outside o' town. Ensure yer not followed.", objectives = "Meet Sully McCleary in Dustwallow Marsh and learn more about your mission." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95198] = { title = "The Return of the King?", description = "Take this. It's a handy bit o' glamour that the mages back home put together to make a quick disguise. It'll make you look like a Kul Tiras Marine which should do nicely for this mission.\n\nSneak in to the tower and do yer best to listen for any mention of the man that washed up on the beach. I warn you though, do not get too close to Jaina. She will see right through this disguise. \n\nCome back and see me if you lose your disguise, I'll set you up with a new one.", objectives = "Use the SI:7 Disguise Kit to eavesdrop on Jaina and her inner circle at the Theramore Mage Tower." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95204] = { title = "Crest of Lordaeron", description = "<A weathered crest depicting the mark of Lordaeron. With so few relics left after the kingdom's fall, someone in the Undercity would be very keen to get their hands on this.>", objectives = "Bring the Crest of Lordaeron to Oran Snakewrithe in Undercity.", progress = "What have you got there, {class}? A tasty morsel?", completion = "<Oran bites the crest to ensure authenticity.>\n\nWell I'll be. A genuine relic of our home. Mostly intact, too. We need to be extra careful with this one.\n\nThank you for your aid in restoring our history, {class}. I'll see to it that we take good care of this." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95212] = { title = "Never Saddle on Quality", description = "We're getting ready to send a team of rams to reinforce the Alterac expedition, but we've run out of material to make their saddles.\n\nCollect pelts from the largest, fiercest leopards to the east and bring them to me. It's biting cold up there and our forces deserve nothing but the finest pelts to keep them warm!", objectives = "Collect 6 Pristine Leopard Pelts and deliver them to Amberstill Ranch.", progress = "You look chilly, {class}. How goes the hunt?", completion = "These pelts will make excellent saddles. You've done the Alliance proud, {class}!" }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95213] = { title = "Stolen Blasting Powder", description = "The keg is stamped:\n\nBLASTING POWDER - DANGER - DO NOT HANDLE - DANGER - QUARRYMASTER AUTHORIZATION ONLY - DANGER\n\nYou get a sinking feeling that the troggs shouldn't have this. It would be best to report this to the quarry sooner rather than later.", objectives = "Bring the Empty Powder Keg to Quarrymaster Thesten at Gol'Bolar Quarry.", progress = "What's that you've got?", completion = "<The {race} turns pale as he sees the empty keg.>\n\n...Where did you find this?" }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95214] = { title = "Stolen Blasting Powder", description = "This keg held enough powder to turn King Magni's throne room into an open air courtyard. We've got to get it back from the troggs before they work out how to ignite it.", objectives = "Recover 16 Stolen Blasting Powder from the troggs east of Gol'Bolar Quarry, then return to Quarrymaster Thesten.", progress = "I hope you've got good news for me?", completion = "That should be all the stolen powder. Thank you, {class}.\n\nPlease accept this reward, and... I'd appreciate if you didn't mention this little incident to anyone." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95216] = { title = "The New Plague", description = "Welcome to the most vital organ of the Undercity: The Apothecarium! Here we experiment on the most virulent of Azeroth's exotic specimens.\n\nYou've caught me in a good mood, so I will let you in on my latest investigation. It appears there is a particularly venomous arthropod stalking the ruins above our fair city. Its toxins are said to eat through even undead flesh. How exhilarating!\n\nI wish to validate these claims. Should you find yourself withering away from its bite, I should love a sample.", objectives = "Collect the Highly Toxic Strain from Witherfang in Ruins of Lordaeron for Theodore Griffs in Undercity.", progress = "Any fool can tell you the most potent transmission method will always be through the blood.\n\nI must see this strain for myself!", completion = "You killed it??\n\nHmmph. Lucky for you this should be enough ichor to reverse engineer its properties. You do not wish to be an enemy of the Royal Apothecary Society.\n\nGet out of my sight!" }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95217] = { title = "The Quarry's Smith", description = "So you're looking to learn the blacksmith's trade? Maybe we can help each other.\n\nThe supply shipment's late, and I need materials for some repairs around the camp. If you get me what I need, I'll teach you some of my techniques. Sound fair?", objectives = "Collect 12 Copper Bars and 4 Toughened Boar Hides and deliver them to Frast Dokner.", progress = "Don't slack off, {name}. Smithin' isn't for the lazy!", completion = "You're a resourceful one, {name}.\n\nNow listen up - I'm not going to repeat myself!" }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95218] = { title = "More of the Same", description = "The Light has forsaken me. A purpose served, and now everything... gone...\n\nIt's just a matter of time until the light turns to darkness.\n\nI fought against the demons and scourge forces with a ferocity I did not know the Light could produce... and yet, I sit here, talking to you, feeling... well, I can't quite put it into words. Some reclaim their purpose after loss, yet I struggle... After all, I am only who I am.\n\nNow, unless the commander has one last call to action, I await what comes next.", objectives = "Speak with Sefira Everbright." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95219] = { title = "From Port to Port", description = "Got another job for ya, kiddo. How do you feel about traveling the world?\n\nThis here is some of the finest port you ever laid eyes on. Trouble is, it's gotta go quite the distance to one of my customers all the way over to Feathermoon Stronghold in Feralas. When you've reached trees taller than you've ever seen before, you know you've reached the spot.\n\nOne of my guys packed it airtight but there's no telling what might set it off, so handle with care, okay bub?", objectives = "Deliver the Cask of Powderfuse Port to Mardrack Greenwell at Feathermoon Stronghold in Feralas." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95248] = { title = "To the Summit of Eternity", description = "You cut down so many of da Scourge dat we finally have a little safety. For dat, we be thankful.\n\nOne more thing. We know dat there are druids at da summit. Dey protect da great tree and da well.\n\nHow come dey never helped us?\n\nWe been here five years! Why did dey never even send a message to anyone about us? Let someone know dat we still here, we still alive!", objectives = "Travel to the Summit of Eternity and speak with the druids about the survivor village." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95250] = { title = "Abominable Creatures", description = "What do you want, {race}? Can't you see there is a war to be won?\n\nMy master has already charged into the fray and has ordered me to maintain my post. It has been quite some time, however.\n\nI doubt you'll survive ten minutes in combat, but if it keeps your simple mind busy, why don't you seek out the Grand Marshal. He is the tallest, most statuesque hero you've ever laid eyes on. You'll know him when you see him.", objectives = "Collect the Head of the Baron in the Ruins of Lordaeron and bring it back to Captain Truman." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95254] = { title = "WANTED: Trapclaw", description = "Calling all anglers!\n\nI'm in the market for some crab meat. Not just the usual shreds either, I'm talking whole claw. I've seen a big one crawling around under the docks, stealing bait and cutting lines.\n\nI'll pay a reward to anyone who brings me that thing's pincer. You'll also get a helping of the dish I whip up.\n\n-- Fimbo Greasemitz", objectives = "Bring Trapclaw's Pincer to Fimbo Greasemitz." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95260] = { title = "Terrors From the Deep", description = "The hide is painted with broad strokes of fish guts and squid ink. It appears to depict some kind of sea monster, rising up from the waves, with a long neck. What could this beast be?\n\nThe nearest port is Powderfuse Port. If this monster is real, and lurks these waters, a sailor there has surely seen it.", objectives = "Find someone at Powderfuse Port who can identify the monster from the painted hide." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95261] = { title = "It Takes Guts", description = "That monster...with the long neck, just like you said. I've seen 'im around those islands -- out on my boat. I tried <hic> tellin' folks, but ohh nooo, you can't <hic> believe ol' Argo. He's just some...some...drunkard fisherman! Makin' up stories!\n\nWe'll show 'em...soon as I get some bait...\n\nHey! Quit standin' around! I'm gonna need entrails, a LOT of 'em. Any beast from around here. The smellier <hic> the better. I'm also gonna need some Rotflesh mushrooms. Those grow in that cave by Windstead.", objectives = "Collect 15 Beast Entrails and 8 Rotflesh Mushrooms for Argo Brinewhistle." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95262] = { title = "The Secret Prison", description = "Can't say I've ever thought much about Alcaz. Near as I can tell, it's an abandoned outpost from the third war of little significance. Never heard nuthin' about a prison there. \n\nWell, there's nothing for it--we've got to get you in there and see what you can see, especially if there's a chance that the king is there.", objectives = "Enter Alcaz Prison and learn what became of the King of Stormwind." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95263] = { title = "Somber News", description = "<The King is dead--killed in an escape attempt just before the Naga attacked. This is devastating news and will shake Stormwind to its core. You need to return to Sully and tell him what you've learned as quickly as possible.>", objectives = "Return to Sully McCleary in Dustwallow Marsh." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95264] = { title = "Shaw Needs To Know", description = "Shaw needs to know as soon as possible. Head back to Stormwind and deliver the news. Please, I beg ye, tell no one else. This could be disastrous for Stormwind and it needs to be handled delicately.", objectives = "Bring the news to Matthias Shaw in Stormwind." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95267] = { title = "The Monster Surfaces", description = "The last part's <hic> easy...just take that big ball 'a guts, aaand chuck it in the water! Er...not here though...that'd be a disaster.\n\nGo to those <hic> murloc islands, where ya found the drawing. Look for fresh wreckage in the water. That's where you gotta throw the bait.\n\nSoon as that thing sticks its head up, chop it off! We'll make a decoration of it...for the boat!", objectives = "Use the Big Ball o' Bait to lure out the sea monster. Then, bring its head to Argo Brinewhistle." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95273] = { title = "Water of Hyjal", description = "Now that we know Deadwood don't foul the water outright with their presence, we can take this sample and cast our wards with sound will. We've heard there is a pool of the mountain's tears within their den.\n\nTravel with force and pour this water into the pool deep in Deadwood Den. \n\nReturn to us when you have learned what secrets the dark depths hold.", objectives = "Empty the Barkskin Purification Tonic provided by Fennar Mossmane in the water at the bottom of Deadwood Den." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95278] = { title = "It Is Time, Brother...", description = "The threat is greater than we thought. Rog'mar must be warned.\n\nDo not stop for anyone on your path.", objectives = "Deliver the missive to Krom'rosh at Rog'mar." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95283] = { title = "The Missing Kor'kron", description = "Lok-tar, {name}. I find myself in need of assistance with a serious matter. \n\nSome time ago we dispatched a contingent of Kor'kron Elite to Dustwallow Marsh on a special mission. The problem is, we are far past their scheduled check-in with no word from them.\n\nHead down to Brackenwall Village in Dustwallow Marsh and speak with an orc named Nazeer Bloodspike. No one is more knowledgeable about the state of Dustwallow than he. Find out what you can.", objectives = "Speak with Nazeer Bloodspike in Brackenwall Village." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95284] = { title = "The Elite of the Elite", description = "A small force of Kor'kron soldiers passed through here a few days ago. Never told me why they were here, and I didn't ask. They bought supplies, took a bit of rest, then moved on.\n\nThe Kor'kron are the elite of the elite and tougher than elekk hooves, but I can't help feeling that something went wrong.\n\nI did overhear one of them mention \"the island\", and there's an island called Alcaz just off the coast. It's a really nasty place. Get some friends and look into what befell these Kor'kron.", objectives = "Find the missing Kor'kron Elites." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95285] = { title = "Right Place, Wrong Time", description = "<Sergeant Ulka struggles to sit up to speak with you. You offer your hand in aid, but she merely swats it away.>\n\nAlright recruit... let's get you caught up.", objectives = "Speak with Sergeant Ulka to learn more about the situation on Alcaz Isle." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95288] = { title = "Smuggler's Paradise", description = "You look like you're in the habit of doing whatever other people tell ya. I like that in a lackey. With a little trainin' you could be a great asset. Let's put that to the test.\n\nRecently some of those Eastsea pirates made off with a shipment of MY stolen goods. That's bad sportsmanship. I stole them first!\n\nLesson one, lackey. Never backstab a backstabber. Go show them that they messed with the wrong goblin and take back my stuff. With force, preferably.", objectives = "Collect 8 Smuggled Goods for Friz Frazzlespark at Powderfuse Port." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95293] = { title = "Smuggler's Special", description = "Those goods you procured from the Eastsea pirates were supposed to be shipped directly to me. That means ol' Bentcoin thinks he can muscle in on my turf. Looks like he's fixin' to start a trade war. We, however, are civilized people.\n\nLesson two, lackey. We don't need to stoop to their level. Take this crate I made 'specially for the good captain. You'll find him on his ship along the Eastwind Shore. He deserves a reward for his shrewd negotiatin' tactics.", objectives = "Deliver The Friz Special to Captain Bentcoin in Eastwind Shore." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95294] = { title = "Smuggler's Bargain", description = "Friz sure knows how to get her point across. Well, you won't hear any objections from me. The Eastsea pirates won't interfere with her business. In exchange, maybe we can come to an arrangement. Pirating's a little difficult when you've got a scorned goblin sending marauding adventurers after you all day.\n\nRun along back to your master, {class}. Let Friz know there's a new captain in charge, and he foresees a profitable relationship in our future.", objectives = "Return to Friz Frazzlespark in Powderfuse Port." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95295] = { title = "I Know a Guy", description = "Ya did good with those pirates, lackey. But here's a lesson for ya you may want to remember. What some may call a pirate, others call a freebooter. And you can't spell freebooter without free booty. And there's no better place for free booty than Booty Bay!\n\n<Friz waits for your reply.>\n\nKeep up with me here, kid. I'm sayin' I need you to go to Booty Bay to meet with my contact. He gets goods from the local pirates there-- err, freebooters. Look, just go find Ruzzgot. He'll explain the rest.", objectives = "Speak to Friz's contact in Booty Bay." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95296] = { title = "Shipping and Handling", description = "Sounds like you're ready for your next lesson, champ. I got some negotiatin' of my own to do here in town, so I need you to run a few errands for me while I'm busy.\n\nAll I need you to do is take the next ship over there by the docks and deliver this crate to my associate in Steamwheedle Port.\n\nDon't gimme that look. It'll be plenty excitin', I'm sure. Gettin' a goblin to pay his dues is much harder than roughin' up the local riffraff, not to mention gettin' through customs. You'll figure it out.", objectives = "Speak with Wharfmaster Steamfizzle at Steamwheedle Port in Tanaris." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95309] = { title = "No Orc Left Behind", description = "Your orders are simple-- Go into the dungeons beneath the keep and find Commander Folkar. Free him if he lives, and learn what you can about what in the twisting nether is going on here.\n\nThere's an army waiting for you down there and you won't survive on your own. I hope you have allies... preferably strong ones.", objectives = "Enter the Alcaz Prison and find Commander Folkar." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95312] = { title = "Coming to Collect", description = "I don't have Friz's money. Well, I had her money, but I bet it all on ol' Slugjaw here in Fizbuz's arena in Gadgetzan.\n\nDon't gimme that look. It was a sound investment. I won big! I just haven't had a chance to collect my winnin's yet. If you're Friz's new errand <boy/girl>, why don't you go get it for me? I got a bad back, you know.\n\nHey, you don't want to go back to your boss empty handed, do ya? Gadgetzan is just west of here. You can't miss it.", objectives = "Speak with Fizbuz Mithril in Gadgetzan." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95314] = { title = "That Shadowvale Green Elixir", description = "Before the Scourge invasion, the reclusive village of Shadowvale was known for its Whispering Elixir. Distilled from herbs found only in Tyr's Fall, the elixir was sought by apothecaries, mystics, and poisoners alike even after being banned in the city.\n\nI've had requests from a number of buyers eager to get their hands on some elixir. Travel to the ruins of Shadowvale deep in the Whispering Forest to the west. I'm prepared to offer significant compensation if you can recover some bottles for me.", objectives = "Collect 8 Bottles of Whispering Elixir from Shadowvale, then return to Carolai Anise in Brill.", progress = "I trust you did not get lost?", completion = "You say there is evil in Shadowvale? I admit, I am not surprised. The forest folk were an odd lot, and they did not care for visitors. Some believe the Whispering Forest itself is cursed, and the elixir distilled from its roots carries that same curse...\n\n...but enough of superstition and rumors, {name}. Thank you for the elixirs. Here, take this as payment." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95315] = { title = "The Riverglades Report", description = "Word from one of our scouts suggests a large force of enemies amassing to the far, far south, well beyond the Wetlands.\n\nEven more curious is there appears to be an alliance settlement out there. Farholde? The name sounds familiar.\n\nLet's not wait on this. Best to begin the conversation before it's too late. We're dealing with enough here as it is.\n\nTake this correspondence and deliver it to whoever claims to be the leader of this detachment.", objectives = "Deliver Captain Nials' Correspondence to Demar Brant at Farholde Keep along the southeastern coast in the Riverglades." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95316] = { title = "The Experimental Method", description = "Alright dirtwalker, you may have noticed the combination of pinecones and fel-infused slime is quite disgusting, if you ask me. It is, however, also very dangerous-- which is just what we need!\n\nTake these pinecones and carefully--I repeat, carefully--make your way to the nearby warlock encampment. Once there, use these items to wreak havoc upon their precious workstations.\n\nI am sure the results will be amusing for you to watch firsthand! This should certainly slow them down.", objectives = "Use the pinecones to destroy the Ashen Reign workstations." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95317] = { title = "Notation, Notation, Notation", description = "Listen, {class}. There have been some awfully noisy visitors just up the mountain. They are tainting the land with their foul demon magic and experimenting with piles of ash. It's high time we investigate.\n\nBy we, I mean you.\n\nI want you to poke around and investigate their camp! See if you can bring me some notes on what our mysterious fel 'friends' have been up to. Surely with egos that large they've written something we can utilize. Perhaps they are carrying something on their person?", objectives = "Find 12 Fel Ash Experimentation Notes." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95318] = { title = "Taste of Ash", description = "So in order to really disrupt operations here and get me out of this cage, we're going to have to kill four very powerful mortals. This cage has demonic wards on it that won't be dispelled until all four are dead, and that key can't be used until the wards are down.\n\nLook, you seem like |5{race} that can hold your own but I'm going to need a bit more convincing that you can actually take on these stupid warlocks before I give you any good info.\n\nLike killing a ton of these warlocks for starters. Easy, no?", objectives = "Slay 12 Ashen Acolytes." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95319] = { title = "Crystalline Collection", description = "Listen, I know you can smell the fel blood pools behind me and I'm sure you've seen the crystals that grow out of them. These crystals have special properties from the ashes of Archimonde that rain down on this side of the hill.\n\nSomething about how they are formed makes them especially good at draining fel energies, which is a big problem for someone like me, but they can still have their uses.\n\nI want you to gather some for me. Try and get a few kinds. I'll know what I need when I see it.", objectives = "Gather 1 Fel-Slime Crystals and 8 Pristine Fel-Slime Crystal." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95320] = { title = "A Curious Question", description = "There is a caged demon just up the road near the entrance of the demon caster encampment that has been making a great deal of fuss.\n\nAll this ranting and raving about imprisonment and freedom. Something about scorching bones and revenge?\n\n<The crow leans in and gives you a mischievous look. As if to emphasize, she then dangles an iron key in one of her talons.>\n\nLet's see if we can't make a deal with our little 'friend' and see what he knows about these nasty demon casters.", objectives = "Find the imprisoned demon." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95321] = { title = "Tazzik's Dues", description = "Tazzik sent you to collect his winnings? That's a joke, right? His slackjaw champion didn't even last two minutes in the arena! That loser didn't earn a single copper.\n\nIt's none of my business, pal, but if I were you I'd skedaddle back to Steamwheedle Port. While you're standin' here talkin' to me, that little rat Tazzik is probably tryin' to hop the next ship outta here.", objectives = "Confront Tazzik in Steamwheedle Port in Tanaris." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95322] = { title = "Get the Goods", description = "Your timin' couldn't be better, friend. I was just on my way to collect my shipment from the Bloodsail Buccaneers. They're good friends of mine. Always happy to supply anything Friz is willin' to pay for.\n\nBut, ahem, just in case, it couldn't hurt for you to be my liaison. A good caravaneer knows it doesn't hurt to show off a little muscle. Just as a deterrent, of course.\n\nThey said they left my stuff in a chest on the hill outside of town for safekeepin'. Why don't you take a look for me, eh?", objectives = "Find the Bloodsail Trunk outside of Booty Bay in Stranglethorn Vale." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95325] = { title = "We've Been Robbed!", description = "I already spent good coin on that crate. We ain't just going to let them have it!\n\nYou want your shipment? Go to the Venture Co's camp up north and find out who's responsible for this backstabbin'! This ain't about money anymore, {name}. This is about justice! And maybe a little about the money.", objectives = "Find the Venture Co. Ledger in the Venture Co. Camp near Lake Nezferiti in Stranglethorn." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95326] = { title = "The Big Payback", description = "<The ledger contains a log of each of Ruzzgot's deliveries. The final note marks the heist a success and Ruzzgot's valuables collected by a nearby Venture Co. agent. The goods must still be with him.>", objectives = "Kill the Venture Co. Agent and take back Ruzzgot's Shipment for him in Booty Bay." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95327] = { title = "All's Well That Ends Well", description = "Looks like a deal's a deal. The Venture Co. got their comeuppance, Friz gets her loot, and everybody's happy. Overall a pretty smooth transaction if I do say so myself.\n\nNow scram, I got another shipment comin' in soon from some Southsea Pirates.", objectives = "Return to Friz Frazzlespark at Powderfuse Port in the Riverglades." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95328] = { title = "Whispering Horror Residue", description = "Against your better judgement you scrape up and collect the squirming remains of the beast. Someone in Undercity might have a use for them.", objectives = "Deliver Whispering Horror Residue to Father Lankester in the War Quarter of Undercity.", progress = "Do you have something for me, {class}?", completion = "What an interesting specimen. From underneath the Whispering Forest, you say? It's no secret that foul place is touched by the void.\n\nI welcome the opportunity to explore the mysteries of shadow, {class}. Allow me to offer you payment for what you've found." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95329] = { title = "Out in the Field", description = "There is a watch tower overlooking the plains to the north. It serves as an observation point to track any motion of the Horde's forces.\n\nThe watcher stationed there is named Cornelius. Speak to him and get a status report. He is all alone out there, so I like to check on him with some regularity. Fair warning, he can be a bit...taciturn. It's why he was assigned such a remote post in the first place.", objectives = "Go to Terral's Watch to get a status report from Watcher Cornelius." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95330] = { title = "Love Thy Neighbor", description = "My husband and I have a farm north of here. I come to Farholde after each harvest to sell what we grow. In good seasons, I like to set aside whatever we don't sell to give to folks who need a little pick-me-up. Gotta take care of your neighbors, I say.\n\nThere's a logging camp north of our farm, right on the river. I'm sure those boys could use some fruits and vegetables to give 'em some variety in their diet.\n\nIf you're heading that way, could you give this to the foreman there? Name's Halligan Turner.", objectives = "Deliver Cassandra's surplus farm goods to Halligan Turner at Turner's Logging Camp." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95331] = { title = "REUSE ME", description = "", objectives = "" }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95349] = { title = "The Earthen Ring", description = "The recent events with the cult have delayed my plans to travel to Azeroth and I must remain here in Valanaar for a time. You and a handful of other Windshapers will be our vanguard instead. Alaana Stormwalker will be waiting to receive our Windshapers upon arrival in Mulgore, and I'd encourage you to explore Azeroth while we finish our business here. We will join you soon.\n\nWhen you are ready, please proceed to the dock just outside this lodge and board the skycutter ship there. \n\nBanu-Alah, {name}.", objectives = "Take the skycutter ship from Zephras Isle to Mulgore and speak with Alaana Stormwalker when you arrive.", completion = "More adventurers from Zephras, I see. Wonderful. The winds surely favor us! It's going to take us some time to get ourselves established here, so you may want to take some time to explore this new land.\n\nAzeroth is an exciting new world, but it's also a dangerous world. You'd do well to prepare yourself for this new adventure by familiarizing yourself with the lands nearby." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95350] = { title = "Welcome to Azeroth", description = "It's a big world down here, and our new allies are the key to our survival.\n\nThe Earthen Ring is a member of the \"Horde\", a proud collection of like-minded peoples. The nearby city of Thunder Bluff is a part of the Horde, and further to the east lies the capital of Orgrimmar.\n\nSeek out the flight master in the center of Thunder Bluff. They will fly you to Orgrimmar where you will make contact with the Horde warchief--Thrall, on behalf of the Windshapers. Winds guide you, {name}.", objectives = "Travel to Orgrimmar and speak with Thrall in the Valley of Wisdom.", completion = "Lok-tar, {class}. I am Thrall, Warchief of the Horde.\n\nAn Earthen Ring messenger told me to expect members of the Windshapers, and here you are. I'd not have expected to see a high elf standing before me here in Orgrimmar, but the Horde will welcome you as our guest all the same.\n\nYou have my blessing to travel through Horde lands. Go with honor, Windshaper." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95378] = { title = "The Hydra's Head", description = "It is time to cut off the heads of this hydra, if you catch my meaning.\n\nThere are three leaders who need to be killed in order to slow the operations here. Conveniently, they also need to be slain to remove the wards on my cage.\n\nTyaeha can be found in the House of Diseases by the creepy tree. Dazka is in the Alchemist ward with all the potions, and that fool Frezzlie is undoubtedly next to the slime pits along the northern ridge of the encampment.\n\nGo slay them and bring me their bones!", objectives = "Retrieve the bones of Frezzlie Popwhiz, Tyaeha Darkoath and Dazka Shadowsleep." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95379] = { title = "A Revenge So Sweet", description = "Brashann Grimdark, Master of Vessels.\n\n<Felflick's mouth curls into a snarl.>\n\nHe was the one to subjugate me at the summit. HE is the reason I am here in the first place.\n\nHis work with these fel-ash crystals are the backbone of this operation. He's been obsessively experimenting with anchoring souls in these crystals and his work has not gone unnoticed by those Blackthorne creeps.\n\nUse this pristine crystal to drain his power, then put an end to him and bring me his soulstone.", objectives = "Slay Brashann Grimdark and search his body for his soulstone." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95380] = { title = "A Prolific Source", description = "Listen here, {class}. It seems we're in quite the sticky situation. I knew those blasted demon casters were up to no good, but this is far worse than I had expected.\n\nGood thing I have an idea!\n\nFor this to work I will need fel-slime from the surrounding slime creatures that can be found in the fel blood pools behind me. Not the bones or bits, just the slime! Make sure you wipe your hands after handling it. It seems to be corrosive.\n\nNot to fear, I'm sure you'll find a way to bring it back to me.", objectives = "Gather 8 Fel-Slime Ooze." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95383] = { title = "Shipping and Handling", description = "<Wharfmaster Steamfizzle inspects the coin you offered him.>\n\nWhoa-ho! Ol' Friz sure is training the new generation right. Apologies for the delay, <sir/ma'am>. You're here to deliver a crate to someone in town, right? I don't know anythin' about that, but if I did, I'd go talk with Tazzik on the dock. He seems to be interested in things like that.\n\nBut be quick about it though, yeah? Don't need folks gettin' the wrong idea, ya know.", objectives = "Deliver Friz's Secret Stash to Tazzik in Steamwheedle Port." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95384] = { title = "Partial Mystical Notes", description = "<The strange symbols on the magical scroll confound you. Though you do not speak the language recorded, you don't sense any particularly volatile forces within. Perhaps a collector of odd magics would find some use for the scroll.>", objectives = "Bring the partial scroll to Dudd Fizzlescroll in Booty Bay." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95385] = { title = "Torn Mystical Scroll", description = "<Faint magic emanates from the scrap of scroll. The language is unfamiliar, though you intuit that it is not dangerous. Most would find the parchment useless, but there may be a unique collector that may find some use out of it.>", objectives = "Bring the partial scroll to Dudd Fizzlescroll in Booty Bay." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95417] = { title = "The Purple Ones", description = "Clubtoe see friends go. Some no come back. Some come back purple. Dat weird. Purple ones no act like friends no more.\n\nWhere others go? Why they no come back? Make Clubtoe think.\n\nYou hit hard. Maybe you go find friends in cave? Maybe you turn purple. Dat weird too.", objectives = "Find missing ogres in the caves beneath Sunnyglade for Clubtoe." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95418] = { title = "Spread the Word", description = "Me done with Twilight. Clubtoe free ogre now.\n\nMe go find Clugfist. He biggestest ogre Clubtoe ever see. He leave Twilight. Take many friends with him. It Clubtoe's turn. Me join free ogres. They go to the hills. Clubtoe miss hills. No more smashing rocks. Maybe you come sometime?\n\nMe stay here till coast is clear. You take Chogg'Zac's heads back to friends. Well. Maybe one head. Me get one too. Fair trade.", objectives = "Deliver the head of Chogg to Tran'gul in Rog'mar." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95420] = { title = "Land of Giants", description = "Clearly these wayward ogres are no friends to the Twilight's Hammer. We orcs have an honored history fighting alongside ogres, and it may be time to call upon those old alliances again. And this head may be the key.\n\nThere have been reports of ogre activity in the hills far to the north. If this Clubtoe is to be believed, that must be where this clan calls home. Go to their stronghold and offer this trophy as a token of our friendship. With luck, they will listen to your proposal before they step on you.", objectives = "Deliver Chogg's head to the ogre city to the north." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95424] = { title = "Might Makes Right", description = "Here ogres value strength and blood.\n\nWeak ones leave Bolder'ok. Go back to Twilight's Hammer.\n\nYou no big. Maybe you strong. Show Clugfist strength and smash weak ogres. If tiny creature can.", objectives = "Kill 7 Twilight Maulers and 7 Twilight Firecallers for Clugfist in Bolder'ok." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95425] = { title = "Unworthy Champion", description = "Klunk once Clugfist's greatest champion. Him strong. Me give Klunk mighty weapon.\n\nBut Clugfist wrong. Klunk weak like others. He leave Bolder'ok. Return to Twilight's Hammer. Take ogres with him to cave east to water. Take mighty weapon with him!\n\nThat Clugfist weapon! Bash Klunk's skull and take back Skullbasher. He nobody's champion!", objectives = "Collect Skullthumper from Klunk for Clugfist in Bolder'ok." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95426] = { title = "Rog'mar Supplies", description = "Supply delivery to this area is no easy feat. All sorts of unscrupulous characters surround us in all directions, each seeking their own piece of the pie.\n\nNow, with that said, perhaps this is an opportunity to slow Rog'mar's growth. What do you say to throwing a little wrench in our orc friends' plans?\n\nHead north of Rog'mar to their training grounds and steal their supply shipments. The recovery time alone ensures our forces remain battle ready while theirs... well, you see where this is going.", objectives = "Retrieve 8 Horde Supply Shipment from the training camps north of Rog'mar." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95427] = { title = "Twilight No More!", description = "Clubtoe friends... dead? Why?\n\nThis Chogg'Zac fault! Dey say they make ogres strong! They lie!!\n\nNo more smashing rocks! Tiny creature help Clubtoe smash Chogg'zac stupid heads instead!", objectives = "Kill Chogg'Zac in the Sunnyglade cave and collect their heads for Clubtoe." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95428] = { title = "Clugfist's Decree", description = "Little {race} smash Twilight good. Maybe your Horde stronger than Clugfist think.\n\nYou free to stay in Bolder'ok. For now.\n\nTell other tinies we spill blood again soon.", objectives = "Report to Krom'rosh in Rog'mar." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95431] = { title = "Rumblings of Discontent", description = "As I've shadowed our enemy's movements, I have discovered a weakness among their ranks. Ogre dissidents have begun to rebel, seeking the same freedom as their Bolder'ok kin. Word of your deeds has spread. We must exploit this.\n\nI spied a Bolder'ok warrior heading to the caves west of here in search of his brothers and sisters. Find him, and join his efforts to rally his people.", objectives = "Look for the Bolder'ok ogre in the nearby cave." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95432] = { title = "Rise Up!", description = "When Crag'rog hear {race}-ling free ogres, Crag'og want free ogres too.\n\nWith tiny {class} here, we smash Twilight together. Break them bones. Make them scream. Free ogres! Then be home in time for stew.", objectives = "Recruit 5 Ogre Miners." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95433] = { title = "Death to the Executioner", description = "When Clugfist leave Twilight, one ogre stand in way. Morg.\n\nMorg massive ogre. Nearly as massive as Clugfist. But not massivest. He need tinies to protect him. Clugfist never got fair fight. Now WE no fight fair.\n\nFind Morg. Bring many tinies with you. Kill him. Take mace back to Clugfist. Then Twilight know they challenge us no more!", objectives = "Collect the Executioner's Mace from Executioner Morg in the Twilight Shroud for Clugfist in Bolder'ok." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95454] = { title = "The Honor of the Kor'kron", description = "My good axe arm is broken and most of my elites are dead. The honor of the Kor'kron rests with you now.\n\nWe were sent here to extract a prisoner, but not just any prisoner... We are here for the King of Stormwind, Varian Wrynn. We intercepted information that he was being held here and our Warchief commanded us to bring him back to Orgrimmar alive. The presence of black dragons... complicates things.\n\nI need you to press on and find Wrynn. I will wait for you here while you search for him.", objectives = "Look for King Varian Wrynn in Alcaz Prison." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95472] = { title = "Consolation Prize", description = "I'm tellin' ya, I can't pay Friz back! I got nothin' left but the shirt off my back!\n\nWhy are you lookin' at me like that...", objectives = "Bring Tazzik's Sweaty Shirt to Friz Frazzlespark in Powderfuse Port." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95483] = { title = "Thrall Needs to Know", description = "Thrall needs to know what happened here. I will meet up with Ulka and see to it that he is fit to travel before returning to Orgrimmar, so I am trusting you to bring this information to the warchief in my stead.\n\nGo now, soldier of the Horde. Tell our warchief what fate befell Varian Wrynn.", objectives = "Bring word of Varian Wrynn's fate to Thrall in Orgrimmar." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95494] = { title = "Bruised Pride and Lion Hides", description = "I need someone with a strong sword arm and some extra time on their hands to help me gather some lion hides. It stings my pride to ask a stranger for this aid, but I took an injury to my leg recently. Until I heal, I'm in no shape to go hunting myself but I have obligations to keep.\n\nThe big ones in this area generally have the best hides, so start with those first.", objectives = "Collect 6 Savannah Lion Hides from the Savannah Matriarchs and Savannah Patriarchs in the Barrens.", progress = "How goes the hunt?", completion = "Yes, these look like they will do nicely. I have an arrangement with a local tanner to deliver these raw hides in exchange for various finished leather goods that I use as part of my trade. \n\nI've never come up short on my end of the arrangement, and even with my injury I do not intend to start now." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95495] = { title = "The Hermit Tanner", description = "These hides are bound for a tanner who I often trade with. He is something of a hermit and he lives alone on the top of the ridge behind me. Climbing up a steep hillside isn't something I can manage easily right now so I'd be in your debt if you could make this delivery for me.\n\nOh, and about this tanner's... appearance. You need not be alarmed. In spite of his looks, he is no threat. I swear this is true.", objectives = "Bring the Bundle of Hides to the hermit on the ridge overlooking the Dry Hills in the Barrens.", progress = "Greetings, {class}. What brings you up to my property today?", completion = "Vrang sent you then? Very well. I appreciate you delivering these hides to me. It's unfortunate that Vrang couldn't make the journey himself. There is a matter I wish to speak with him about." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95507] = { title = "Vrang's Game", description = "While you are out there, it would be of great help to me if you could check on my traps for me. I've got them strewn all over the valley.\n\nBring back any small game that I've caught. Keep your eye out for the other wildlife, though. This area can be dangerous if you aren't paying attention.", objectives = "Collect 8 Trapped Game from traps found in Sprung Traps in the Barrens.", progress = "<Vrang grunts at you as you approach.>", completion = "Thank you for your aid, {class}. I was starting to wonder if I'd have to go to bed hungry tonight because this cursed wound on my leg." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95508] = { title = "Unwelcome Guests", description = "Yes, I used to be a member of the Kul Tiras navy. After Lord Admiral took Theramore and started his campaign in Durotar, I had... \"objections\" to his methods. Particularly the methods involving executing civilians.\n\nThere's more to the story but... wait... what's that?\n\nThere's a group of men coming up the ridge!", objectives = "Help Walton survive the encounter with Terry Longdrink and the Kul Tiras marines.", completion = "Well, looks like we are all alive. I... knew that someday that would catch up to me. I'm in your debt for your help here today.\n\nPlease, take this. It's not much, but it's the least I can do.\n\nSafe travels, {class}." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95511] = { title = "Your First Feline Friend", description = "Greetings, friend! I see today is a big day indeed; today you will bond with your first saber.\n\nAs you may or may not know these sabers are fiercely intelligent and extremely loyal to their bonded rider. You won't find a more noble and steadfast companion. As such, you have an important choice to make. You and your saber will traverse the world together, so choose wisely! Fear not, whatever choice you make will be the correct one.\n\nGo, examine the sabers and return to me when you have made your choice.", objectives = "Inspect the riding sabers to choose your first mount." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95534] = { title = "Strahnbrad Mystery", description = "<The note is singed in places, but is still readable.>\n\nRumor has it those old bellows have a mind of their own, springing to life when no one is watching. I don't care if it's a ghost story, you'd better get to the bottom of it before I return.\n\nThere's great power in Strahnbrad, I know it.\n\n< The rest of the note is singed and torn, as if burnt by fire magic. >", objectives = "Solve the mystery of Strahnbrad and report your findings in town in Hillsbrad." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95555] = { title = "Corrupted Nature", description = "<A sickly energy emanates from the staff, wholly warping the natural flow of magic around you. Despite the disturbance, you cannot seem to put it down. Distantly, you notice a similar, equally foul energy resonating, drawing you in. Perhaps you can find the source of this cursed item.>", objectives = "Find the source of corruption from the staff in Feralas." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95561] = { title = "Apple of My Eye", description = "<The loud cries of baby Dawnbright echo through Farholde Keep. Tessa looks at you with a tired smile.>\n\nOh, hello there adventurer. Sorry for the noise. Little Emma here seems to be quite fussy today, but I'm not sure why. Maybe some food will help.\n\nDo you think you could help me find something for her to eat? My husband stepped out to get some supplies so my hands are a little too full to get them myself. If you could find a few apples around here I could make a lovely mash for her.", objectives = "Collect 6 Fresh Apples for Tessa Dawnbright in Farholde Keep." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95562] = { title = "Cut Off the Heads", description = "I have a confession to make. Lady Amberhall did send me to collect those samples, but in truth I volunteered. Sunnyglade was my home before the war took it from me, and I could not rest knowing monsters still taint it. Be it horde or Twilight.\n\nThere is no victory here by learning from them. There's nothing to learn. They're beasts, plain and simple, and should be put down like beasts.\n\nWe must slay their master at the bottom of this cave and bring an end to this. Surely my mistress will understand.", objectives = "Kill Chogg'Zac in the caves beneath Sunnyglade and retrieve their heads for Apprentice Claire." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95568] = { title = "Seeds for a New Season", description = "You have arrived on Mount Hyjal at a time of changes, stranger.\n\nYou may have seen that the landscape is scarred by the old war and tainted by fel energies. For Hyjal to survive, nature must bloom again.\n\nIf you are willing to help me gather seeds from some of the untainted plants, I would be grateful. Many flowers grow in the wild lands east of here. Look for small red or yellow flowers.", objectives = "Collect 10 Untainted Seeds for Ketharas." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95569] = { title = "Hope for Hatchlings", description = "The owls are under threat by the fel corruption that afflicts the mountainside, and the creatures poisoned and enraged by those energies. Many owls have abandoned their nests for safer places higher up the mountain. Others have fallen in defense of their young.\n\nFor the owls to have a future, their eggs must be protected and their fledglings nurtured. Bring the abandoned eggs to me. You may find eggs in abandoned nests at the base of trees north and east of here.", objectives = "Rescue 12 Hyjal Owl Eggs and bring them to Ketharas." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95599] = { title = "The Old Key", description = "<The key is covered in a thick layer of rust, suggesting that the key has been underwater for a significant amount of time.\n\nThere must be a matching lock somewhere nearby to use it on but you'll have to search for it. Perhaps the pool of water to the southwest of this camp might be a good place to start?>", objectives = "Find the old chest that the key belongs to nearby in Feralas." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95601] = { title = "The Purple Ones", description = "<This dead ogre must be one of the friends Clubtoe was looking for. The Twilight's Hammer seem to be conducting rituals on their members, empowering some and killing more.\n\nThese ritualists and their monstrosities must be stopped before they spread.>", objectives = "Kill 5 Empowered Brutes and 10 Twilight Ritualists then return to Clubtoe in Sunnyglade." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95602] = { title = "Sickening Lights", description = "Me hate smashing rock. All day me smash. Chogg'Zac say so. He big boss. Say we smash tinies, but now we work for tinies. That stupid.\n\nWhy smash rock? Me no know. Find shiny light in rocks. Chogg'Zac like shiny, me guess. Are you here for shiny light too? Others won't like that. They really like light. They draw pictures with it.\n\nClubtoe not get it. Light make Clubtoe feel sick. Me hate light. Me want SMASH shiny pictures! But Chogg'Zac be mad. Squish Clubtoe. That bad. But someone should.", objectives = "Destroy 5 Twilight Ritual Circles found throughout the caves underneath Sunnyglade." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95603] = { title = "Bats in the Belfry", description = "Since brother Lowley and I began serving Farholde in a more secular capacity, the church here has fallen into disuse. I'd like to think that once the fighting is over, we will be able to bring the Light back to this place. Although, I fear that may not be for a long while...\n\nStill, we need to keep the church in working order, in the hope that day will come.\n\nTo that end, a colony of bats has taken to roosting in the upper stories of the church. It would be a great help if you could remove them.", objectives = "Kill 5 Roosting Duskbats in the Farholde Cathedral for Sister Rowland." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95611] = { title = "Rites of Respect", description = "One cannot take without giving in return. This is the cycle of life.\n\nYou have done well, {name}. Thanks to your efforts, the wildlife on the mountain will continue to thrive.\n\nNow, it is time we show our respect for these lands by offering the unused remains back to the ground.\n\nTake this bundle and visit the shrine to the west. You shall recognize it as a simple pair of standing stones. Return to me once the ritual is complete.", objectives = "Bury the remains at Ketharas' shrine." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95613] = { title = "Keeping the Light On", description = "While we no longer hold service at the church, I feel it important to keep the candles lit on the graves of our fallen in the church's crypt. To me, keeping the candle's flame alive is a symbol that they are not forgotten and their sacrifices were not in vain.\n\nIf you would, bring me candles so that I might continue this ritual. It would mean a great deal to me.\n\nIf you're not sure where to find them, speak with Marla in the house just outside of the church. She's a friend and may have some to spare.", objectives = "Bring 5 Holy Candles to Sister Rowland in Farholde Keep." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95615] = { title = "In Memoriam", description = "If you don't mind, I'd like you to do the honor of lighting these memorial candles. Go to the cemetery just outside and place a fresh candle wherever you see one that's gone out.\n\nSuch a task is a far cry from the excitement of your other adventures, I'm sure. Think of this as an opportunity for service and reflection--a quiet moment to acknowledge those who left this world before us, so that we might carry on and make it a better place.", objectives = "Place 1 Memorial Candles on graves in the chapel graveyard for Sister Rowland at Farholde Keep." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95621] = { title = "Trouble in the Valley", description = "This morning I spotted a group of humans searching for something in the valley below. I managed to use my rifle's scope for a better look, and it was clear that they were soldiers sporting the livery of Kul Tiras. \n\nIf you'd be willing to take work from me, travel to where these soldiers made camp near the wrecked caravan to the south. Kill any you find and try to learn why they are here.", objectives = "Travel to the wrecked caravan and learn more about why the Kul Tirans are here.", progress = "The remnants of Daelin Proudmoore's fleet who still fly his banner are just as rotten and barbaric as the admiral himself was before he died.\n\nI don't know why they are so far from Tiragarde, but it can't be good.", completion = "So they are looking for a deserter... Well, it seems that the past has finally caught up to me." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95642] = { title = "Abominable Magics", description = "You there! Thank the light you've come. Did Amberhall send you to find me?\n\nNo? Figures as much. Ashe Amberhall sent me down here to investigate the Twilight's Hammer. As you can see, they are digging for something within the Riverglades, but I need a sample of their witchcraft to figure out what.\n\nIt's imperative Farholde gets those samples. Please, {class}. Take this catalyst. It's enchanted to absorb the powers of the cult. Runes, cultists, it doesn't matter. Just hold it aloft and it will do the rest.", objectives = "Absorb 25 samples into the Crystal Catalyst from Twilight's Hammer cultists and Twilight Ritual Circles in the cave underneath Sunnyglade for Apprentice Claire." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95643] = { title = "Indiscriminate Purge", description = "As Lady Amberhall's apprentice in the dark arts, I may not look it but I'm usually quite capable of handling things on my own. I did not, however, anticipate an entire cave of void-infused ogres.\n\nIf you managed to get all the way down here without being captured, you must be powerful yourself. I was not so lucky with those ogres and their masters roaming about. Do the world a favor and kill the hideous beasts. Nothing good comes from a fanatic with a purpose, empowered or otherwise.", objectives = "Kill 5 Twilight Ritualists and 5 Empowered Brutes within the caves underneath Sunnyglade." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95646] = { title = "Horrors in the Highland", description = "These brackish wetlands hold a greater well of unsalted southern waters. It pains me, yet within my roots I sense a corruption seeping through that mountain gully.\n\nThe creatures, like those in our lowlands, react more bitterly to the taint. Lacking the sea's hardening salt since life's dawn, they have little strength against such evil.\n\nGo to those highlands, and bring me the Highland Horror's root core.", objectives = "Kill a Highland Horror within Excavation Sites and bring its root core to Rethiel the Greenwarden in the Wetlands." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95647] = { title = "Lost in the Thicket Things", description = "My husband, Ardin, has a rare gift for sensing nature. He'll scale any peak to gather the herbs and flowers I need for my alchemy, keeping our shelves and pantry stocked.\n\nBut I fear he's wandered into trouble. An excavation crew passed through seeking supplies. They spoke, among other things, of towering grasses unlike anything they'd ever seen. Those were what he told me he had to go see for himself. He's been gone too long!\n\nIf you learn anything of him, I'd be grateful.", objectives = "Find Ardin Grassman in the Excavation Sites." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95663] = { title = "Dragonmaw Rumors", description = "The Dragonmaw are a formidable clan.\n\nThey're known for binding magic strong enough to make dragons serve, and rumor claims they're preparing some display of it in the Wetlands. Whether truth or bluster, the Deathstalkers can't act on half-formed whispers. Broken symbols carried only that much to me.\n\nA deathstalker agent needs a hand in the hills above the Dragonmaw encampment. Meet her there. She'll reveal the next steps.", objectives = "Travel to the Wetlands and meet the Deathstalker Agent in the hills above the Dragonmaw camp.", completion = "Arrival of the courageous few? Mind your voice." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95664] = { title = "Elder Knowledge", description = "This unusual composite shard scatters light like a living prism. Its nature is uncertain, but its power feels ancient. The most knowledgeable minds for artifacts of this bygone age must reside on the Elder rise in Thunder Bluff.", objectives = "Take the Titan Relic to the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff and look for someone who can tell you more about it.", progress = "Spirits honor you. Have you come to share with us?", completion = "It is a favored sign to have a stranger approach in this manner. I feel a power amidst you... what is this you have brought?" }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95682] = { title = "Open the Maw", description = "Dragonmaw. <She lets out a dry, amused scoff.>\n\nThe remnants of the dragon-wrangling clan think they've found something that could lead to them rising to their former power. In the eyes of whom... their false warchief?\n\nClear out their ragtag clan within the Excavation Sites so our Deathstalkers can move in undetected.\n\nIf the Dragonmaw carry anything of note upon them, return it to me--this information must stay between us and our royal command.", objectives = "Slay the Dragonmaw forces within the Excavation Site and return to the Deathstalker Agent outside with anything you recover.", progress = "We're here to get the important job done. If you can help, prove it.", completion = "Don't mind me snatching that right out of your hands.\n\nI recognized that orcish scrawl. So they're hoping to appease Rend? A fruitless and wasted effort. \n\nNo matter, this is highly valuable knowledge for the dark lady to consider.\n\nHere, I won't be taking any of this with me--and don't talk about the mission, grunt." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95697] = { title = "Changing Tastes", description = "Zamja tells me we need more homestyle cooking.\nIf we start selling raptor, she thinks it'll draw in customers who don't usually visit Borstan's Firepit.\n\nHer idea is not so bad. But I want something that rises above the smells of our birth villages. We're in Orgrimmar! Borstan should serve a grand take on their familiar favorites.\n\nA hunter recently came back from the Wetlands with a giant talon from the thicket raptors in the Excavation Sites.\n\nUp for a job?", objectives = "Enter the Excavation Sites in the Wetlands and bring back Thicket Raptor Meat.", progress = "Farm-raised boar, farm-raised crawler... what's next, farm-raised raptor?", completion = "Look at the marbling on these! What are they eating up there? Thank you for going all the way and back for us. If you don't mind waiting, we'll cook some for you now, on the house, of course!" }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95737] = { title = "Seeking Caitlin", description = "From time to time, I correspond with others in my craft--herbalists or eccentrics who study rare plants and local oddities. We trade discoveries, and sometimes warnings of what lies ahead.\n\nOne alchemist in the Wetlands wrote of an excavation team her husband was part of, uncovering signs of a long-lost primordial grass... but she never sent word of its abundance or accessibility.\n\nIf you can, check on Caitlin Grassman in Menethil Harbor.", objectives = "Speak with Caitlin Grassman in Menethil Harbor.", completion = "Llana must be wondering where those grass seeds are that I promised I'd have my husband bring back! It comforts me to know she's as concerned as I am. It must be something about the excavation site itself that we're both sensing." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95748] = { title = "The Gurubashi Legends of Old", description = "This is odd. This piece of the tablet you have brought me refers to the lost city of I'lalai as if it is a massive sprawling civilization. But the ruins off of the reef are not large enough to be something of that size.\n\n{name}, to the north of the Vile Reef there is an ancient troll ruin on the hills along the coast. A tablet that contains legends of the lost troll city is within. I wish to study this legend further.\n\nTake this hide and charcoal to create a rubbing of this tablet, then return to me.", objectives = "Use the hide and charcoal to create a rubbing of the Third Troll Legend tablet." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95751] = { title = "Odd Totems", description = "The spirits have shown me a vision of heat, sun, and endless rolling dunes. A pair of lonely carved totems, overlooking the bones of a mighty beast half-buried by the sands of time. I was shown the desert hills of Tanaris, I am quite sure. \n\nThe totems' purpose is not known to me, but there is surely a purpose for their lonely vigil. I wish for you to seek this place out and see if you can solve this mystery.", objectives = "Investigate the Odd Totems in Tanaris." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95753] = { title = "Challenge of the Desert Wolf", description = "<The totem pulses with wild magic. The image of a ghostly wolf appears in your mind, beckoning you. \n\nIt appears to be offering you a challenge.\n\nAnother totem--a twin to the one that your hand now rests upon, appears in the distance just beyond the large sun-bleached skeleton nearby.>", objectives = "Reach the other Odd Totem at the end of the massive skeleton before time runs out." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95766] = { title = "Fine Feathered Friend", description = "The cycle of renewal has finally begun. The ancients... shall rise again, and the power of the natural world take its course... to bloom.\n\nYou... have helped us tip the scales in nature's favor. Perhaps... we can yet make a larger impact... on a more dire situation.\n\nHead west... where the land itself is ashen... and you may find an entity who can help. She may look like just a small bird... but her power is great.", objectives = "Find the strange bird in the corrupted lands on the southwest slope." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95769] = { title = "Threading a Solution", description = "Every day be a challenge when you living rough like we do! Takes a toll on your tools, your clothes, your whole life. Good thing it can't take our spirit!\n\nWe be really hurting from our clothes and blankets wearing out. You do some tailoring, right? So maybe you can bring me some Bolts of Runecloth and I can fix a few holes?", objectives = "Bring 6 Bolts of Runecloth to Mez'dan in Elderwild on Mount Hyjal." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95770] = { title = "Locating the Lost City", description = "After rereading the legend, it doesn't seem like we are in the wrong place for the lost city, but perhaps there is yet some detail that has been overlooked.\n\nIn my younger years I used to dive in the Vile Reef ruins, but that was before the murlocs settled there. If memory serves there was a cavern there.\n\nI have heard that there are now naga gathering in that region, which is unusual. I want to know what has lured them there.\n\nGo and explore just west of the Vile Reef and return to me with any news.", objectives = "Explore the Vile Reef and find the cavern entrance." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95771] = { title = "A Taste of Darkness", description = "", objectives = "" }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95772] = { title = "Songblade Search", description = "Me brother tried draggin' me off tae the Wetlands with some diggin' crew out o' Loch Modan. Said they were headin' into hills no dwarf's ever set boot in for some sort o' excavation.\n\nAye, I'd 'ave gone, if I wasn't already behind on this pile o' girdles I've got to refit.\n\nDaewyn normally writes after he sends off, though. Haven't heard a thing, gives me a strange feelin' this time.\n\nIf yer marchin' that way, mind checking in on me brother?", objectives = "Look for Dorin Songblade's brother, Daewyn, in Whelgar's Excavation Site." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95773] = { title = "Enemies in the Water", description = "{class}, your arrival is timely. I have just received new reports of naga activity just off of our coast. They seem to be swarming around some old troll ruins near the ocean floor.\n\nWe are already stretched thin defending from the local Bloodscalp and ogres ransacking our caravans. We cannot afford a surprise attack from the sea.\n\nGo and slay as many as you are able, and bring me their tridents as proof of your success.", objectives = "Gather 10 Brinescale Tridents from Brinescale Skirmishers." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95774] = { title = "Her Name Is Olgra", description = "The healer who saved me could not save her, and she has died in battle. Her name is Olgra, and I will never forget her.\n\nYou did not find her adornments on her body? She wore many jewels of polished bone.\n\nSlay the Razormane Raiders near where she fell, and find her precious works of art!\n\nI will place them with the memorial that I build in her memory.", objectives = "Slay quilboars and collect 4 of Olgra's Adornments for Mankrik's memorial.", progress = "I have only memories now, but I will build a tribute to Olgra so that they never fade.", completion = "I will place these adornments with Olgra's memorial, so that I never forget her. My blood will always run hot with revenge from this day until my last day. Each swing of my blade and enemy felled will be in her name.\n\nYou have done me... done us... a great honor. \n\nLok-tar, {name}." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95775] = { title = "The Drowned City", description = "What I am about to ask you is no small feat, {class}, and will likely require strong allies to accomplish.\n\nI want to know more about the ruins on the other side of the cavern the naga are guarding. If my suspicions prove correct, it could indeed be the lost city of I'lalai. The amount of lost historical knowledge at our fingertips could be unrivaled, but I am too old to venture myself.\n\nEnter the ruins and gather etchings of any tablets you find there, then return to me.", objectives = "Use the hide and charcoal to create rubbings of the tablets found in the Drowned City." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95776] = { title = "The Only Good Brinescale...", description = "You have done well to slay the naga just off of our coast, but the fact that they are in our waters in such numbers means there is yet a larger threat.\n\nI have spoken to Kin'weelay, and he thinks these Brinescale naga are infiltrating the ruins of the Drowned City. If the naga are there, then they are up to no good and are likely searching for something.\n\nWe can't let them get their hands on anything that could compromise us here and it is time to put an end to this. Slay their leader and return to me.", objectives = "Slay Var'Taka in the Drowned City." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95786] = { title = "An Acquaintance in Southshore", description = "{name}, I have a friend in the Hillsbrad Foothills that is studying troll legends and evil magic. I think he may have insight about how this foul magic captured Colenel Kurzen's mind.\n\nI also have a scout's report that the local trolls seem to be agitated, mentioning the word...\"I'lalai\".\n\nI must know if this is related to Kurzen's corruption! Here, take the fetishes and legends along with this scouting report to Loremaster Dibbs. With any luck he will be able to unravel some of their secrets.", objectives = "Find Loremaster Dibbs in Southshore and bring him the Savage Coast Report Bundle." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95787] = { title = "Take Two With Water", description = "<Loremaster Dibbs' hands shake as he reads the scouting report and the troll legends.>\n\nCould it be? By this account it sounds like the lost troll city of I'lalai has risen just off the coast of Stranglethorn! We must investigate immediately. Why, if my research is correct this could be the archeological discovery of the century!\n\nPlease, I know it is a long trek back to Stranglethorn but if you find yourself in this Drowned City, collect any legends you find there and return them to me.", objectives = "Use the hide and charcoal to create rubbings of the tablets found in the Drowned City." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95788] = { title = "Magics of the Drowned City", description = "The Skullsplitter fetishes Brother Nimetz sent with you are indeed powerful, though I do not think they contributed to Kurzen's condition, or at least not directly.\n\nStill, if the rumors are true and the lost troll city of I'lalai has indeed risen from its watery grave, it is possible the dark magics used to raise the doomed city may be related.\n\nIf you dare to venture into the Drowned City of I'lalai, please gather any troll fetishes you find and bring them here to me for further study.", objectives = "Collect 5 I'lalai Fetishes from trolls in the Drowned City." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95789] = { title = "Shady Saltseers", description = "Hey pal, you look like you can handle yourself in a fight.\n\nBaron Revilgaz has me keep'n my ear to the ground for magical objects. Word on the street is that a sunken troll ruin has mysteriously become, eh, un-sunk, which means there are a lot of unclaimed goods, if you catch my meaning.\n\nProblem is, it's also caught the eye of pirates! Not just any pirates, the Saltseers specifically collect magical artifacts. I need you to go into the Drowned City, clear them out and take their stolen artifacts.", objectives = "Collect 10 Voodoo Infused Artifacts from Saltseer pirates in the Drowned City." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95790] = { title = "Digestible Research", description = "<This journal seems to have been torn to shreds. From what little you can make out, it looks as if this was a field journal of one of the unfortunate Explorers' League adventurers.\n\nChew marks on the outside of the journal suggest it was likely raptors.\n\nPerhaps its pages can be found and reassembled.>", objectives = "Collect 15 Partially Digested Journal Pages from the Shaper's Terrace." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95791] = { title = "The Saltseer Captain", description = "The Saltseer pirates have been a thorn in my side recently and knowing they're in the Drowned City makes it worse! I mean they're always bad news, but there is one captain in particular I want outta the picture. That damned Captain Dreadrise!\n\nHe and his crew are very accomplished at gathering all the magical artifacts I've been after, and I'm tired of the competition.\n\nI want you to remove Captain Dreadrise and his Saltseer Coroners from the picture. Permanently.", objectives = "Slay 3 Saltseer Coroners and Captain Dreadrise in the Drowned City." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95792] = { title = "Clear 'em Out", description = "If you wanna land a big score, you gotta go where others wouldn't dare! This cave behind me's rich with untapped mineral deposits. I'm talkin' BIG bucks if we can get a crew in there.\n\nThere's just this... teeny tiny... dragon problem. It's nothing, really.\n\nIf you're willing to go in there and save me the hassle of clearing the dragons out, there's a nice reward in it for you. Not to mention, you'll be in the good graces of a future mining tycoon!", objectives = "Kill 8 Cinderscale Whelps and 4 Cinderscale Warriors for Gelinda Coppergleam." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95793] = { title = "Stemming the Demon Tide", description = "Ah, a {class}. I see great strength and determination in you--qualities necessary to rid these lands of evil.\n\nThe demons that walked these lands during the great battle were defeated, yet some still remain. It is important to prevent them from escaping.\n\nThe ruins to the east are dangerous. Carry your strength into their den. Destroy the unwelcome before our lands perish.", objectives = "Slay 12 Felguard Sentinels in Dae'gun." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95795] = { title = "Fallen in the Fen", description = "<You cover the dwarf's body with his cloak.>\n\nTravel to Lakeshire and personally inform Dorin Songblade what became of his brother within the Excavation Sites.", objectives = "Return to Dorin Songblade.", completion = "Ah no...\n<He buries his head in his hands and sobs.>\n\nI should 'ave gone with 'em. \n\nMuch of what I was smithin' was for 'im, was plannin' a surprise but it wasn't ready when he came by gettin' things for his journey.\n\nNow that these are finished, I don't have it in me to reforge or sell any of it.\nYou can have this. It's the least I can do for you, bringing me this grim day." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95798] = { title = "The Web of Magic", description = "{name}, I want you to take this I'lalai Fetish to my friend Abra in Dalaran. I would love to have her examine it if she has the time to do so.\n\nShe is also particularly interested in troll practices and magic, so I believe this discovery will be exciting for her to unravel.\n\nDo be careful, though. The Kirin Tor can be a bit particular about who they let into their grand city. If you haven't already become a noteworthy visitor, you may need to find a way into their good graces.", objectives = "Bring the I'lalai Fetish to Abra Cadabra in Dalaran." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95799] = { title = "Findings for the Explorer's League", description = "I must write my colleague in Ironforge at the Explorer's League immediately. This is a discovery of historical proportions.\n\nWould you mind delivering the letter to Ironforge for me? I will write a copy of my translations of the tablets for you.", objectives = "Bring Loremaster Dibbs' I'lalai Translations to Historian Karnik in Ironforge." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95803] = { title = "A Token of Good Faith", description = "Now that we've claimed the head of the tarnished commander, I need you to deliver it to the Undercity. Sylvanas Windrunner mistrusts us greatly, and all but openly disparages us.\n\nDeliver Rudolph Gelhardt's head to the Dark Lady. Show her that we tend to our own house and are devoted to the prosperity of the forsaken.", objectives = "Bring the head of Rudolph Gelhardt to Sylvanas Windrunner in the Undercity.", progress = "Why are you addressing me, {class}?", completion = "I don't doubt Danitha's sincerity and desire to earn a place for your kind amongst the Forsaken. However, I suspect that this isn't the last time we'll see one of your brothers and sisters go mad and turn the light against their own people.\n\nThere may come a time when I decide that tolerating your misbegotten order is no longer in the best interests of the Forsaken. I suggest you continue to serve your people diligently.\n\nWe will be watching." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95805] = { title = "Grace of An'she and Mu'sha", description = "The sun and the moon, An'she and Mu'sha, are not part of our world like the elements, yet their light gives us life, guidance, and hope.\n\nWe pay respect to the spirits of the world, and so we pay respect to the twins as well.\n\nIf you would show your respect, take this smoldering incense and bring it to a shrine in the hills to the southeast, overlooking the mesa, south of the quilboar. Be quick, so that you can reach the shrine before the incense burns away.\n\nDon't get it wet!", objectives = "Carry the Smoldering Incense to the shrine of An'she and Mu'sha in the southeastern hills before the incense burns to ash in ten minutes!", progress = "<The smoke from the incense rises toward the sky.>", completion = "<As you empty the incense into the fire, the scent wafts around you, leaving you with just the empty pouch and a subtle sense of fulfillment.>" }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95809] = { title = "Heartwoven", description = "I need a moment to rest before I find my own way out.\n\n<He pulls some reeds from his pack and quickly braids and bends them into a heart.>\n\nTake this, and bring it back to Caitlin. Let her know I'll be home soon! Now that we have a path cleared out thanks to you, I'll gather my bushels and follow your trail.\n\nThank you.", objectives = "Return to Caitlin Grassman in Menethil Harbor.", progress = "I'm more than worried about him!", completion = "Goodness, that sounds terrible!\n\nBy the light, I'm grateful he's one of the survivors.\n\n<She holds the reed-woven heart to her own.>\n\nI'll start cooking a hearty meal for him. Thank you for bringing me this. I'd like you to have something as a token of our appreciation." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95810] = { title = "Lost Relic Carry", description = "You pick up a fractured piece of the rock-mech automaton. It has a texture unlike anything you've touched before, a composite material of unknown makeup. This is certainly bound to be more 'device' than 'debris.'\n\nProspector Whelgar himself at his excavation site might have something useful to share about the relic.", objectives = "Bring the Titan Relic to Prospector Whelgar in the Wetlands excavation site." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95816] = { title = "Sign Me Up!", description = "Greetings, accomplished craftsperson!\n\nCompletion of this form will grant you non-exclusive, revocable, and legally limited permission to display advertisement signs for your tradeskill(s) all across Azeroth!\n\nOnce completed, please bring this to your local Azeroth Commerce Authority branch's Contract Coordinator to begin processing.\n\nHappy crafting!", objectives = "Bring the completed form to Elaine Compton in Redridge Mountains." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95817] = { title = "Rotgath Stonebeard", description = "Have you ever met Rotgath Stonebeard? He is a dwarven blacksmith in Ironforge. Not the most chatty fellow around, but always reliable. We often come to him when we need bulk crafts of simpler designs--the kind that Stondry is too proud to take on himself.\n\nHis turnaround times are excellent, particularly when it comes to helping new craftspeople get their shops established. I would trust no other to get your sign made fast. Let him know I sent you if he gives you any trouble!", objectives = "Meet Rotgath Stonebeard near the Great Forge in Ironforge." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95818] = { title = "A Quick Craft", description = "We can get ye sorted out and out of here in no time, provided you have the materials on hand! We are going to need 25 Mithril Bars and 15 Heavy Leather. Normally we need some other metals and the like too, but I've got some scrap that's been taking up space we can use for those extra bits.\n\nOh, as a personal favor, I am gonnae ask for 5 Goldthorn as well. My wife knows a great recipe for tea and I'd like to surprise her. Consider this your payment!", objectives = "Bring the requested materials to Rotgath Stonebeard near the Great Forge in Ironforge." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95819] = { title = "Sign Me Up!", description = "Greetings, accomplished craftsperson!\n\nCompletion of this form will grant you non-exclusive, revocable, and legally limited permission to display advertisement signs for your tradeskill(s) all across Azeroth!\n\nOnce completed, please bring this to your local Durotar Supply & Logistics Contract Coordinator to begin processing.\n\nHappy crafting!", objectives = "Bring the completed form to Jornah in The Barrens." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95820] = { title = "Karolek", description = "We have done well to create great relationships with the merchants and craftspeople of Orgrimmar. Among these excellent relationships is an orc named Karolek, a leatherworker who ensures a steady supply of hides and other useful equipment to us.\n\nHe also happens to be great at making signs!\n\nIf you'd like to get your sign made fast, I would recommend him over anyone else. Let him know I sent you.", objectives = "Meet Karolek at the Kodohide Leatherworkers shop in Orgrimmar." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95821] = { title = "A Quick Craft", description = "The materials for the sign should be easy to come by as an accomplished crafter like yourself. All we will need is 30 Heavy Leather and 12 Mithril Bars.\n\nNormally for a rush order I would charge a few gold, but I have had a craving for homemade Goldthorn Tea lately. Don't worry, I enjoy making it myself, but I do need 5 Goldthorn to make it happen.\n\nIf you bring me all of these, you'll have your first sign ready to go in no time!", objectives = "Bring the requested materials to Karolek in the Kodohide Leatherworkers shop in Orgrimmar." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95882] = { title = "WANTED: Scoutmaster Vargas", description = "An Alliance scouting party has been seen on a small island northeast of Rog'mar. They are led by a scoutmaster who has made tracking enemy movements increasingly difficult. The bastard even named his filthy pet after me as an open mockery. He knows I'm hunting him.\n\nThis human has eyes everywhere, and they need to be put out. I already claimed one before he managed to flee. Bring me his other as proof that the scoutmaster is no more. Show him he is not as untouchable as he thinks.\n\n-- Neza Bloodsnout", objectives = "Bring the Scoutmaster's Eye to Neza Bloodsnout in Rog'mar." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95883] = { title = "The Tortured Soul", description = "<The preparations for a hastily-assembled ritual are gathered unceremoniously on the altar. According to the scrap of note, everything has been gathered. All that's missing are the offering of blood and the Tortured Soul.\n\nThe undead around you look tortured enough. They may have what you seek.>", objectives = "Collect a Tortured Soul from the nearby undead in Beren's Peril in Silverpine Forest.", progress = "<The offering stone is ominously still.>", completion = "<The tortured soul lets out a foul energy in the presence of the offering stone.\n\nIt appears you are closer to fulfilling the ritual.>" }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95884] = { title = "The Offering Stone", description = "<The scrap of note is mostly illegible. What is still readable, however, are notes about preparations for an offering.\n\nAn offering stone is mentioned, as well as a ritual.\n\nPerhaps you can find this offering stone nearby.>", objectives = "Find the Offering Stone in Beren's Peril in Silverpine Forest.", completion = "<Strange implements and items litter the rough surface of the stone.\n\nThis is surely the offering stone that is mentioned in the note.>" }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95885] = { title = "The Offering of Blood", description = "<All that's left now is the offering of blood.\n\nThe note scrap mentioned a 'willing sacrifice.'\n\nAn intense sense of dread washes over you.>", objectives = "Use the Tortured Soul to give an offering of blood at the Offering Stone in Beren's Peril.", progress = "<The offering stone is ominously still.>", completion = "<The offering stone is inert now. It appears your ritual drained it of power. To what end, you do not know, but it is over now.\n\nThe rough stone cracks and crumbles, now devoid of purpose.\n\nSomething glitters from within the remnants...>" }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95912] = { title = "WANTED: Blademaster Kaijo", description = "With each orc we cut down, another takes its place--somehow even more capable than the last. A skilled warrior must be training this new generation. If we are to make a dent in their numbers, we need to ensure they don't have a chance to recoup their losses.\n\nIf any soldier is brave enough, it's imperative we find this blademaster and put an end to him. He is likely at the trainee camp north of the Horde outpost even now. Kill him, take his banner, and destroy the orcs' morale.\n\n-- Ember Bladewhisper", objectives = "Bring the Blademaster's Banner to Ember Bladewhisper in Farholde Keep." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95913] = { title = "Fit for a Princess", description = "<Tessa rocks her baby, trying to help her sleep.>\n\nIf she isn't hungry, maybe she's just tired. To be honest, Emma here was a delightful surprise, but that means we were a little unprepared. My husband built her this lovely bassinet, but I worry these blankets are too old. She deserves the best, after all.\n\nIf you're still willing to help, I would be forever grateful if you could find some pelts for me to line her bed with. If this stops her crying, I think everyone in Farholde would be grateful.", objectives = "Collect 3 Coyote Pelts for Tessa Dawnbright in Farholde Keep." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95924] = { title = "Panic at the Digsite", description = "Ye there! Aye, I'm talkin' ta ye! We've made the discovery of a lifetime down in Un'Goro! Can ye believe it?\n\nThere's just one problem... our dig site's been overrun by voracious beasts of the killin' nature. Very unpleasant indeed.\n\nWith yer help, we can reclaim our camp and git back ta workin'. Now, what do ye say? I'll make it worth yer while.", objectives = "Slay 6 Ravasaur Matriarchs, 9 Ironhide Ravasaurs and Venomridge in Shaper's Terrace." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95925] = { title = "Mapping the Way Forward", description = "{class}, we've made the discovery of a lifetime! I can't believe it; the ruins in Un'Goro are open!\n\nWe've already sent a team but they have encountered... trouble. If you're headed in there anyway would ya be able to finish this map?\n\nIt sounds like there's an Achromatic Crystal in there and an unearthed watcher somewhere near a giant Western Gate that sounds interesting.\n\nThe other landmarks that would be helpful are the Pillar of Assimilation, the Western Gate and the Regrowth Vestibule.", objectives = "Find Interesting Landmarks in Shaper's Terrace and fill out the explorer's map at each." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95926] = { title = "The Dark Crystal", description = "You there! I have a job for someone of your... skills.\n\nI have gotten word from my sources of a crystal found in Shaper's Terrace that can seemingly drain the elements around it. Or perhaps it can drain life essence itself. It is unclear from this report.\n\nI must have a fragment of this crystal! Just think of the applications of such a powerful artifact.\n\nGo to Shaper's Terrace and bring me back a sample of this colorless Achromatic Crystal, and I will reward you for your efforts.", objectives = "Gather a colorless Drained Crystal Fragment near the Achromatic Crystal in the Shaper's Terrace." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95928] = { title = "Crystalline Elements", description = "Ah, it is good you have come here, {class}.\n\nI have been studying crystals of late and word has reached me about a peculiar set of crystals said to be from Un'Goro Crater. I have samples of the most basic ones, but I have heard tell of larger more potent crystals seen in a place called Shaper's Terrace.\n\nI do not know much of this place aside from it containing these crystals that supposedly have the very elements within them. If you find yourself there, please bring me a sample of each color.", objectives = "Bring Mayena Earthseeker a Moist Crystal, a Charged Crystal, a Noxious Crystal and a Fiery Crystal from Shaper's Terrace." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95934] = { title = "Proof of Profit", description = "My surveying tools show signs of a never-before-seen mineral in these caves. Cubic draconia, I call it. Probably worth a fortune.\n\nExciting as this is, no one's gonna come help me dig it up if I can't show 'em proof that it exists. Sure, I have the readings from my tools, but people like to hold a big shiny crystal, not look at charts.\n\nI'm sure there's a few crystals poking up from the dirt in there. If you're willing to dodge a few dragons and get one, you'd really be helpin' a gal out.", objectives = "Find a piece of Cubic Draconia for Gelinda Coppergleam." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95935] = { title = "Hail the Dragonslayer", description = "The dragon's head is all teeth, scale, and ash--a grisly prize taken from a grisly creature. Holding it, you feel the heat of its last fiery breath still radiating from its mouth.\n\nWhile the threat Scaldaron once posed is no more, the sentries at the Southern Watch ought to know about what happened here.", objectives = "Take the Head of Scaldaron to Cedric Dalton at the Southern Watch." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95936] = { title = "Hail the Dragonslayer", description = "The dragon's head is all teeth, scale, and ash -- a grisly prize taken from a grisly creature. Holding it, you feel the heat of its last fiery breath still radiating from its mouth.\n\nWhile the threat Scaldaron once posed is no more, the warriors of Rog'mar ought to know about what happened here.", objectives = "Take the Head of Scaldaron to Krom'rosh at Rog'mar." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95943] = { title = "Foreman's Plight", description = "G'day, <lad/lass>. Name's Bertrand, Bertrand Ironbrow! At yer service.\n\n<Bertrand extends a filthy hand.>\n\nThese fine folk contracted me tae oversee construction of this here keep. What they lack in experience they make up for in spirit! Problem is, I misplaced me tools.\n\nHad a bit of a run in with a few Twilight in a small grove northwest o' here. Had to choose between me life or me tools. On one hand, I'm alive. On the other... ye see where this is goin'.\n\nThink ye could help find me tools?", objectives = "Locate the Foreman's Crate and return it to Bertrand Ironbrow in Farholde Keep." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95951] = { title = "Fetch 'n' Fletch", description = "'Ey boss-<mon/lady>, ya need help from ol' Tan'jani? Don't worry about it, I fix you up good.\n\nOrcs be good at hittin' humans with axes, but when you wanna stick 'em before dey see ya comin', that's when you call on the headhunters. You wanna learn to stick 'em too? I see it in your eyes, heheh.\n\nFirst we get you your own spears. Dis one's mine. Go to the human camp to de west and take their wood. Take knife with ya. You can sharpen their lumber into good spears for stickin'. Den bring 'em back.", objectives = "Collect Wood Bundles from Peasant Woodpiles in Turner's Logging Camp then fletch them into 20 Makeshift Stickin' Spears." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95955] = { title = "Stick 'Em", description = "You got de spears, now ya gonna learn how to throw dem.\n\nDe Riverglades be full o' crocolisks. Nasty tings. Snap you up if ya ain't quick. Perfect for target practice, heheh.\n\nGo stick yourself a bunch of dem. Den you come back to ol' Tran'jani for ya prize. If ya can stick a crocolisk, ya can stick any'ting.", objectives = "Impale 10 Freshwater Crocolisks then return to Tran'jani in Rog'mar." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95957] = { title = "Drink Up!", description = "Here ya go, champ. One drink for ol' grumpy guts over there. If this doesn't sober him up, nothin' will.\n\nOh and uh... wash your hands after touchin' this. And don't get it in your eyes.", objectives = "Deliver Zizplink's Frothing Mug to Gray Dawnbright in Powderfuse Port." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95961] = { title = "Stepped Out", description = "<Tessa's baby continues to wail loudly.>\n\nI guess she isn't tired. Oh... everyone makes it look so easy. Her father always knows how to cheer her up. If only he'd come home already.\n\n{name}, I hate to ask this, but can you see what is taking him so long? He set out a while ago but he should have been back by now. Emma just lights up when she sees him.\n\nYou should find him at Powderfuse Port-- he seems to go there a lot lately. You'll know my Gray when you see him. He shines as brightly as the sun.", objectives = "Find Gray Dawnbright in Powderfuse Port." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95975] = { title = "Her World", description = "Tess says little Emm can't sleep without me? And you did all that for them? A total stranger? Damn it. What was I thinking...\n\nEven if I can't guarantee a perfect world for her, I still need to be a part of it. What am I even fighting for if I can't hope for a brighter future?\n\nThank you for helping my family in my absence, friend, but it's time for me to go home. If I could ask one more favor, can you pick some flowers and take them to Tess? Let her know I'll be home soon? I need to clean up first.", objectives = "Gather 20 Wildflowers and deliver them to Tessa Dawnbright in Farholde Keep." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95981] = { title = "Watching the Roads", description = "Taking away their pendants is just the first step. If the Kirin Tor really are shipping a steady supply of relics from Dalaran, we must stop them at the source.\n\nSearch the roads around Ambermill for Dalaran's wizards and watchers. Their presence has allowed free access across our borders for too long. If we can cull their numbers, that should put a stop to these pendants making it into Silverpine Forest in the first place.", objectives = "Slay 8 Dalaran Wizards and 8 Dalaran Watchers for Shadow Priest Allister in the Sepulcher.", completion = "Ever since the barrier went down around Dalaran, the Kirin Tor have maintained a death grip on the roads. They're paranoid about something, that much is certain.\n\nFor now, however, the why is irrelevant." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95982] = { title = "Not My Circus", description = "Folks keep dumpin' their furry friends here like I know what I'm doin'. And then they blame me if they come back and their horse or wolf or... whatever they brought is dead or ran off. What do I look like, I'm runnin' a charity?\n\nYou look like you know your way around a trough. Mind whippin' me up some grub I can use to keep these beasties in check?\n\nIf you can't make it yourself, someone might be willin' to sell you some. And hurry! Last thing I need is a stampede of hungry animals.", objectives = "Bring 10 Briny Seafood Stew to Jasper Geartoggle in Powderfuse Port." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95983] = { title = "A Feast for Buzzards", description = "The skeleton is badly mangled. Deep markings on its limbs vaguely match patterns of teeth and claws. Many days beneath the beating sun have made the bones pale and brittle as well. The brutality of both the attacker and the weather have rendered the victim's identity a mystery.\n\nYou can't take the whole skeleton with you, but you could bring its skull to the nearby watchman and see what he knows.", objectives = "Bring the Gnawed Skull to Watcher Cornelius at Terral's Watch." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95984] = { title = "Song of the Strider", description = "These markings are from a lion. By the look of them, this one's especially large. The leader of the nearby pride, most likely.\n\nIf rumor spreads about a man-eating lion prowling around on my watch, Demar will be furious. Fortunately, I have a plan.\n\nI can make a whistle that mimics the call of a wounded tallstrider. We can use that to lure the beast out. I'll just need one of their beaks to give it the right sound. There's tallstriders all over the plains. Get me a beak, and make it snappy!", objectives = "Bring an Intact Tallstrider Beak to Watcher Cornelius at Terral's Watch." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95986] = { title = "King of the Wild Plains", description = "The whistle's made, {name}. \n\nTake it, and go to the top of the hill where the lions are. Should be just north of here.\n\nOnce you're there, blow the whistle, and our man-eater should appear. I'd tell you not to come back if you don't manage to kill him, but you'll probably be dead anyhow.\n\nNow then, off with you. Let's see if you fare better than our skeletal friend.", objectives = "Use the Tallstrider Call to call forth the leader of the lion pride. Slay the beast and retrieve its hide for Watcher Cornelius at Terral's Watch." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95988] = { title = "Goes Down Smooth", description = "Talked to Gray, didja? Ball of laughs, that guy. Last thing he needs is you gettin' him another drink. This is an inn not a bar. He's lucky I haven't thrown him out.\n\nYou tryin' to take him with you, be my guest. Though I don't think he's in any condition to go anywhere like that. Not without a little goblin pick-me-up.\n\nWhy don't ya gather some ingredients for me from this list while I prepare your little friend his 'drink.' We'll see if he still wants booze after he's had my specialty cocktail.", objectives = "Gather 3 Crawler Spittle, Fresh Chum, Goblin Degreaser, and Expired Poison for Innkeeper Zizplink in Powderfuse Port." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95991] = { title = "WANTED: Ghostmaw", description = "It's dangerous enough transportin' horses 'round the glades without talk of some mysterious phantom crocolisk snappin' up my prized ponies! They say this one must be at least three times as big as a regular croc. And twice as mean!\n\nI ain't a gamblin' man. I ain't takin' no chances with my horses till someone puts this good-fer-nothin' monster down. If anyone finds this varmint along the rivers, bring me its tooth so's I know it's safe to travel again. Till then, I'm stayin' put!\n\n-- Wheatley", objectives = "Bring Ghostmaw's Fang to Wheatley in Farholde Keep." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95992] = { title = "WANTED: Ghostmaw", description = "Dese waters be treacherous. My headhunters keep the paths clear as dey can, but there be a beasty stalkin' de rivers even we cannot catch. Excitin', eh?\n\nBoss say we gotta clear it out, so we got a little competition goin'. Find de white one patrollin' de rivers and bring me its fang. Whoever sticks this slippery crocolisk win de whole pot. Just don't get snapped yourself, heheh!\n\n-- Tan'jani", objectives = "Bring Ghostmaw's Fang to Tan'jani in Rog'mar." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95998] = { title = "The Great Outdoors", description = "Well howdy there, {class}. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. Good for you. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.\n\nIt's a big wide world out there and you'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful. Not sure how your outdoorsman skills are but I reckon I could teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.\n\nHave a seat near the fire, get comfy. I'll walk you through it.", objectives = "Sit near Sam's Basic Campfire and wait until you receive the Boosted Rest buff.", progress = "Having the skills needed to survive the outdoors is critical. A well-rested and well-prepared adventurer has a much higher chance of surviving this lifestyle.", completion = "So now that we've learned the basics, why don't you go and learn a tradeskill. They will also teach you the know-how to create a proper camp fixture suitable to your new profession." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[95999] = { title = "WANTED: Incinerator Gar'im", description = "Wanted! Incinerator Gar'im, Leader of an orc incursion in Render's Valley. Purported to be working with the Blackrock of Stonewatch Keep.\n\nBeware of Incinerator Gar'im. He and his Shadowcasters are extremely dangerous. A handsome reward will be given to any brave soul that can deliver proof of Incinerator Gar'im's demise to Magistrate Solomon.", objectives = "Deliver the Broken Staff of Incinerator Gar'im to Magistrate Solomon in Lakeshire.", progress = "What do you have there, {race}?", completion = "Excellent work, {name}! Incinerator Gar'im was preparing to bolster the defenses at Stonewatch Keep. With this victory, we may yet succeed in reclaiming the keep!" }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96003] = { title = "Drawing Down the Malevolent", description = "As suspected, the vessels fused into something new--something powerful.\n\nI suppose if the vessels capture stored energy, there must be a way to use that power to our advantage. Fel artifacts are rarely safe or easy to come by, but we might as well do something with it, hmm?\n\nTime for a field test.\n\nTake the crystal and use it against Bethra'zel and Mazzogore--two of their most powerful demons. Their presence alone has ensured the camp is well protected. Let's see if we can change that.", objectives = "Use the Eye of Endless Influence on Bethra'zel and Mazzogore to siphon their power, then deliver the killing blow." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96009] = { title = "High Stakes", description = "One thing that never ceases to amaze me is the drive of humans. They see a desolate warzone teemin' with orcs and cultists and figure that's the perfect spot tae set up shop! Amazin'.\n\nBut, it's not me job tae tell 'em where to build. Just gotta show 'em how. And if we want this keep tae be as big as they say, we're gonna need lots o' wood.\n\nWith how dangerous the roads have become our lumber shipments from the mill tae the northwest are slowin' to a crawl. Think ye can fetch a few bundles for us?", objectives = "Collect 10 Wood Bundles from Turner's Logging Camp for Bertrand Ironbrow in Farholde Keep." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96010] = { title = "Fragments of the Pylons", description = "Although I am sure we can attribute the damage to both pylons to the reckless centaur stomping about, I suspect the timing of their rampage resulted in the shards being separated. I know little about their quarrels, but I do know there are at least two main factions that have trespassed into Shen'dralas: the ferocious Magram and the cunning Gelkis.\n\nKeeping these treasures in the midst of a battlefield would be unwise. By now, I am assuming they have taken their trophies back to their own villages.", objectives = "Recover shards and fragments of the pylons, found guarded at the Magram and Gelkis villages. Return them to Mordent Evenshade." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96015] = { title = "A Miner Problem", description = "We should be thankful that our foe is stupid. An army of ogres at their disposal, and the Twilight's Hammer have them working in the mines nowhere near the fight. I don't know if I chalk it up to mismanagement or an internal struggle, but either way they're in no position to defend themselves.\n\nThat's where we come in. With the cult's focus divided, we have an opportunity to strike the enemy while they're vulnerable and split them further. Go to this mine and sow some chaos among their ranks.", objectives = "Defeat 5 Ogre Miners and 5 Twilight Subjugators in the cave near the Twilight's Shroud for Sergeant Riftan." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96016] = { title = "The Tempest's Weapons", description = "Ye did good, and I can see yer itchin' fer yer reward. Sorry tae say, I'm not exactly a dwarf of many possessions.\n\n<Veyric gestures broadly at his remote location.>\n\nTell ye what, though. I hear a troll named the Windwatcher lives out in the Alterac Mountains. He's a powerful shaman himself, and an expert in storm elementals. If ye bring that there elemental core to him, I bet he can make ye a weapon worthy of yer victory.", objectives = "Deliver the Eye of the Tempest to Bath'rah the Windwatcher in Alterac Mountains." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96018] = { title = "Powering the Pylons", description = "You may have seen the floating sparks of mana scattered throughout Shen'dralas. This is a new phenomenon, likely the result of the damage the pylons have endured.\n\nWe need this mana back in a semicrystallized form. We can accomplish this by using the Mana Sieve found within the temple. Borrow the sieve and collect any floating mana orbs you find.\n\nThe temple's denizens will not appreciate their precious artifact being borrowed without their consent, but they will understand in time.", objectives = "Acquire the Mana Sieve from within the temple in Shen'dralas and use it to collect Ancient Mana Crystals. Once you have acquired enough mana, empower the pylons and return to Mordent Evenshade." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96020] = { title = "Playing with Fire", description = "<The carving is faintly warm to the touch, despite the long-cold char on the body you retrieved it from.\n\nIt appears the poor soul didn't finish whatever they were trying to enact. Though you don't recognize the inscriptions on the idol, it calls to your fire magic. Perhaps you may succeed where they have failed.>", objectives = "Complete the Brimstone Carving's ritual and bring the results to a warlock trainer." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96025] = { title = "As the Crow Flies", description = "Thank you for your help, {name}. A dear friend of mine awaits your arrival at the summit.\n\nYou can find her up the road to the east.", objectives = "Meet Elaena's friend at the summit in Hyjal." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96026] = { title = "Step Two: More Rock", description = "Dese good rock. Now need finishing touch. More rock.\n\nOnly rock can make rock stronger. Dat the way of rocks.\n\nMe see some tinies make extra heavy rock. Bring me heavy rocks and me make weapon.", objectives = "Deliver 10 Heavy Weightstones to Hamur in Bolder'ok." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96031] = { title = "Camping 101: Leatherworking", description = "You've become a leatherworker. Good for you, {class}. I reckon I know someone that can teach you how to make yourself a tent that will keep you cool on hot days, and dry on rainy days.\n\nWith a good tent over your head, you'll ensure that you get all the rest you need to stay sharp on your travels.", objectives = "Speak with Gretta Finespindle in Ironforge to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.", completion = "There you have it, your very own camp tent. Most folk don't care much for tents being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\n\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96044] = { title = "Camping 101: Blacksmithing", description = "So, you've become a Blacksmith. That's a great choice if you want to make sure your blades never dull.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can help with that by teaching you how to craft a Sharpening Wheel. Bring one of these out at your camp and all the warriors and rogues in the area will be lining up to hone their weapons.", objectives = "Speak with Tognus Flintfire in Kharanos to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.", completion = "There you have it, you can now craft your very own Sharpening Wheel. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\n\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96045] = { title = "Camping 101: Alchemy", description = "Now that you've taken up Alchemy, I can also teach you how to craft a Mana Well for your camp once you've learned a bit. Build one of these and all of the healers and spellcaster types will come running to get a refreshing taste.", objectives = "Speak with Vosur Brakthel in Ironforge to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.", completion = "There you have it, you can now craft your very own Mana Well. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\n\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96046] = { title = "Camping 101: Mining", description = "Mining isn't the most glamorous, but it's good honest work and a fine profession for you to explore.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Lodestone for your camp. Build one of these and everyone who wants to swing a sword will be eager to gather round your fire and soak up the extra \"oomph\" it can provide to increase their combat prowess.", objectives = "Speak with Yarr Hammerstone in Kharanos to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.", progress = "Yes, I can teach you.", completion = "There you have it, you can now craft your very own Lodestone. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\n\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96047] = { title = "Camping 101: First Aid", description = "So you've taken up First Aid? That's an honorable... and pragmatic pursuit as a {class}.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a First Aid Kit for your camp. Injuries are a reality in the world of adventuring and offering some much-needed healing at your camp could even save lives.", objectives = "Speak with Thamner Pol in Kharanos to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.", progress = "I can teach you once you've gained some skill with your profession.", completion = "There you have it, you can now craft your very own First Aid Kit. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\n\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96050] = { title = "Camping 101: Fishing", description = "You might not think so, but your skill as a fisherman can actually come in handy at camp.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Fish Bowl for your camp. You can use this fixture to help provide a bit of joy to yourself and your fellow adventurers. A happy adventurer is a strong adventurer and I'm sure your combat capabilities will reflect that.", objectives = "Speak with Paxton Ganter near Iceflow Lake in Dun Morogh to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.", completion = "There you have it, you can now craft your very own Fish Bowl. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\n\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96055] = { title = "Camping 101: Herbalism", description = "Looks to me like you've gained some skill in herbalism. Picking flowers isn't just for dilly-dallying, you know. It can be useful... and profitable.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Incense Candle for your camp. High spirits are a key component to keeping healers and spellcasters in the fight, and an Incense Candle can provide a boost that magic users will surely appreciate.", objectives = "Speak with Reyna Stonebranch in Ironforge to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.", completion = "There you have it, you can now craft your very own Incense Candle. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\n\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96056] = { title = "Camping 101: Skinning", description = "Being able to skillfully harvest the skins and hides of fallen beasts is one of the more valuable skills an adventurer can possess.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Camp Chair for your camp. Sometimes it's important to just take a load off, and you can use some of those hides you've gathered to make a comfy chair to sit in. A bit of relaxation can help ensure that you are at your peak condition and can strike where it counts the next time you find yourself in a dust-up.", objectives = "Speak with Balthus Stoneflayer in Ironforge to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.", completion = "There you have it, you can now craft your very own Camp Chair. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\n\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96057] = { title = "Camping 101: Tailoring", description = "Tailoring is a surprisingly potent tradeskill to invest in, and I'm sure it'll serve you well.\n\nI know someone that can teach you how to craft a Faction Banner for your camp, provided you have the skill for it. Inspiration and morale are a key part of success on any battlefield, and an inspirational banner can go a long way to keeping you energized.", objectives = "Speak with Uthrar Threx in Ironforge to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.", completion = "There you have it, you can now craft your very own Rallying Banner. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\n\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96058] = { title = "Camping 101: Engineering", description = "Engineers like yourself can cook up all sorts of bits, bots, and bombs for fun and profit.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Reagent Bot for your camp. This helpful automaton can help keep you well-supplied so that you and your allies never run out of the materials needed to fuel your spells.", objectives = "Speak with Bronk Guzzlegear in Kharanos to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.", completion = "There you have it, you can now craft your very own Reagent Bot. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\n\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96059] = { title = "Camping 101: Enchanting", description = "Now that you've begun your journey into being an enchanter, I reckon I can teach you how to craft an Enchanted Lute for your camp once you've learned the ropes.\n\nIt's so important to find entertainment during your downtime, and this bit of magic can help ensure you are ready to weather all sorts of challenges when you hit the old dusty trail once again.", objectives = "Speak with Thonys Pillarstone in Ironforge to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.", progress = "Yes, I can teach you.", completion = "There you have it, you can now craft your very own Enchanted Lute. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\n\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96060] = { title = "Tempered Expectations", description = "Let me be the first to share that I was a master swordsman in life. I forged weapons by day and wielded them by night.\n\nAs you are quite well aware, my relationship with this particular blade is now extraordinarily complicated. Though I think I could swing it around, I'm not convinced it would be of much use unless I was fighting other spirits. Is that really of any value to me in Shen'dralas?\n\nNonetheless, I would like its capabilities tested and I think our forests could use a gentle culling.", objectives = "Use the Phantasmal Blade to execute 8 wildlife in Shen'dralas, then return to Vindael at the temple." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96063] = { title = "Gaseous Gold", description = "The fuel of the future's not coal, or oil, it's gas, baby! Those marshy ponds to the southwest spew it out by the ton, and I've got just the invention to put it to use--a new type of engine that runs on the stuff. The gas is a real pain to collect, though.\n\nIf you feel like making a humble contribution to the future of science and industry, why don't you help me get some of that gas? You can see it coming up from vents near the water.", objectives = "Gather 5 Marsh Gas Vials for Sleebo Fizzlespout." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96067] = { title = "Rock 'em and Sock 'em", description = "You may have noticed my mechanical companion here, G45-B4G. Whirlin' around in that burlap chest of his is the one, and only, working prototype of my gas-powered engine.\n\nI figure it's in need of some stress testing. How'd you like to take him on in a fight? I can power him up with the gas you've collected.\n\nOh, and don't worry about hurting him. He can't feel a thing!", objectives = "Help Sleebo test his creation." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96076] = { title = "In Demand - Ancient Elven Curiosities", description = "My employers are looking to get their hands on magical curiosities from the ruined elven city of Eldre'Thalas, now known as Dire Maul. Some kind of magical research. In any case, if you could acquire these items, I can afford to reward you generously.\n\nRetrieve a Felvine Seed from Alzzin the Wildshaper in the eastern wing, an Ancient Memento from Prince Tortheldrin in the western wing, and an Earthstone Diamond Pinky Ring from King Gordok in the northern wing.", objectives = "Travel to Dire Maul to acquire a Felvine Seed from Alzzin the Wildshaper, an Ancient Memento from Prince Tortheldrin, and an Earthstone Diamond Pinky Ring from King Gordok, and bring them to Pix Xizzix in Booty Bay." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96077] = { title = "Belle's Ring", description = "Yes, Thomas Belle.\n\n<Daythor's demeanor changes suddenly, appearing as though to recall a fond memory of this individual.>\n\nThomas was one of the first to fall as the scourge laid siege to our outpost. I hadn't heard of his passing until the battle was over. Tragic... He was such a promising young man.\n\nI suppose it would be right for us to deliver this to his beloved Michelle. If memory serves me right, he spoke often of Goldshire.", objectives = "Deliver the ring to Michelle Belle at the Lion's Pride Inn in Elwynn Forest." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96078] = { title = "A Tale Spun Around the Fire", description = "{name}, we Darkspear keep much of our traditions alive by oral storytelling. We pass legends such as these to the next generation, teaching lessons and weaving cautionary tales to our younglings.\n\nThese etchings must be taken to our spiritual leader, Master Gadrin in Sen'jin Village. He is one of the wisest Darkspear and he will wish to hear the truth of this tale.\n\nI have prepared an extra copy of this tale for you as well. If you ever lose your copy, I would be happy to create another, for a small fee.", objectives = "Take the tablet etchings to Master Gadrin in Sen'jin Village in Durotar." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96081] = { title = "Wound Dressings", description = "If there is one thing a fighting force always needs, it's bandages. Unfortunately, Farholde has no reliable way to manufacture cloth. Thus, we depend on imports from the goblins or, if we are lucky, what we can take back from the orcs.\n\nCurrently, our supply of quality cloth is running low. I will have to start making bandages of old shirts before long. If you have the means to aid us, you would be saving many lives.", objectives = "Gather 20 Mageweave Cloth for Brother Lowley at Farholde Keep." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96082] = { title = "Doctor's Orderly", description = "I will fashion the cloth you've given me into bandages. In the meantime, please take these ones that I have already made, and dress the wounds of the soldiers who need it. It should be a matter of basic first aid.\n\nYour assistance here is both necessary, and highly appreciated. I simply cannot be everywhere at once.", objectives = "Bandage up 3 Wounded Soldiers for Brother Lowley." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96083] = { title = "Clerical Quarantine", description = "You have done all you can here, for now.\n\nIf you wish to be of further aid, go up the hill to the chapel. It is the smaller building outside the main church.\n\nSister Rowland is looking after a few quarantined soldiers there who have contracted an unknown illness.", objectives = "Speak to Sister Rowland at the chapel in Farholde Keep." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96084] = { title = "Something's in the Water", description = "I will spare you the grisly details, but these soldiers are violently ill. The nature of their sickness leads me to believe there is an issue with either their food or their water.\n\nI've already checked the crops coming in from the nearby farms, so this only leaves the water, which comes from the local rivers. The best place to collect a sample is from the pools in the plains to the north. Nearly every river runs through the area, so it would be wise to check for contamination there.", objectives = "Collect a sample of drinking water from the plains for Sister Rowland at the chapel in Farholde Keep." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96085] = { title = "Upstream Contamination", description = "The impurities in this sample look organic in nature. Not quite waste, but certainly something toxic.\n\nI am no expert on wildlife, but I would guess that there is something upstream causing the water contamination. Some kind of animal, or at least a creature.\n\nFollow the rivers as far north as you can, and see if you can find what is responsible for this. If it is an animal, it must be put down. It is for the safety of all here in Farholde.", objectives = "Find whatever creature is causing the drinking water contamination and eliminate it. Then, return to Sister Rowland at the chapel in Farholde Keep." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96101] = { title = "The Great Outdoors", description = "Greetings, {class}. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. This is good. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.\n\nYou'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful in this line of work. Not sure how your outdoor skills are but I can probably teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.\n\nHave a seat near the fire and get comfortable. I'll walk you through it.", objectives = "Sit near Raan's Basic Campfire and wait until you receive the Boosted Rest buff.", progress = "Having the skills needed to survive the outdoors are critical. A well-rested and well-prepared adventurer has a much higher chance of surviving this lifestyle.", completion = "So now that we've learned the basics, why don't you go and learn a tradeskill from the trainers in the village nearby. They will also teach you how to create a camp fixture suitable to your new profession." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96102] = { title = "Camping 101: Tailoring", description = "Tailoring is a surprisingly potent tradeskill to invest in, and I'm sure it'll serve you well.\n\nI know someone that can teach you how to craft a Faction Banner for your camp, provided you have the skill for it. Inspiration and morale are a key part of success on any battlefield, and an inspirational banner can go a long way to keeping you energized.", objectives = "Speak with Snang in Orgrimmar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.", completion = "There you have it, you can now craft your very own Rallying Banner. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\n\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96103] = { title = "A Feast for Buzzards", description = "The skeleton is badly mangled. Deep markings on its limbs vaguely match patterns of teeth and claws. Many days beneath the beating sun have made the bones pale and brittle as well. The brutality of both the attacker and the weather have rendered the victim's identity a mystery.\n\nYou can't take the whole skeleton with you, but you could bring its skull to a hunter at Rog'mar and see what they know.", objectives = "Bring the Gnawed Skull to Neza Bloodsnout at Rog'mar." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96104] = { title = "Song of the Strider", description = "These markings are from a lion. By the look of them, this one is especially large--the leader of the nearby pride.\n\nI would gladly hunt the beast myself, but you have first claim. Instead, I will aid you.\n\nI can make a whistle that mimics the call of a wounded tallstrider. You can use it to lure the lion out. I'll just need one of their beaks to give it the right sound.\n\nThere are tallstriders all over the plains. Find me a beak and the hunt can begin!", objectives = "Bring an Intact Tallstrider Beak to Neza Bloodsnout at Rog'mar." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96105] = { title = "King of the Wild Plains", description = "The whistle is made, {name}.\n\nTake it and go to the top of the hill south where the lions dwell.\n\nOnce you are ready to face your quarry, blow the whistle and the beast should appear.\n\nI wish you luck in your hunt. May you return in glory.", objectives = "Use the Tallstrider Call to call forth the leader of the lion pride. Slay the beast and retrieve its hide for Neza Bloodsnout at Rog'mar." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96107] = { title = "Feathers for Fletching", description = "A hunter goes through more arrows in her lifetime than there are stars in the sky.\n\nPersonally, I make mine by hand. I only trust my own work.\n\nThe coarse feathers of the nearby buzzards make for excellent fletching. Would you aid me by collecting a few?", objectives = "Bring 6 Plains Buzzard Feathers to Neza Bloodsnout at Rog'mar." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96108] = { title = "Poison Tips", description = "Arrows are always essential, but sometimes you need something more potent to take down your prey.\n\nThis is where poison coatings come into play. They ruin the meat, but if you need something dead, they do the job.\n\nPoisons can either be brewed or, if you are brave, gathered. You strike me as the latter.\n\nThe vipers by the pools to the south produce a powerful venom. If I have estimated you correctly, I think you could collect some of it.", objectives = "Bring 4 samples of Glade Viper Venom to Neza Bloodsnout at Rog'mar." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96109] = { title = "A Hunter's Quiver", description = "As important as a hunter's weapons is her quiver. A good quiver holds many arrows, while not being so large as to slow the wearer down. It must be durable, and fit snugly onto the body.\n\nAround here, there is no better material for a quiver than the pelts of lions. They are already well-suited for the life of a hunter on the plains.\n\nThe lions gather on a hill to the south. You can see it from here. Please, bring me their pelts.", objectives = "Gather 6 Prized Lion Hides for Neza Bloodsnout at Rog'mar." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96125] = { title = "In Need of Relief", description = "Now that the lion hides have been collected, and the orcish poachers culled, I can finally get a break.\n\nAt least, that's what I would say, if the man who was supposed to relieve me of my watch wasn't missing.\n\nDunston Willis, explorer extraordinaire, went to investigate the ogre settlement to the north a few days ago. He said he'd take over my post upon his return.\n\nFind him. If he's alive, bring him back here. If he's hanging up on meat hooks, bring me proof so Demar can send me someone else.", objectives = "Find Dunston Willis somewhere among the ogres in Bolder'ok." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96126] = { title = "An Ogre's Captive", description = "I'm not sure how you got in here, but please, listen to me.\n\nAs you know, I serve as a watchman for Farholde Keep.\n\nWhile on patrol, I was ambushed by a band of these brutes and taken prisoner. Now, I am forced to fight in the ring for their amusement.\n\nI haven't much strength left. If I'm to escape, it's now or never. \n\nMy captor is an ogre they call \"Gronok the Butcher\". He has the key to my shackles. Will you bring me that key and help me out of here?", objectives = "Find Gronok the Butcher, kill him, and bring Dunston the key to his shackles." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96130] = { title = "Chakuyak", description = "Among the prairie wolves that hunt the hills nearby is one that is especially aggressive. We have taken to calling her Chakuyak. She has become a threat to travelers coming from abroad.\n\nShe stalks the trees west of Stonebull Lake, moving from tree stand to tree stand.\n\nEnd this threat and bring me her pelt, and I will speak your praises to the chief. Beware, for she is dangerous! You might see other hunters seeking her out there, and perhaps you could work as a team.", objectives = "Defeat Chakuyak and bring back her pelt.", progress = "Have you found the big wolf?", completion = "Taking the life of such a beautiful creature is a sad event, but it was necessary for the safety of our people. I will make certain that the pelt does not go to waste. Thank you." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96131] = { title = "An Oldstone But An Old Friend", description = "I'm sure you've met that old stick-in-the-mud, that lives in the cave south of here? \n\nYou must take this staff to him along with my feather. He will know what it means. Or he won't! Either way it will get his attention.\n\nHe may be an oldstone, but he is reliable. He's one of the few mortals I would trust with a matter as grave as this. \n \nQuickly, Dirtwalker! I fear a shadow is falling over Hyjal we cannot see.", objectives = "Take the Faintly Glowing Branch to Ketharas." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96135] = { title = "Heed My Call", description = "Euck, just bein' around these blasted totems is givin' me the willies--but that's good. This much twisted corruption will be exactly what we need tae summon the quilboar's elementals.\n\nGo to the Thousand Needles and find a suitable spot for your defenses. The steam pools should work. They're rich with fire, earth, water, and air alike. Place these totems and be ready for a fight. The Razormane won't take too kindly to yer interference.", objectives = "Use the Twisted Totems to put an end to the quilboar ritual." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96136] = { title = "Call of Air", description = "As you have no doubt experienced yourself, the elements of Azeroth are unique to those in Zephras. It is one thing to channel the forces of nature within the elemental plains, and another thing entirely to do it down here in the muck.\n\nI could grant you your totem of air, but I think it would do you more good to meet with the one who trains the other earth-bound initiates. What say you, {name}?", objectives = "Find Prate Cloudseer in Thousand Needles." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96137] = { title = "Ira's Dagger", description = "A small dagger belonging to the self-appointed ranger, Ira, who kept the forests safe by preventing the beasts within from attacking travelers.\n\nWith Ira's spirit still wandering the woods, perhaps her unfinished business was to clear out the worg that continue to claim victims throughout the forest.", objectives = "Defeat 10 Young Black Ravagers and 7 Black Ravagers then return to Sirra Von'Indi in Darkshire for more information.", progress = "What have you got there?", completion = "Ira? Are you sure? Sounds like the woman was damn near a ghost before she died. I'm surprised you found her.\n\nRest assured I will take great care of this dagger." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96138] = { title = "Merrick's Bow", description = "A bow left by the spirit of Merrick Valor, famed Watcher who prided himself on keeping the roads safe from encroaching enemies.\n\nWith Merrick's spirit still wandering the roads, perhaps his unfinished business was to clear out invaders near his home in Raven Hill. The ogres south of town may be what's troubling his spirit.", objectives = "Defeat 1 Splinter Fist Warriors and 8 Splinter Fist Taskmasters then return to Sirra Von'Indi in Darkshire for more information." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96139] = { title = "The Valor Family", description = "In dark times like these, it's important we remember our heroes as much as our foes. Darkshire would not still be standing if it weren't for the bravery of folk like the good Lady Althea or those who lost their lives at Raven Hill.\n\nHave you read much on Raven Hill? No, of course not. Its history was wiped out along with its people. My library, impressive as it is, has little on the subject.\n\nIf you happen to find anything, I'd appreciate it if you brought it here. Those folk deserve to be remembered.", objectives = "Search Raven Hill for anything of interest and return to Sirra Von'Indi in Darkshire.", progress = "Have you found anything? I'm not holding out much hope.", completion = "This tome appears to be about the Valor family. I believe I've heard of a few of them. Good folk. Not sure they merit an entire book about them.\n\nI'll make you a copy of the tome. If you see anything else related to them on your travels, I'll be happy to take it off your hands." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96145] = { title = "Past Wing and Claw", description = "Traveler, be wary! Though the Shrine of Aviana lies ahead, the area is claimed now by the harpies of the Wormwing tribe.\n\nLike my family, the Highfeathers, I am a follower of Aviana, but the Wormwings are not so loyal. They are a danger to anyone who passes through their territory.\n\nIf you can make your way past them, my cousin Phoebe Highfeather helps to protect the shrine.", objectives = "Seek Phoebe Highfeather at the Shrine of Aviana." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96204] = { title = "The Windshaper's Wrath", description = "Now that I'm free I'm going to make these vile creatures regret ever laying eyes on a Windshaper.\n\nLet's get out of here, {class}.", objectives = "Accompany Lumina Windsinger and help her escape Fenris Keep.", completion = "Thank you again, {name}. I've been aquatinting myself with Trevan here, who I've learned sent you along on my trail.\n\nI've heard... less than charitable things about paladins thus far in my travels. As a sky-touched shen'dorei elf traveling through horde territory, I can certainly understand how easily intolerance and prejudice can take root. \n\nYou and your kind have a friend among the Windshapers." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96209] = { title = "The Ancient, Orokai", description = "The ancient, Orokai, stands vigil just outside of town. Take this to him. The ancients are wondrous and wise. Provided this branch has not been separated from its parent tree for too long, he will be able to \"speak\" with it to learn what tales it has to tell.\n\nYou can find Orokai to the southwest of the town, not too far away.", objectives = "Seek out Orokai in Moonglade." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96222] = { title = "Khan Hratha", description = "While war rages throughout the region, the Maraudine centaur stand unchallenged in the Valley of Spears. I worry that they will grow callous in time and stir further unrest if the other clans continue to turn a blind eye to their presence.\n\nKhan Hratha possesses a Maraudine Key Fragment, and I wish to have it as a negotiation tactic. Find a war horn mouthpiece from the centaur there and use it to challenge him atop the highest peak.\n\nBring the key to me, and I will have a proposition for you.", objectives = "Bring the Maraudine Key Fragment to Umarak in the Desolace." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96241] = { title = "Talkin' bout Toxins, Mon", description = "Something funny be happenin' over there at Gloomrise. Ol' Mazu'kon be hearin all about these nasty new beasties skitterin' all around there.\n\nSome say those creepy crawlies got a venom that have some unique properties and this be gettin' me curious. Take my extractor. Use it on the dead bodies layin' around that place to harvest the venom. Do this and I be in ya debt, mon.", objectives = "Use the Toxin Extractor to gather 5 Gloomrise Toxin Samples from the Gnawed Corpses at Gloomrise.", progress = "Did ya get what I need?", completion = "Heh... when I said unique properties, I wasn't kiddin' mon! You seem no worse for wear, so it be all good.\n\nThank you for your aid, {class}. It be much appreciated." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96243] = { title = "Call of Earth", description = "It's past time ye heeded the earth, brave Shaman. The elements already prickle in yer skin, but once ye speak with the stone, the ground itself'll set firm 'neath yer soles--and in yer soul.\n\nSeek out Teo Hammerstorm, in Coldridge Valley. Ye'll find him within Anvilmar, a holdfast forged by hammer, fire, and will.", objectives = "Find Teo Hammerstorm in Dun Morogh.", completion = "The land itself let me know ye were comin'! Aye, sometimes, the burnin' fire within us is enough to power us through the snow without even touchin' the ground!" }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96246] = { title = "Blackmaw Pouches", description = "", objectives = "" }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96252] = { title = "Tarnished Treasures", description = "{class}, I would ask a favor of you. One that is deeply personal.\n\nWhen they ambushed and killed my sisters, the Wormwings took their jewelry claiming these treasures as trophies of battle. What's worse, they've stashed our treasures in their nests with their unborn young; further proof of their depravity.\n\nPlease collect my fallen sisters' treasures. Avoid harming the unhatched eggs if you can, but I'll lose no sleep over the broken eggs of our enemies.", objectives = "Collect 8 Tarnished Highfeather Bangles from Wormwing Harpy nests." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96255] = { title = "Amalgamated Marrow", description = "<Something wriggles ominously within the bone pile as green ooze seeps out from under the freshly added bones.>", objectives = "Slay the Awakened Fel Ash Slime." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96259] = { title = "Defending the Dead", description = "There is an ancient tauren burial ground at the place called Gloomrise, just northwest of this camp. Of late it has been infested with a particularly vicious brood of spiders. These spiders not only pose a threat to the people of Mulgore, they are also damaging a site that most tauren consider to be sacred.\n\nIt would be of great service if you could travel to Gloomrise and put an end to this infestation. The ancestors will surely smile upon you if you see this done.", objectives = "Kill 10 Gloomrise Hatchlings and 5 Gloomrise Soldiers.", completion = "Thank you for your service to the people of this land. It may take time for us to completely clear out the infestation, but your efforts have created a stable foothold for us to leverage against these vile creatures." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96260] = { title = "Stronger than Steel", description = "Have you heard what befell the burial ground at Gloomrise? Giant spiders--rumored to have a venom so strong that it can wake the dead--have spread like wildfire. Nasty business, if you ask me.\n\nOne of the scouts dispatched to investigate returned half dead and covered in an incredibly resilient, crystalline spider silk. I harvested what I could, but I would highly value more samples of this silk for additional study.\n\nBring me more of this crystalline silk and I will reward you.", objectives = "Gather 3 strands of Crystalline Silk from Gloomrise Spinners.", progress = "This silk's remarkable properties could be used to make lightweight, durable cloth with remarkable defensive properties. I am eager to experiment with more of it.", completion = "These are excellent samples, and more than sufficient for my needs.\n\nHere, take this. I was able to craft a rather unique cloak with a weave I spun from the small sample of silk already in my possession. I am hopeful that you will find it useful in your travels.\n\nEarthmother watch over you, {class}." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96261] = { title = "The Broodmother", description = "As is often the case with infestations such as the one we are facing at Gloomrise, a single powerful matriarch often leads to the rapid spread of a hostile spider population.\n\nIf we wish to drive these beasts off for good, we'll need to seek out the progenitor and end her. When you go to Gloomrise, seek out the broodmother there and destroy her. I'd advise you to bring allies, and be ready for anything. These seem to be no ordinary spiders.", objectives = "Kill Broodmother Valraxx at Gloomrise.", completion = "Reanimated dead? The broodmother possessing a night elven form? These are troubling revelations. One has to wonder what it all means... I fear that must be a concern for a later time.\n\nThank you, {name}. You've done the Earthen Ring and the people of Mulgore a great service." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96262] = { title = "Prickly Pinecones", description = "I've known these hills since I was a hatchling. If there is one thing I know, it's that pinecones can solve a lot of problems.\n\nProbably not what you expected, eh?\n\n<The crow winks at you, conspiratorially.>\n\nGo fetch me some; it's part of a little scheme I'm hatching. I promise you it will be worth the effort.\n\nYou should be able to find them under any healthy or living tree nearby. Stay away from those corrupted ones though, those pinecones aren't any good!", objectives = "Collect 10 Prickly Pinecones under healthy trees." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96264] = { title = "Elemental Aid", description = "So yer a big shot shaman now, eh? Ye've mastered the elements and want tae put 'em to good use? I think I got just the thing.\n\nIf ye want the elements' respect, ye gotta repay yer debts to 'em. They help you, you help them. And right now they need all the help they can get from those who would abuse their power.\n\nEarth's rumblin', {name}. It speaks of the quilboar amassin' for some ritual of terrible power. We need tae go investigate their kraul and see what they're up to. Bring me back whatever ye find.", objectives = "Defeat Charlga Razorflank in Razorfen Kraul and collect information on the quilboar's plans." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96265] = { title = "Secret of the Barrow Deeps", description = "<The corrupted shards combine into a gem seething with tainted power. The Watchers will want to see this.>", objectives = "Take the Corrupted Gemstone to Thera Duskwhisper in Winterspring." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96294] = { title = "A Darker Truth", description = "<The Broodmother you just killed is no spider at all, but rather a night elf druid who assumed a twisted animal form. A variety of questions flood your mind about the nature--and purpose--of the spiders at Gloomrise.\n\nYou notice a note peeking out of the folds of the dead elf's robe. Perhaps this document may answer some of the questions filling your head.>", objectives = "Bring the letter you recovered from Broodmother Valraxx to Muln Earthfury at Skywatcher Plateau.", progress = "What is this?", completion = "This is... most disturbing. Why would a druid be behind a brood of dangerous spiders? Who or what is this \"Wild King\" and \"Pact\" that is referenced in this letter?\n\nI will confer with the druids of the Cenarion Circle on this. Perhaps they will know more.\n\nThank you again for your aid. As disturbing as this information is, we will rest easier knowing that the person controlling these vile creatures has been destroyed." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96296] = { title = "Fetid Corruption", description = "<The second you near the pulsing nodule it falls from the tree, exposing a weeping green sap. It seems the tree has corruption within its bark that has spread deep, but the tree is not yet dead.\n\nLooking around it is clear it has spread to some of the surrounding trees, but not all suffer from the same level of corruption.\n\nPerhaps it is not too late to save the infected trees nearby.\n\nSurely the Highfeathers would be grateful if you remove as many corrupted knots as you can find.>", objectives = "Find and remove 6 Corrupted Knots from the trees nearby." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96301] = { title = "Power Wash", description = "With the venomous, poisonous heart of the chimaera Ghansurok in hand, soak in the ancient waters of the Well of Eternity.\n\nWatch closely how the waters react to the corruption, how nature remembers what systemic corruption has tried to unmake.\n\nBring the organ back to me, and together we will read the signs it bears, and learn whether balance can yet be restored... or if the wound runs too deep.", objectives = "Enter the Well of Eternity and observe its effects on the Venom-dripping Heart." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96302] = { title = "Arch Absolution", description = "I've compacted this potent, pungent resin. Take this prepared incense and stand before the fallen form of The Defiler's remains.\n\nSpeak the incantation as the smoke rises, not to banish what remains, but to steady the spirit. His visage still carries the memory of terror, and even now it stirs fear in those who linger too long.\n\nLet the smoke carry calm and resolve, warding the mind against dread, so that those who walk this place may remember the victory, not the horror.", objectives = "Take Marn's incense and allow the smoke to ward the air around Archimonde's remains." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96303] = { title = "Memory Mist", description = "{name}, the ancestral spirits called to Hyjal during the great battle weren't all lost. Some linger still, drawn to Nordrassil after the great sacrifice. These wisps have stayed within the root canopy that hangs over the well, trapped in a state of purgatory between this world and the next.\n\nUse this enchanted branch to bring peace to these wisps, joining their memories with eternity.\n\nYou need not release them all yourself. Recover the will of five and return the branch to us.", objectives = "Use the Enchanted Branch to release 5 wisps around Nordrassil." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96321] = { title = "The Dying God", description = "I... don't have much time, mortal. You must take this staff, a branch of the world tree... corrupted... wrong. I carried it here...\n\nThe Wild Gods... they must know. Take it to her. The... crow...\n\n<The dying Wild God grows still and his eyes stare blankly ahead. What little is left of his corporeal form seems to break apart and drift away. There is a faintly glowing branch on the ground, with a sickly green crystal affixed to its head.>", objectives = "Find someone on Mount Hyjal who may be interested in the Faintly Glowing Staff." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96322] = { title = "A Revenge Now Bitter", description = "You know, for a mortal I'm impressed with how easily you follow orders.\n\nYou just went in there and killed all of those people without batting an eye!\n\nAhhhh... but now it's time for YOUR end of the deal, 'friend'. I've helped you dismantle the moronic Ashen Reign, take out their leaders and cripple their operations here.\n\nI think I've earned my freedom.\n\n<Felflick's eyes glimmer in anticipation.>", objectives = "Speak to Felflick." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96332] = { title = "A Little Payback", description = "A second wave of Naga was approaching the keep when we were falling back. I suspect that the battle is still raging inside. \n\nWe Kor'kron play blood for blood. If you are going in there anyway, I want you to kill any Naga you see. I saw a sorceress among them as well, and you can bet that was their leader. Bring me her head.\n\nWe lost a lot of good orcs today and I won't rest easy knowing that we didn't give as good as we got.", objectives = "Enter the Alcaz Prison and slay 15 Strashasz Soldiers, 8 Strashaz Enchantresses, and bring the head of Tidemistress Ca'zass to Sergeant Ulka." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96334] = { title = "Blood Red Bandanas", description = "Most of the humans we fought wore blood red bandanas. I seem to recall hearing of a criminal organization operating in the Eastern Kingdoms known as 'The Defias Brotherhood' who are known for their red masks. Why they are active here in Kalimdor I don't know, but kill any that cross your path and bring their masks to Eitrigg in Orgrimmar. \n\nHe'll be able to determine if these are in fact Defias masks.", objectives = "Enter Alcaz Prison and collect 8 Blood Red Bandanas from the human guards there." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96335] = { title = "The Man in the Iron Chains", description = "Wow! That was impressive. The way you took down that dragon was really something!\n\nWhile you are here... do you think you might be able to help me get out of this ball and chain?\n\nIf he hasn't fled or been killed already, the torturer they call 'The Questioner' should have the keys to these shackles. Get the key from that sadist and bring it to me.\n\nI promise that I'll make it well worth your while if you do.", objectives = "Recover the Alcaz Shackle Key from The Questioner in Alcaz Prison." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96337] = { title = "More Valuable Than Gold", description = "I told you that I'd make it worth your while to free me. I don't have any gold for you, but I have something better.\n\nTake this. It will help you find a treasure more valuable than gold. Do what you want with it, but if anyone asks you where you got it, tell them that the person who gave it to you died. \n\nTell them he was vaporized by dragonfire... blown out to sea.", objectives = "Use the note provided by Mason Connery to find his hidden treasure." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96339] = { title = "Legacy Reward: Replica Ironforge Air Rifle", description = "", objectives = "", completion = "Wait, wait, you said your name was {name}?\n\n{name}! I am so glad to finally meet you. Someone delivered a package here addressed to you and assured me that you would eventually come to pick it up. I tried to tell them that we don't do that around here, but before I could get a word in, they were already gone!\n\nYour timing is great, too. It was gonna be lumped up with all the other garbage that I toss into the sea nightly.\n\nWhat? We all do it. Ugh, just take your package and go!" }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96369] = { title = "Bad News for Folkar", description = "<The King is dead--killed in an escape attempt just before the Naga attacked. Many Kor'kron died to learn this news, but this knowledge could shake the Alliance to its core. You need to return to Commander Folkar and tell him what you've learned as quickly as possible.>", objectives = "Report back to Commander Folkar." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96376] = { title = "State Secrets", description = "", objectives = "" }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96377] = { title = "State Secrets", description = "", objectives = "" }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96379] = { title = "State Secrets", description = "", objectives = "" }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96381] = { title = "A Bit of Wet Work", description = "Was spyin' on the shore of Alcaz with my trusty lookin' glass whilst you were off eavesdroppin' on Lady Proudmoore. I think the island may be under attack. I saw naga--lots of them, chargin' onto shore. \n\nThe enemy of my enemy is certainly not my friend when it comes to naga, so let's do the world a favor and take some of them out. I also spied what looks to be the leader--a spellcaster type barkin' orders. Take her out as well, if you can.", objectives = "Enter the Alcaz Prison and slay 15  Strashasz Soldiers, 8 Strashaz Enchantresses, and bring the head of Tidemistress Ca'zass to Sully McCleary." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96383] = { title = "Legacy Reward: Spectral Bear Cub", description = "", objectives = "" }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96390] = { title = "Nip 'Em in the Bud", description = "Dark Iron spies have infiltrated Dun Morogh. To what end I canna' be sure, but this is a problem we need to nip in the bud before it is allowed to grow.\n\nHead eastward to Ironband's Compound and kill the Dark Iron spies that you find there.", objectives = "Slay 10 Dark Iron Spies in Dun Morogh.", completion = "These Dark Irons may be our cousins but they ain't family, that's for sure. I shed no tears for any misfortune that befalls them that stray too far from that accursed mountain o' theirs.\n\nHopefully this is enough to put 'em off of further incursions into these lands." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96391] = { title = "Underground Map", description = "The map you are holding seems to show a complex series of underground tunnels and highways that all seem to converge on a point underneath Ironforge itself.\n\nYou can't be sure what the runes say as they are written in the ugly jagged rune language of the Dark Iron dwarves, but you can guess at the purpose of these tunnels. As you are reading the map, a gust of wind washes over you and you can faintly hear a dwarven voice carried on it. Earthseer Farsen needs to see this.", objectives = "Deliver the Dark Iron Map to Earthseer Farsen in Dun Morogh.", progress = "Oh what's this, then?", completion = "Judging by this map, it certainly looks like these Dark Irons are planning some sort of incursion into the vaults beneath Ironforge. The band ye busted up to the east must be a scouting force.\n\nThank ye for bringing me this. If we hurry, we might be able to beat them to whatever their goal is down there." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96392] = { title = "Farsen's Watch", description = "Greetings to ye, friend. My name is Earthseer Farsen and I'm visiting Dun Morogh from Aerie Peak. As I was travelin', I couldn't help but notice that we have, well... a bit o' a Dark Iron Dwarf problem.\n\nIf ye have a moment, I can show ye what I mean. I've got a bit o' magic that should do the trick.", objectives = "Speak with Earthseer Farsen and ask him to lend you his far sight to observe the Dark Iron threat.", progress = "Farsight can show ye a great many things, even things ye'd rather not see.", completion = "So ye see now, {class}? Thick as cockroaches they are, and that's just the ones we can see from the sky.\n\nYe look like a sturdy enough sort. Hows about a bit o' violence?" }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96393] = { title = "Old Ironforge Incursion", description = "Gather some allies and head down into the caverns beneath Old Ironforge. Enter the Hall of Thanes there and push to the lower vaults. \n\nMy Dark Iron is a bit rusty, but I can make out a name--one Durgen Dirgehammer. It's likely that he's the commander. Take his head and deliver it to King Magni Bronzebeard. \n\nOh, and when you do, tell him his old friend Farsen sends his regards!", objectives = "Enter the Hall of Thanes beneath Old Ironforge and claim the Head of Durgen Dirgehammer.", progress = "What do ye need, citizen?", completion = "A Dark Iron incursion--right beneath our feet? Well, I'm relieved to hear that the Dark Iron commander has been dispatched.\n\nThe guards will head in and clean up the rest of the rabble. We'll see to it that the breaches are sealed and the lower levels reinforced to ensure that no further incursions are possible.\n\nThank ye for yer service to Ironforge, {class}. Take this as a small token of my gratitude. Oh, and if ye see that old Wildhammer rockhugger Farsen again, tell 'em to pay me a proper visit." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96394] = { title = "The Restless Dead", description = "Something has disturbed the tombs down in the Hall of Thanes, and strange noises have been heard coming from deep within the vaults. The spirits of the dead are light sleepers, and whatever is going on down there seems to have startled them.\n\nHead down there and see what you can do about that for us. If any of the dead are awake--well, put them back down!", objectives = "Kill 15 Enraged Apparitions, 10 Tormented Souls and put the spirit of Anvilmar to rest.", progress = "I don't have time for ghouls and ghosts. I have a job to do down here.", completion = "Ah good, it's done then. I can't have the other keepers refusing to enter the hall to do their duties on account of \"ghosts\" and \"angry dead\", can I?" }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96395] = { title = "An Ancient Grudge", description = "The... Thane... my mighty... Thane... he... needs to... rest.\n\nPlease... help him... help him... rest...\n\nConsumed... by... ancient... grudge... No... rest...", objectives = "Put the spirit of Faldrim Anvilmar to rest and then return to the Ghostly Attendant in the Hall of Thanes.", completion = "My... Thane... he... rests... yes... rest.\n\nThank... you...\n\nI... rest..." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96403] = { title = "Important Heirlooms", description = "You there, adventurer... I could really use your aid.\n\nI was sneaking--uh... 'patrolling' in the vaults when a force of Dark Iron dwarves emerged from the depths in mole machines! I don't know what they are here for, but there is priceless loot--uh or, rather... I mean, 'important cultural heirlooms' down there! Please, recover any such relics you see and return them here.\n\nI assure you that anything you recover will be catalogued and returned to its proper place of honor.", objectives = "Collect 8 Dwarven Heirlooms from the Hall of Thanes.", progress = "<Thom appears to absentmindedly rub his hands together as he looks at you.>", completion = "Look at you, as brave as you are enterprising! I'm a gnome of my word, and your reward is well earned! \n\nNow, let me take a look at the haul--uh, I mean... the recovered heirlooms. I need to get started appraising--excuse me, 'cataloging' them so that they can be put back in their proper places as quickly as possible." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96408] = { title = "A Visitor to Dun Morogh", description = "Last night one of our mountaineers spotted a campfire on a hillside to the east. It looks to be pretty high up, overlooking the Gol'Bolar Quarry.\n\nIt's probably nothing, but I'd like you to go check on that camp. If they are friendly, no harm done. If they aren't friendly... well, you know what to do.", objectives = "Investigate the campsite overlooking the Gol'Bolar Quarry.", completion = "Greetings, friend. How are ya?" }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96435] = { title = "A Fitting End", description = "<Felflick cackles gleefully as he regards the bloody bones of the Ashen Reign leaders.>\n\nOh this is just perfect!\n\n<Felflick hops back and forth in his cage, snickering all the while.>\n\nNow it is time to give those warlocks the fate they deserve. There is a massive bone pile to the west of here if you follow the road. Trust me, it's impossible to miss. That's where all their 'failed' experiments go.\n\nThat is where I wish to dump these fools' remains. Let the whole world know what failures they are!", objectives = "Throw the warlock bones onto the bone pile near the slime pools." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96438] = { title = "Battle at the Mannoroc Coven", description = "{name}, I need your aid. One of our brothers passing through Nigel's Point in Desolace overheard details of a battle that took place at the Mannoroc Coven. It was reported that one side brought powerful holy magic to bear in the battle against the warlocks there. Wielders of the light were certainly involved.\n\nI'd like to learn more of who was involved in this skirmish. If one of our people was involved--or fell there... I want to know about it.", objectives = "Investigate the battle at the Mannoroc Coven in Desolace." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96449] = { title = "Aeonas's Secret Refuge", description = "Come to think on it, I do know of a secluded spot far to the south of here. Someone once told me it was called Newman's Landing, though don't ask me who this \"Newman\" is. You should start looking for Ol' Aeonas there.\n\nYou are welcome to make use of my old dingy moored just over yonder just past the northernmost dock. She isn't much, but she'll get you there faster than swimming.\n\nI do hope nothin' happened to him. I'd rest easier if you went and checked on our friend.", objectives = "Use the Old Dingy at Menethil Harbor to search for Aeonas." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96476] = { title = "In Search of Aeonas", description = "Aeonas mentioned something about Felwood, so it's possible that's where he is. There's a small settlement in the southern portion of the woods there known as the Emerald Sanctuary. I'd suggest asking around there to see if anyone has seen him.", objectives = "Search for signs of Aeonas the Vindicated at the Emerald Sanctuary in Felwood." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96494] = { title = "Gathering Storm", description = "With the perimeter scouted, you've proven useful and trustworthy enough to bring into the fold.\n\nI'm here representing SI:7's efforts to gain crucial information important to the Alliance. Not just anyone is privy to this knowledge. Mind your discretion.\n\nA druidic cult known as the Blackthorne Pact has taken root nearby, operating in service to something they call the Wild King.\n\nFind the domain of this \"Wild King\" and mark it. Then we can report back to Stormwind with certainty.", objectives = "Find the Blackthorne reinforcement point at the entrance to Hyjal Summit." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96529] = { title = "A Shaw Deal", description = "Your help has been key to our scouting efforts. Take this information to Master Mathias Shaw in Stormwind.\n\nRemember, you're not to speak of our activities here, my presence, or SI:7 involvement to anyone else. I have a lot to continue setting up here, and plans to keep on track. \n\nWe'll be in touch.", objectives = "Bring the Blackthorne Information to Master Mathias Shaw in Stormwind." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96550] = { title = "Battle Recall", description = "The aged scabbard is embellished with carved designs and markings. This matches the description spoken by the war veteran. A dramatic view of the land below is a breathtaking sight.\n\nPerhaps simply holding the scabbard in your hand while remembering the veteran's words will beckon the spirit to this memory.", objectives = "Use the Embroidered Scabbard to speak with the war veteran and hear his story at the overlook in Elderwild." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96558] = { title = "Soldier's Solace", description = "Beneath the shattered stones of that watchtower lies a cache we buried in haste, when the world was starting to burn. What little we carried from Hyjal rests there still. Take it--you have earned that much.\n\nThe pull is increasing... the mountain no longer holds me as it once did. I am unsure if we will ever speak again.\n\nBecause of you, I remember who I was, and who we were. Go with my thanks, and let this spirit finally be at peace.", objectives = "Recover the Battle Cache buried on Mount Hyjal." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96559] = { title = "Supply Drop", description = "Every Gnomish test pilot knows that one must be prepared for the worst-case scenario when taking to our great skies!\n\nThat's why we never leave the hangar without our pilot survival kits. They have a self-activating beacon attached that will radio our position home as soon as you open it. Not to mention being stuffed full of other useful supplies.\n\nIf you can find that pack wherever it fell, by all means open it immediately and help yourself to the contents. You'll still be doing me a favor!", objectives = "Locate Fenwick Togglespring's Pilot Survival Kit." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96561] = { title = "Last Wishes", description = "<You unfold the simple parchment.>\n\nTo my Rowdy Redridge Rebels,\n\nThe lumberjacks here say the gulpers in that pond are biting like they're racing each other to the bait. Good fish, better eating. After this war is over, we're due an angling competition between friends.\n\nThe setting is simple: we stand on the center island and fish till the sun slips behind Hyjal's highest peak.\n\nWhoever catches the most, doesn't have to gut 'em for our dinner!\n\n-- Tobin --", objectives = "Find the fishing pond near the destroyed Alliance lumbermill in the Cradle of Tranquility." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96603] = { title = "Unstable Magic", description = "Archmage Rhonin is presently abroad investigating a disturbance in the flow of magic across Azeroth. The Archmage has charged me with soliciting the aid of strong adventurers like yourself in gathering important field data to aid him.\n\nTake this Arcane Censer. While afflicted by its magic, you will be able to extract motes of unstable magic from the most skilled spell casters and other singularly powerful entities you may encounter. Bring me said motes and the Kirin Tor will be in your debt.", objectives = "Bring 10 Motes of Unstable Magic to Archmage Celindra in Dalaran." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96604] = { title = "The Great Outdoors", description = "Lok-tar, {class}. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. This is good. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.\n\nYou'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful in this line of work. Not sure how your outdoor skills are but I can probably teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.\n\nHave a seat near the fire and get comfortable. I'll walk you through it.", objectives = "Sit near Brakk's Basic Campfire and wait until you receive the Boosted Rest buff.", progress = "Having the skills needed to survive the outdoors are critical. A well-rested and well-prepared adventurer has a much higher chance of surviving this lifestyle.", completion = "So now that we've learned the basics, go learn a tradeskill from the trainers in the village nearby. They will also teach you how to create a camp fixture suitable to your new profession." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[96605] = { title = "The Great Outdoors", description = "Greetings, {class}. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. This is good. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.\n\nYou'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful in this line of work. Not sure how your outdoor skills are but I can probably teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.\n\nHave a seat near the fire and get comfortable. I'll walk you through it.", objectives = "Sit near Kaga's Basic Campfire and wait until you receive the Boosted Rest buff.", progress = "Having the skills needed to survive the outdoors are critical. A well-rested and well-prepared adventurer has a much higher chance of surviving this lifestyle.", completion = "So now that we've learned the basics, why don't you go and learn a tradeskill from the trainers in the village nearby. They will also teach you how to create a camp fixture suitable to your new profession." }
