WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[97952] = { title = "Camping 101: Blacksmithing", description = "So, you've become a Blacksmith. That's a great choice if you want to make sure your blades never dull.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can help with that by teaching you how to craft a Sharpening Wheel. Bring one of these out at your camp and all the warriors and rogues in the area will be lining up to hone their weapons.", objectives = "Speak with Basil Frye in Undercity to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.", progress = "Yes, I can teach you.", completion = "There you have it, you can now craft your very own Sharpening Wheel. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\n\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[97953] = { title = "Camping 101: Enchanting", description = "Enchanters make everything better and are always welcome at any camp out in the wilds.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Enchanted Lute for your camp. It's so important to find entertainment during your downtime, and this bit of magic can help ensure you are ready to weather all sorts of challenges when you hit the old dusty trail once again.", objectives = "Speak with Vance Undergloom in Brill to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.", completion = "There you have it, you can now craft your very own Enchanted Lute. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\n\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[97954] = { title = "Camping 101: Engineering", description = "Engineers like yourself can cook up all sorts of bits, bots, and bombs for fun and profit.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Reagent Bot for your camp. This helpful automaton can help keep you well-supplied so that you and your allies never run out of the materials needed to fuel your spells.", objectives = "Speak with Graham Van Talen in Undercity to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.", completion = "There you have it, you can now craft your very own Reagent Bot. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\n\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[97955] = { title = "Camping 101: First Aid", description = "So you've taken up First Aid? That's an honorable... and pragmatic pursuit as a {class}.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a First Aid Kit for your camp. Injuries are a reality in the world of adventuring and offering some much-needed healing at your camp could even save lives.", objectives = "Speak with Nurse Neela in Brill to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.", progress = "I can teach you once you've gained some skill with your profession.", completion = "There you have it, you can now craft your very own First Aid Kit. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\n\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[97956] = { title = "Camping 101: Fishing", description = "You might not think so, but your skill as a fisherman can actually come in handy at camp.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Fish Bowl for your camp. You can use this fixture to help provide a bit of joy to yourself and your fellow adventurers. A happy adventurer is a strong adventurer and I'm sure your combat capabilities will reflect that.", objectives = "Speak with Clyde Kellen in Brill to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.", progress = "I can teach you once you've gained some skill as a fisherman.", completion = "There you have it, you can now craft your very own Fish Bowl. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\n\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[97957] = { title = "Camping 101: Herbalism", description = "Looks to me like you've gained some skill in herbalism. Picking flowers isn't just for dilly-dallying, you know. It can be useful... and profitable.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Incense Candle for your camp. High spirits are a key component to keeping healers and spellcasters in the fight, and an Incense Candle can provide a boost that magic users will surely appreciate.", objectives = "Speak with Faruza in Brill to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.", completion = "There you have it, you can now craft your very own Incense Candle. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\n\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[97958] = { title = "Camping 101: Leatherworking", description = "You've become a leatherworker. Good for you, {class}. I reckon I know someone that can teach you how to make yourself a tent that will keep you cool on hot days, and dry on rainy days.\n\nWith a good tent over your head, you'll ensure that you get all the rest you need to stay sharp on your travels.", objectives = "Speak with Shelene Rhobart on the road to Undercity from Brill to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.", completion = "There you have it, your very own camp tent. Most folk don't care much for tents being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\n\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[97959] = { title = "Camping 101: Mining", description = "Mining isn't the most glamorous, but it's good honest work and a fine profession for you to explore.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Lodestone for your camp. Build one of these and everyone who wants to swing a sword will be eager to gather round your fire and soak up the extra \"oomph\" it can provide to increase their combat prowess.", objectives = "Speak with Brom Killian in Undercity to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.", progress = "You've come to learn, then?", completion = "There you have it, you can now craft your very own Lodestone. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\n\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[97960] = { title = "Camping 101: Skinning", description = "Being able to skillfully harvest the skins and hides of fallen beasts is one of the more valuable skills an adventurer can possess.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Camp Chair for your camp. Sometimes it's important to just take a load off, and you can use some of those hides you've gathered to make a comfy chair to sit in. A bit of relaxation can help ensure that you are at your peak condition and can strike where it counts the next time you find yourself in a dust-up.", objectives = "Speak with Rand Rhobart on the road to Undercity from Brill to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.", completion = "There you have it, you can now craft your very own Camp Chair. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\n\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[97961] = { title = "Camping 101: Tailoring", description = "Tailoring is a surprisingly potent tradeskill to invest in, and I'm sure it'll serve you well.\n\nI know someone that can teach you how to craft a Faction Banner for your camp, provided you have the skill for it. Inspiration and morale are a key part of success on any battlefield, and an inspirational banner can go a long way to keeping you energized.", objectives = "Speak with Bowen Brisboise on the road to Brill from Deathknell to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.", completion = "There you have it, you can now craft your very own Rallying Banner. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\n\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics." }
WordHunterWoW_QuestEN[97963] = { title = "Camping 101: Alchemy", description = "So, you chose to cook up brews and potions as an Alchemist. I'm sure that'll come in handy in your travels.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Mana Well for your camp. Build one of these and all of the healers and spellcaster types will come running to get a refreshing taste.", objectives = "Speak with Nyassa Swiftdraught in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.", progress = "Yes, I can teach you.", completion = "There you have it, you can now craft your very own Mana Well. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\n\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics." }
